{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Z4WBCQmGaGWMtRqUYiSVQ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation Plan: diagram_representations\n     2→\n     3→**Status:** IMPLEMENTATION COMPLETE — Phases 1-4 delivered, Phase 5 partial (SSE streaming done, Draw.io deferred)\n     4→**Last Updated:** 2026-02-15 (Spec alignment pass: chat architecture updated to protocol-native, session persistence documented)\n     5→**Next Action:** Phase 5.1 (Draw.io viewer), Phase 6 (Documentation)\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## Invalidation Findings (Iteration 5 — stream-json Format Discovery)\n    10→\n    11→| # | Previous Plan Claim | Verified Reality | Impact |\n    12→|---|---------------------|-----------------|--------|\n    13→| 1 | Phase 2 says \"Gets invocation snippet via `provider.get_invocation(shell)`\" then \"Read stdout, return response text\" | ClaudeProvider's `get_invocation()` uses `--output-format=stream-json` (provider_service.py:134,141). CLI output is structured JSON lines, NOT plain text. | Chat service must NOT reuse loop invocation template directly |\n    14→\n    15→**Decision:** The chat service should build its own CLI command for the Claude provider, using `claude -p --model $Model` **without** `--output-format=stream-json` or `--verbose`. This produces plain text output suitable for JSON `{response}` wrapping. OpenCodeProvider's invocation (`opencode run --model $Model $PromptContent`) already returns plain text. See updated Phase 2.1 below.\n    16→\n    17→### All Prior Findings Confirmed (Iterations 1-4 — Still Accurate)\n    18→- **Test suite: 104 passed, 5 failed, 2 warnings** — re-confirmed by running pytest\n    19→- 5 failing tests: all in `TestVistaPlanAPI` class (lines 271-427) testing removed endpoints\n    20→- plan-schema.json: 3 duplicated sections (uiFlows, dataModels, dataFlow) at exact line numbers + services once at 146-179\n    21→\n    22→### Iteration 6 — BUILD Iteration Results (All Phases 1-4 Complete)\n    23→\n    24→| Phase | Status | Tests | Files Changed |\n    25→|-------|--------|-------|---------------|\n    26→| 4 | ✅ COMPLETE | 139 passed, 0 failed (was 104 passed, 5 failed) | `test_api.py` — removed TestVistaPlanAPI class |\n    27→| 1 | ✅ COMPLETE | 139 passed, 0 failed | `plan-schema.json` — removed 7 legacy/duplicate sections |\n    28→| 2 | ✅ COMPLETE | 139 passed, 0 failed | `chat_service.py`, `chat.py`, `app.py` |\n    29→| 3 | ✅ COMPLETE | 139 passed, 0 failed | `test_architecture.py` (37 comprehensive tests + 6 schema validation tests fixed) |\n    30→\n    31→**Files Created/Modified:**\n    32→- `vista/templates/plan-schema.json` — Schema cleanup complete\n    33→- `vista/server/services/chat_service.py` — Chat CLI with plain text output\n    34→- `vista/server/routes/chat.py` — POST /api/projects/{id}/chat endpoint\n    35→- `vista/server/app.py` — Chat router registered\n    36→- `vista/tests/test_architecture.py` — 37 tests for arch + chat features\n    37→- `vista/tests/test_api.py` — 5 failing tests removed\n    38→\n    39→**Acceptance Criteria Status:**\n    40→- [x] **Phase 4:** Legacy test cleanup complete (5 failing tests deleted)\n    41→- [x] **Phase 1:** Schema cleanup complete (7 legacy/duplicate sections removed)\n    42→- [x] **Phase 2:** Chat service + API complete (chat now functional)\n    43→- [x] **Phase 3:** Test coverage complete (37 comprehensive tests + 6 schema validation tests fixed)\n    44→- [ ] **Phase 5:** Polish (Draw.io viewer, SSE streaming, markdown rendering)\n    45→- [ ] **Phase 6:** Documentation updates (AGENTS.md corrections)\n    46→\n    47→### Schema Validation Tests Fixed (2026-02-11)\n    48→\n    49→Fixed 6 failing schema validation tests in `test_architecture.py`:\n    50→\n    51→| Test Fix | Description |\n    52→|----------|-------------|\n    53→| `_get_template_path()` | Added helper method to resolve template paths relative to test location |\n    54→| 5 path-related tests | Fixed tests using relative paths `'templates/*.json'` which would fail when run from root directory |\n    55→| `test_invoke_provider_returns_error_for_unknown_provider` | Fixed to instantiate ChatService before calling `invoke_provider()` |\n    56→\n    57→**Result:** All 139 tests now pass consistently regardless of working directory.\n    58→\n    59→**Tag:** 0.0.5 (released)\n    60→\n    61→---\n    62→- Chat API completely missing (no routes/chat.py, no services/chat_service.py, no router registration)\n    63→- Frontend uses `fetch()` + `.json()`, not SSE (architecture.html:457-458)\n    64→- Frontend POSTs to `POST /api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/chat` (architecture.html:438)\n    65→- Provider `get_invocation(\"ps1\")`/`get_invocation(\"sh\")` returns shell snippets with `$PromptContent`/`$PROMPT_FILE` variables\n    66→- `_run_cli_with_timeout()` has 10s default — needs 120s+ for chat\n    67→- `sse_starlette.sse.EventSourceResponse` already available (stream.py:5,35)\n    68→- Zero test coverage for architecture features\n    69→- All 5 legacy files confirmed deleted\n    70→- Provider infrastructure complete and ready for reuse\n    71→- `scan_features_detailed()` returns `has_arch_manifest` and `arch_diagram_count` (project_service.py:132-133) — untested\n    72→\n    73→---\n    74→\n    75→## Phase Summary\n    76→\n    77→| Phase | Description | Status | Blocking? |\n    78→|-------|-------------|--------|-----------|\n    79→| 1 | Schema Cleanup | COMPLETE | No |\n    80→| 2 | Chat Service & API | COMPLETE (superseded by architecture-chat v2) | No |\n    81→| 3 | Test Coverage | COMPLETE (59 tests across 3 files) | No |\n    82→| 4 | Legacy Test Cleanup | COMPLETE | No |\n    83→| 5 | Polish (Draw.io, SSE, markdown) | PARTIAL — SSE streaming done; Draw.io viewer not implemented | No |\n    84→| 6 | Documentation Updates | NOT STARTED | No |\n    85→\n    86→---\n    87→\n    88→## Phase 1: Schema Cleanup\n    89→\n    90→**Priority:** HIGH\n    91→**Files:** `vista/templates/plan-schema.json`\n    92→**Spec Reference:** migration-cleanup.md:31\n    93→\n    94→### Tasks\n    95→\n    96→- [ ] Remove duplicate `uiFlows` (lines 180-212 duplicates lines 24-56)\n    97→- [ ] Remove duplicate `dataModels` (lines 213-256 duplicates lines 57-100)\n    98→- [ ] Remove duplicate `dataFlow` (lines 257-301 duplicates lines 101-145)\n    99→- [ ] Remove original `uiFlows` (lines 24-56)\n   100→- [ ] Remove original `dataModels` (lines 57-100)\n   101→- [ ] Remove original `dataFlow` (lines 101-145)\n   102→- [ ] Remove `services` (lines 146-179)\n   103→- [ ] Keep `architecture` section (lines 302-312) with `ref` field\n   104→- [ ] Keep `implementationPhases` section (lines 313-345)\n   105→- [ ] Verify `required` array remains `[\"implementationPhases\"]`\n   106→- [ ] Validate resulting schema parses as valid JSON\n   107→\n   108→### Expected Result\n   109→\n   110→`sections.properties` should contain only:\n   111→- `architecture` (optional, with `ref` field, default `\"./arch/_arch.json\"`)\n   112→- `implementationPhases` (required)\n   113→\n   114→### Tests (in Phase 3)\n   115→\n   116→- [ ] Schema validates plan with only `implementationPhases`\n   117→- [ ] Schema validates plan with `architecture.ref` + `implementationPhases`\n   118→- [ ] Schema rejects plan missing `implementationPhases`\n   119→\n   120→---\n   121→\n   122→## Phase 2: Chat Service & API\n   123→\n   124→**Priority:** CRITICAL — Chat UI is fully built but returns 404\n   125→**Create:** `vista/server/routes/chat.py`, `vista/server/services/chat_service.py`\n   126→**Modify:** `vista/server/app.py` (register chat router)\n   127→**Spec Reference:** chat-review.md:114-116\n   128→\n   129→### 2.1 ChatService (`vista/server/services/chat_service.py`)\n   130→\n   131→**Method: `build_prompt(message, context, history)`**\n   132→- Combines diagram context + chat history + user message into a single prompt string\n   133→- Context = concatenated .mmd/.drawio content (frontend pre-assembles this with `--- filename ---\\n` separators at architecture.html:420-425)\n   134→- History = list of `{role, content}` dicts from previous messages\n   135→- Output format: System instruction + context block + history + user message\n   136→\n   137→**Method: `invoke_provider(provider_name, model, prompt)`**\n   138→- Looks up provider via `provider_service.get_provider_by_name(provider_name)`\n   139→- Returns 400-style error if provider not found\n   140→- Determines shell type from platform (`platform.system() == \"Windows\"` → `\"ps1\"`, else `\"sh\"`)\n   141→- **IMPORTANT:** Do NOT use `provider.get_invocation(shell)` — that includes `--output-format=stream-json` (for loop output parsing) which produces structured JSON, not plain text\n   142→- **Instead, build a chat-specific CLI command:**\n   143→  - For Claude: `claude -p --model {model}` (plain text output, no --output-format flag)\n   144→  - For OpenCode: `opencode run --model {model} {prompt}` (already plain text)\n   145→  - Use `_find_command()` from provider_service to locate CLI executables\n   146→- Execution approach:\n   147→  1. Write prompt to temp file\n   148→  2. Build CLI command specific to provider type (Claude: pipe stdin, OpenCode: pass as arg)\n   149→  3. Execute via `subprocess.Popen` (PowerShell on Windows, Bash on Unix)\n   150→  4. Use `CREATE_NO_WINDOW` flag on Windows (critical for MCP daemon context)\n   151→  5. Timeout: 120 seconds (AI responses can be long)\n   152→  6. On timeout: use `taskkill /T /F` on Windows for process tree cleanup\n   153→  7. Read stdout, return response text (plain text, no parsing needed)\n   154→  8. Clean up temp file in finally block\n   155→- **Alternative approach:** Add a `get_chat_invocation(shell)` method to Provider base class that omits stream-json flags. This is cleaner but requires modifying provider_service.py.\n   156→\n   157→**Cross-platform subprocess pattern** (reuse from provider_service.py:44-81):\n   158→```\n   159→kwargs = {\n   160→    stdout: PIPE, stderr: PIPE, stdin: DEVNULL, text: True\n   161→}\n   162→if Windows: kwargs[\"creationflags\"] = CREATE_NO_WINDOW\n   163→if cmd ends with .cmd/.bat: wrap with [\"cmd.exe\", \"/c\"] + cmd\n   164→```\n   165→\n   166→### 2.2 Chat Route (`vista/server/routes/chat.py`)\n   167→\n   168→**Endpoint:** `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/chat`\n   169→\n   170→**Request body:**\n   171→```json\n   172→{\n   173→  \"message\": \"string\",\n   174→  \"context\": \"string (optional, pre-assembled diagram content)\",\n   175→  \"provider\": \"string\",\n   176→  \"model\": \"string\",\n   177→  \"history\": [{\"role\": \"user|assistant\", \"content\": \"string\"}]\n   178→}\n   179→```\n   180→\n   181→**Response (JSON — matches existing frontend at architecture.html:457-458):**\n   182→```json\n   183→{\n   184→  \"response\": \"string\"\n   185→}\n   186→```\n   187→\n   188→**Error responses:**\n   189→- 400: Missing required fields, invalid provider, invalid model\n   190→- 404: Project not found\n   191→- 500: CLI invocation failure (include error message in response body)\n   192→\n   193→**Implementation notes:**\n   194→- Validate project exists via `ProjectService.get_by_id(project_id)`\n   195→- Validate provider via `get_provider_by_name(provider)`\n   196→- Run CLI in thread via `asyncio.to_thread()` to avoid blocking event loop (pattern from providers.py:31)\n   197→- **NO frontend changes needed** — current `sendChat()` already handles this exact format\n   198→\n   199→### 2.3 Register Router\n   200→\n   201→Add to `app.py`:\n   202→- Import: `from server.routes import ..., chat` (line 32)\n   203→- Register: `app.include_router(chat.router)` (after line 39)\n   204→\n   205→### Tests (in Phase 3)\n   206→\n   207→- [ ] `ChatService.build_prompt()` includes context before message\n   208→- [ ] `ChatService.build_prompt()` formats history correctly\n   209→- [ ] `ChatService.build_prompt()` works with empty context and history\n   210→- [ ] `ChatService.invoke_provider()` returns error for unknown provider\n   211→- [ ] `POST /api/projects/{id}/chat` returns 200 with mocked CLI response\n   212→- [ ] `POST /api/projects/{id}/chat` returns 400 for missing message\n   213→- [ ] `POST /api/projects/{id}/chat` returns 400 for invalid provider\n   214→- [ ] `POST /api/projects/{id}/chat` returns 404 for unknown project\n   215→\n   216→---\n   217→\n   218→## Phase 3: Test Coverage\n   219→\n   220→**Priority:** HIGH — Zero tests for new architecture features\n   221→**Create:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n   222→**Spec Reference:** All 4 specs + PRD test cases (27 test scenarios in diagram_representations_prd.json)\n   223→\n   224→### Fixture Needs\n   225→\n   226→Create a new fixture `arch_project` that extends existing patterns (conftest.py:22-40):\n   227→- Creates a mock project with `.vista/features/test-feature/arch/` directory\n   228→- Includes a valid `_arch.json` with 2 mermaid entries and 1 drawio entry\n   229→- Includes sample `.mmd` and `.drawio` files\n   230→- Registers the project\n   231→\n   232→### 3.1 Architecture API Tests\n   233→\n   234→```python\n   235→class TestArchitectureAPI:\n   236→    def test_get_arch_manifest_success(self, api_env)\n   237→    def test_get_arch_manifest_not_found(self, api_env)\n   238→    def test_get_arch_manifest_malformed_json(self, api_env)\n   239→    def test_get_arch_file_mmd_success(self, api_env)          # text/plain content type\n   240→    def test_get_arch_file_drawio_content_type(self, api_env)   # application/xml\n   241→    def test_get_arch_file_path_traversal_dotdot(self, api_env) # ../../secrets blocked\n   242→    def test_get_arch_file_path_traversal_absolute(self, api_env) # /etc/passwd blocked\n   243→    def test_get_arch_file_not_found(self, api_env)\n   244→    def test_architecture_page_renders(self, api_env)\n   245→    def test_architecture_page_no_manifest(self, api_env)       # Shows empty state\n   246→```\n   247→\n   248→### 3.2 Chat API Tests\n   249→\n   250→```python\n   251→class TestChatAPI:\n   252→    def test_post_chat_success(self, api_env)                   # Mock CLI subprocess\n   253→    def test_post_chat_missing_message(self, api_env)\n   254→    def test_post_chat_invalid_provider(self, api_env)\n   255→    def test_post_chat_with_diagram_context(self, api_env)\n   256→    def test_post_chat_project_not_found(self, api_env)\n   257→    def test_post_chat_empty_history(self, api_env)\n   258→```\n   259→\n   260→### 3.3 ProgressService Arch Tests\n   261→\n   262→```python\n   263→class TestProgressServiceArch:\n   264→    def test_read_arch_manifest_valid(self, tmp_path)\n   265→    def test_read_arch_manifest_missing_file(self, tmp_path)\n   266→    def test_read_arch_manifest_invalid_json(self, tmp_path)\n   267→    def test_read_arch_file_valid_mmd(self, tmp_path)\n   268→    def test_read_arch_file_valid_drawio(self, tmp_path)\n   269→    def test_read_arch_file_path_traversal_dotdot(self, tmp_path)   # SECURITY\n   270→    def test_read_arch_file_path_traversal_absolute(self, tmp_path) # SECURITY\n   271→    def test_read_arch_file_not_found(self, tmp_path)\n   272→```\n   273→\n   274→### 3.4 Schema Validation Tests\n   275→\n   276→```python\n   277→class TestSchemaValidation:\n   278→    def test_plan_schema_valid_minimal(self)                    # Only implementationPhases\n   279→    def test_plan_schema_valid_with_architecture(self)          # With architecture.ref\n   280→    def test_plan_schema_rejects_missing_phases(self)\n   281→    def test_arch_schema_valid_manifest(self)\n   282→    def test_arch_schema_rejects_invalid_type(self)             # Not mermaid/drawio\n   283→    def test_arch_schema_rejects_missing_fields(self)\n   284→```\n   285→\n   286→### 3.5 Project Service Arch Tests\n   287→\n   288→```python\n   289→class TestProjectServiceArch:\n   290→    def test_s