{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QwSY848t9uTZrx7g7GQncK","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→/**\n     2→ * Notion-style Architecture Chat - Shared JavaScript\n     3→ * Use this for architecture.html and diagram_expand.html\n     4→ */\n     5→\n     6→// =========================================================================\n     7→// Architecture Chat Module\n     8→// =========================================================================\n     9→\n    10→const ArchChat = {\n    11→    // Configuration (set before init)\n    12→    projectId: null,\n    13→    featureName: null,\n    14→    \n    15→    // State\n    16→    currentSessionId: null,\n    17→    eventSource: null,\n    18→    isStreaming: false,\n    19→    streamingMsgEl: null,\n    20→    streamingText: '',\n    21→    _allSessions: [],\n    22→    _modelFetchId: 0,\n    23→    _lastServiceHealth: {},\n    24→    \n    25→    // DOM Element references (populated during init)\n    26→    elements: {},\n    27→    \n    28→    /**\n    29→     * Initialize the chat module\n    30→     * @param {Object} config - { projectId, featureName, providers }\n    31→     */\n    32→    init(config) {\n    33→        this.projectId = config.projectId;\n    34→        this.featureName = config.featureName;\n    35→        this.providers = config.providers || [];\n    36→        \n    37→        this._cacheElements();\n    38→        this._attachEventListeners();\n    39→        this.loadSessions();\n    40→        this.pollServiceHealth();\n    41→        setInterval(() => this.pollServiceHealth(), 10000);\n    42→        \n    43→        if (this.providers.length > 0) {\n    44→            this.fetchModels(this.providers[0].name);\n    45→        }\n    46→    },\n    47→    \n    48→    /**\n    49→     * Cache DOM element references\n    50→     */\n    51→    _cacheElements() {\n    52→        this.elements = {\n    53→            panel: document.getElementById('arch-chat-panel'),\n    54→            fab: document.getElementById('arch-chat-fab'),\n    55→            messages: document.getElementById('arch-chat-messages'),\n    56→            input: document.getElementById('arch-chat-input'),\n    57→            sendBtn: document.getElementById('arch-chat-send-btn'),\n    58→            cancelBtn: document.getElementById('arch-chat-cancel-btn'),\n    59→            sessionPopup: document.getElementById('arch-session-popup'),\n    60→            sessionList: document.getElementById('arch-session-list'),\n    61→            sessionName: document.getElementById('arch-session-name'),\n    62→            providerSelect: document.getElementById('arch-chat-provider'),\n    63→            modelSelect: document.getElementById('arch-chat-model'),\n    64→            attachedContext: document.getElementById('arch-attached-context'),\n    65→            attachedList: document.getElementById('arch-attached-list'),\n    66→            inputContext: document.getElementById('arch-input-context'),\n    67→            contextCount: document.getElementById('arch-context-count'),\n    68→            selectedElementsBar: document.getElementById('arch-selected-elements-bar'),\n    69→            selectedElementsList: document.getElementById('arch-selected-elements-list'),\n    70→            welcome: document.getElementById('arch-chat-welcome'),\n    71→        };\n    72→    },\n    73→    \n    74→    /**\n    75→     * Attach event listeners\n    76→     */\n    77→    _attachEventListeners() {\n    78→        // Enter to send\n    79→        this.elements.input?.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n    80→            if (e.key === 'Enter' && !e.shiftKey) {\n    81→                e.preventDefault();\n    82→                if (!this.isStreaming && this.currentSessionId) this.sendChat();\n    83→            }\n    84→        });\n    85→        \n    86→        // Auto-resize textarea\n    87→        this.elements.input?.addEventListener('input', (e) => {\n    88→            e.target.style.height = 'auto';\n    89→            e.target.style.height = Math.min(e.target.scrollHeight, 120) + 'px';\n    90→        });\n    91→        \n    92→        // Close popup when clicking outside\n    93→        document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n    94→            const popup = this.elements.sessionPopup;\n    95→            const dropdown = document.querySelector('.arch-chat-header-dropdown');\n    96→            if (popup && dropdown && !popup.contains(e.target) && !dropdown.contains(e.target)) {\n    97→                popup.classList.remove('open');\n    98→            }\n    99→        });\n   100→    },\n   101→    \n   102→    // =========================================================================\n   103→    // UI Actions\n   104→    // =========================================================================\n   105→    \n   106→    togglePanel() {\n   107→        const isOpen = this.elements.panel?.classList.toggle('open');\n   108→        this.elements.fab?.classList.toggle('hidden-fab', isOpen);\n   109→        if (isOpen && !this.currentSessionId) {\n   110→            this.loadSessions();\n   111→        }\n   112→    },\n   113→    \n   114→    toggleSessionPopup() {\n   115→        this.elements.sessionPopup?.classList.toggle('open');\n   116→    },\n   117→    \n   118→    setInput(text) {\n   119→        if (this.elements.input) {\n   120→            this.elements.input.value = text;\n   121→            this.elements.input.focus();\n   122→        }\n   123→    },\n   124→    \n   125→    // =========================================================================\n   126→    // Session Management\n   127→    // =========================================================================\n   128→    \n   129→    async loadSessions() {\n   130→        try {\n   131→            const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${this.projectId}/chat/sessions?feature=${this.featureName}`);\n   132→            const sessions = await resp.json();\n   133→            this._allSessions = sessions;\n   134→            this._renderSessionList();\n   135→            \n   136→            if (sessions.length > 0 && !this.currentSessionId) {\n   137→                await this.loadSession(sessions[0].id);\n   138→            }\n   139→        } catch (err) {\n   140→            console.error('Failed to load sessions:', err);\n   141→        }\n   142→    },\n   143→    \n   144→    _renderSessionList() {\n   145→        const list = this.elements.sessionList;\n   146→        if (!list) return;\n   147→        \n   148→        if (this._allSessions.length === 0) {\n   149→            list.innerHTML = '<div style=\"padding: 20px; text-align: center; color: #737373; font-size: 0.875rem;\">No sessions yet</div>';\n   150→            return;\n   151→        }\n   152→        \n   153→        list.innerHTML = this._allSessions.map(s => {\n   154→            const date = new Date(s.updated_at).toLocaleDateString();\n   155→            const isActive = s.id === this.currentSessionId;\n   156→            return `\n   157→                <div class=\"arch-session-item ${isActive ? 'active' : ''}\" onclick=\"ArchChat.selectSession('${s.id}')\">\n   158→                    <div class=\"arch-session-item-info\">\n   159→                        <div class=\"arch-session-item-name\">${this._escapeHtml(s.name)}</div>\n   160→                        <div class=\"arch-session-item-meta\">${s.message_count} messages · ${date}</div>\n   161→                    </div>\n   162→                    <button class=\"arch-session-item-delete\" onclick=\"event.stopPropagation(); ArchChat.deleteSession('${s.id}')\" title=\"Delete\">\n   163→                        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M4 4l8 8M12 4l-8 8\"/></svg>\n   164→                    </button>\n   165→                </div>\n   166→            `;\n   167→        }).join('');\n   168→    },\n   169→    \n   170→    async selectSession(sessionId) {\n   171→        this.toggleSessionPopup();\n   172→        if (sessionId === this.currentSessionId) return;\n   173→        await this.loadSession(sessionId);\n   174→    },\n   175→    \n   176→    async loadSession(sessionId) {\n   177→        try {\n   178→            if (this.currentSessionId && this.currentSessionId !== sessionId) {\n   179→                fetch(`/api/projects/${this.projectId}/chat/sessions/${this.currentSessionId}/cancel`, { method: 'POST' }).catch(() => {});\n   180→            }\n   181→            \n   182→            const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${this.projectId}/chat/sessions/${sessionId}`);\n   183→            if (!resp.ok) throw new Error('Session not found');\n   184→            const session = await resp.json();\n   185→            \n   186→            this.currentSessionId = sessionId;\n   187→            \n   188→            // Update header\n   189→            if (this.elements.sessionName) {\n   190→                this.elements.sessionName.textContent = session.name;\n   191→            }\n   192→            \n   193→            // Sync provider/model dropdowns\n   194→            if (session.provider && this.elements.providerSelect) {\n   195→                this.elements.providerSelect.value = session.provider;\n   196→                await this.fetchModels(session.provider);\n   197→                if (session.model && this.elements.modelSelect) {\n   198→                    this.elements.modelSelect.value = session.model;\n   199→                }\n   200→            }\n   201→            \n   202→            // Render messages\n   203→            if (this.elements.welcome) this.elements.welcome.style.display = 'none';\n   204→            if (this.elements.messages) this.elements.messages.innerHTML = '';\n   205→            \n   206→            session.messages.forEach(m => {\n   207→                this.appendMessage(m.role, m.content, false);\n   208→            });\n   209→            \n   210→            this.setChatEnabled(true);\n   211→            this.connectSSE(sessionId);\n   212→            this._renderSessionList();\n   213→        } catch (err) {\n   214→            console.error('Failed to load session:', err);\n   215→        }\n   216→    },\n   217→    \n   218→    async createNewSession() {\n   219→        const provider = this.getSelectedProvider();\n   220→        const model = this.elements.modelSelect?.value;\n   221→        if (!model) { alert('Select a model first'); return; }\n   222→        \n   223→        try {\n   224→            const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${this.projectId}/chat/sessions`, {\n   225→                method: 'POST',\n   226→                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n   227→                body: JSON.stringify({\n   228→                    feature_name: this.featureName,\n   229→                    provider: provider,\n   230→                    model: model,\n   231→                }),\n   232→            });\n   233→            const session = await resp.json();\n   234→            \n   235→            await this.loadSessions();\n   236→            await this.loadSession(session.id);\n   237→        } catch (err) {\n   238→            console.error('Failed to create session:', err);\n   239→        }\n   240→    },\n   241→    \n   242→    async deleteSession(sessionId) {\n   243→        if (!confirm('Delete this chat session?')) return;\n   244→        try {\n   245→            await fetch(`/api/projects/${this.projectId}/chat/sessions/${sessionId}`, { method: 'DELETE' });\n   246→            \n   247→            if (this.currentSessionId === sessionId) {\n   248→                this.disconnectSSE();\n   249→                this.currentSessionId = null;\n   250→                this.setChatEnabled(false);\n   251→                \n   252→                // Show welcome state\n   253→                if (this.elements.messages) this.elements.messages.innerHTML = '';\n   254→                if (this.elements.welcome) this.elements.welcome.style.display = 'flex';\n   255→                if (this.elements.sessionName) this.elements.sessionName.textContent = 'New AI chat';\n   256→            }\n   257→            \n   258→            await this.loadSessions();\n   259→        } catch (err) {\n   260→            console.error('Failed to delete session:', err);\n   261→        }\n   262→    },\n   263→    \n   264→    // =========================================================================\n   265→    // Provider & Model\n   266→    // =========================================================================\n   267→    \n   268→    getSelectedProvider() {\n   269→        return this.elements.providerSelect?.value || 'claude';\n   270→    },\n   271→    \n   272→    onProviderChange() {\n   273→        this.fetchModels(this.getSelectedProvider());\n   274→    },\n   275→    \n   276→    async fetchModels(providerName) {\n   277→        const thisId = ++this._modelFetchId;\n   278→        if (this.elements.modelSelect) {\n   279→            this.elements.modelSelect.innerHTML = '<option disabled selected>Loading models...</option>';\n   280→        }\n   281→        \n   282→        try {\n   283→            const resp = await fetch(`/api/providers/${providerName}/models`);\n   284→            if (thisId !== this._modelFetchId) return;\n   285→            if (!resp.ok) throw new Error('Failed');\n   286→            const data = await resp.json();\n   287→            if (thisId !== this._modelFetchId) return;\n   288→            \n   289→            if (data.error) {\n   290→                if (this.elements.modelSelect) {\n   291→                    this.elements.modelSelect.innerHTML = '<option disabled selected>Timed out</option>';\n   292→                }\n   293→                return;\n   294→            }\n   295→            \n   296→            if (this.elements.modelSelect) {\n   297→                this.elements.modelSelect.innerHTML = '';\n   298→                data.models.forEach(m => {\n   299→                    const opt = document.createElement('option');\n   300→                    opt.value = m;\n   301→                    opt.textContent = m;\n   302→                    this.elements.modelSelect.appendChild(opt);\n   303→                });\n   304→            }\n   305→        } catch {\n   306→            if (thisId !== this._modelFetchId) return;\n   307→            if (this.elements.modelSelect) {\n   308→                this.elements.modelSelect.innerHTML = '<option disabled selected>Failed</option>';\n   309→            }\n   310→        }\n   311→    },\n   312→    \n   313→    // =========================================================================\n   314→    // Service Health\n   315→    // =========================================================================\n   316→    \n   317→    async pollServiceHealth() {\n   318→        try {\n   319→            const resp = await fetch('/api/services/health');\n   320→            if (!resp.ok) return;\n   321→            const data = await resp.json();\n   322→            const services = data.services || [];\n   323→            \n   324→            this._lastServiceHealth = {};\n   325→            services.forEach(svc => {\n   326→                this._lastServiceHealth[svc.name] = svc;\n   327→                const dotId = svc.name === 'companion' ? 'arch-status-companion' : `arch-status-${svc.name}`;\n   328→                const dot = document.getElementById(dotId);\n   329→                if (dot) {\n   330→                    dot.classList.toggle('online', svc.status === 'running');\n   331→                }\n   332→            });\n   333→            \n   334→            this.updateProviderAvailability(services);\n   335→        } catch (e) {\n   336→            // Silently fail\n   337→        }\n   338→    },\n   339→    \n   340→    updateProviderAvailability(services) {\n   341→        if (!this.elements.providerSelect || !this.elements.providerSelect.options) return;\n   342→        \n   343→        for (const opt of this.elements.providerSelect.options) {\n   344→            const svcName = opt.value === 'claude' ? 'companion' : opt.value;\n   345→            const svc = services.find(s => s.name === svcName);\n   346→            if (svc && svc.status !== 'running') {\n   347→                opt.disabled = true;\n   348→                opt.textContent = opt.textContent.replace(/ \\(offline\\)$/, '') + ' (offline)';\n   349→            } else {\n   350→                opt.disabled = false;\n   351→                opt.textContent = opt.textContent.replace(/ \\(offline\\)$/, '');\n   352→            }\n   353→        }\n   354→    },\n   355→    \n   356→    // =========================================================================\n   357→    // SSE Connection\n   358→    // =========================================================================\n   359→    \n   360→    connectSSE(sessionId) {\n   361→        this.disconnectSSE();\n   362→        const url = `/api/projects/${this.projectId}/chat/sessions/${sessionId}/stream`;\n   363→        this.eventSource = new EventSource(url);\n   364→        \n   365→        this.eventSource.addEventListener('token', (e) => {\n   366→            const data = JSON.parse(e.data);\n   367→            this.appendStreamToken(data.text);\n   368→        });\n   369→        \n   370→        this.eventSource.addEventListener('message_done', (e) => {\n   371→            const data = JSON.parse(e.data);\n   372→            this.finalizeStreamMessage(data.content);\n   373→        });\n   374→        \n   375→        this.eventSource.addEventListener('chat_error', (e) => {\n   376→            const data = JSON.parse(e.data);\n   377→            this.finishStreaming();\n   378→            this.appendMessage('error', data.detail, false);\n   379→        });\n   380→        \n   381→        this.eventSource.addEventListener('diagram_changed', (e) => {\n   382→            const data = JSON.parse(e.data);\n   383→            if (typeof onDiagramChanged === 'function') {\n   384→                onDiagramChanged(data.file, data.content);\n   385→            }\n   386→        });\n   387→        \n   388→        this.eventSource.addEventListener('diagram_added', (e) => {\n   389→            const data = JSON.parse(e.data);\n   390→            if (typeof onDiagramAdded === 'function') {\n   391→                onDiagramAdded(data.file, data.content);\n   392→            }\n   393→        });\n   394→        \n   395→        this.eventSource.addEventListener('diagram_removed', (e) => {\n   396→            const data = JSON.parse(e.data);\n   397→            if (typeof onDiagramRemoved === 'function') {\n   398→                onDiagramRemoved(data.file);\n   399→            }\n   400→        });\n   401→        \n   402→        this.eventSource.addEventListener('ping', () => {});\n   403→        \n   404→        this.eventSource.onerror = () => {\n   405→            // Auto-reconnect is handled by EventSource\n   406→        };\n   407→    },\n   408→    \n   409→    disconnectSSE() {\n   410→        if (this.eventSource) {\n   411→            this.eventSource.close();\n   412→            this.eventSource = null;\n   413→        }\n   414→    },\n   415→    \n   416→    // =========================================================================\n   417→    // Messaging\n   418→    // =========================================================================\n   419→    \n   420→    appendMessage(role, content, scroll = true) {\n   421→        if (this.elements.welcome) this.elements.welcome.style.display = 'none';\n   422→        if (!this.elements.messages) return;\n   423→        \n   424→        const div = document.createElement('div');\n   425→        div.className = `arch-chat-msg ${role}`;\n   426→        \n   427→        if (role === 'assistant') {\n   428→            div.innerHTML = `\n   429→                <div class=\"arch-msg-avatar\">\n   430→                    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n   431→                        <path d=\"M12 3c-4.5 0-8 3.5-8 8 0 2.5 1.5 4.5 3 6l-1 4 4-1c1.5.5 3 .5 4.5.5 4.5 0 8-3.5 8-8s-3.5-8-8-8z\"/>\n   432→                    </svg>\n   433→                </div>\n   434→                <div class=\"arch-msg-content\">${marked.parse(content)}</div>\n   435→            `;\n   436→        } else if (role === 'user') {\n   437→            div.innerHTML = `<div class=\"arch-msg-bubble\">${this._escapeHtml(content)}</div>`;\n   438→        } else if (role === 'error') {\n   439→            div.innerHTML = `\n   440→                <div class=\"arch-msg-avatar\" style=\"background: #ef4444;\">\n   441→                    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n   442→                        <path d=\"M12 8v4M12 16h.01\"/>\n   443→                    </svg>\n   444→                </div>\n   445→                <div class=\"arch-msg-content\">${this._escapeHtml(content)}</div>\n   446→            `;\n   447→        }\n   448→        \n   449→        this.elements.messages.appendChild(div);\n   450→        if (scroll) this.elements.messages.scrollTop = this.elements.messages.scrollHeight;\n   451→        return div;\n   452→    },\n   453→    \n   454→    showThinking() {\n   455→        this.hideThinking();\n   456→        if (this.elements.welcome) this.elements.welcome.style.display = 'none';\n   457→        if (!this.elements.messages) return;\n   458→        \n   459→        const el = document.createElement('div');\n   460→        el.className = 'arch-chat-thinking';\n   461→        el.id = 'arch-thinking-indicator';\n   462→        el.innerHTML = `\n   463→            <div class=\"arch-thinking-avatar\">\n   464→                <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n   465→                    <path d=\"M12 3c-4.5 0-8 3.5-8 8 0 2.5 1.5 4.5 3 6l-1 4 4-1c1.5.5 3 .5 4.5.5 4.5 0 8-3.5 8-8s-3.5-8-8-8z\"/>\n   466→                </svg>\n   467→            </div>\n   468→            <div class=\"arch-thinking-content\">\n   469→                <span>Thinking</span>\n   470→                <div class=\"arch-thinking-dots\">\n   471→                    <div class=\"arch-thinking-dot\"></div>\n   472→                    <div class=\"arch-thinking-dot\"></div>\n   473→                    <div class=\"arch-thinking-dot\"></div>\n   474→                </div>\n   475→            </div>\n   476→        `;\n   477→        this.elements.messages.appendChild(el);\n   478→        this.elements.messages.scrollTop = this.elements.messages.scrollHeight;\n   479→    },\n   480→    \n   481→    hideThinking() {\n   482→        const el = document.getElementById('arch-thinking-indicator');\n   483→        if (el) el.remove();\n   484→    },\n   485→    \n   486→    appendStreamToken(text) {\n   487→        this.hideThinking();\n   488→        if (this.elements.welcome) this.elements.welcome.style.display = 'none';\n   489→        if (!this.elements.messages) return;\n   490→        \n   491→        if (!this.streamingMsgEl) {\n   492→            this.streamingMsgEl = document.createElement('div');\n   493→            this.streamingMsgEl.className = 'arch-chat-msg assistant';\n   494→            this.streamingMsgEl.innerHTML = `\n   495→                <div class=\"arch-msg-avatar\">\n   496→                    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n   497→                        <path d=\"M12 3c-4.5 0-8 3.5-8 8 0 2.5 1.5 4.5 3 6l-1 4 4-1c1.5.5 3 .5 4.5.5 4.5 0 8-3.5 8-8s-3.5-8-8-8z\"/>\n   498→                    </svg>\n   499→                </div>\n   500→                <div class=\"arch-msg-content\"></div>\n   501→            `;\n   502→            this.elements.messages.appendChild(this.streamingMsgEl);\n   503→            this.streamingText = '';\n   504→            this.isStreaming = true;\n   505→        }\n   506→        \n   507→        this.streamingText += text;\n   508→        const contentEl = this.streamingMsgEl.querySelector('.arch-msg-content');\n   509→        if (contentEl) {\n   510→            contentEl.innerHTML = marked.parse(this.streamingText);\n   511→        }\n   512→        this.elements.messages.scrollTop = this.elements.messages.scrollHeight;\n   513→    },\n   514→    \n   515→    finalizeStreamMessage(fullContent) {\n   516→        if (this.streamingMsgEl) {\n   517→            const content = fullContent || this.streamingText;\n   518→            const contentEl = this.streamingMsgEl.querySelector('.arch-msg-content');\n   519→            if (contentEl) {\n   520→                contentEl.innerHTML = marked.parse(content);\n   521→            }\n   522→        }\n   523→        this.finishStreaming();\n   524→    },\n   525→    \n   526→    finishStreaming() {\n   527→        this.hideThinking();\n   528→        this.streamingMsgEl = null;\n   529→        this.streamingText = '';\n   530→        this.isStreaming = false;\n   531→        this.setChatBusy(false);\n   532→    },\n   533→    \n   534→    async sendChat() {\n   535→        if (!this.elements.input || !this.currentSessionId) return;\n   536→        \n   537→        const message = this.elements.input.value.trim();\n   538→        if (!message) return;\n   539→        \n   540→        this.elements.input.value = '';\n   541→        this.appendMessage('user', message);\n   542→        this.showThinking();\n   543→        \n   544→        // Build context (override this in page-specific code)\n   545→        const context = this.buildContext ? this.buildContext() : '';\n   546→        \n   547→        this.setChatBusy(true);\n   548→        \n   549→        try {\n   550→            const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${this.projectId}/chat/sessions/${this.currentSessionId}/messages`, {\n   551→                method: 'POST',\n   552→                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n   553→                body: JSON.stringify({\n   554→                    message,\n   555→                    context: context || null,\n   556→                    provider: this.getSelectedProvider(),\n   557→                    model: this.elements.modelSelect?.value || null,\n   558→                }),\n   559→            });\n   560→            \n   561→            if (!resp.ok) {\n   562→                const detail = await resp.json().catch(() => null);\n   563→                this.finishStreaming();\n   564→                this.appendMessage('error', detail?.detail || 'Failed to send message');\n   565→                this.setChatEnabled(true);\n   566→                return;\n   567→            }\n   568→            // Response streams via SSE\n   569→        } catch (err) {\n   570→            this.finishStreaming();\n   571→            this.appendMessage('error', err.message);\n   572→            this.setChatEnabled(true);\n   573→        }\n   574→    },\n   575→    \n   576→    async cancelChat() {\n   577→        if (!this.currentSessionId) return;\n   578→        try {\n   579→            await fetch(`/api/projects/${this.projectId}/chat/sessions/${this.currentSessionId}/cancel`, { method: 'POST' });\n   580→        } catch {}\n   581→        this.finishStreaming();\n   582→        if (this.elements.input) this.elements.input.disabled = false;\n   583→    },\n   584→    \n   585→    setChatEnabled(enabled) {\n   586→        if (this.elements.input) this.elements.input.disabled = !enabled;\n   587→        if (this.elements.sendBtn) this.elements.sendBtn.disabled = !enabled;\n   588→    },\n   589→    \n   590→    setChatBusy(busy) {\n   591→        if (this.elements.sendBtn) {\n   592→            this.elements.sendBtn.style.display = busy ? 'none' : 'flex';\n   593→        }\n   594→        if (this.elements.cancelBtn) {\n   595→            this.elements.cancelBtn.style.display = busy ? 'flex' : 'none';\n   596→        }\n   597→        if (this.elements.input) this.elements.input.disabled = busy;\n   598→    },\n   599→    \n   600→    // =========================================================================\n   601→    // Utilities\n   602→    // =========================================================================\n   603→    \n   604→    _escapeHtml(str) {\n   605→        if (!str) return '';\n   606→        return str.replace(/&/g, '&amp;')\n   607→                  .replace(/</g, '&lt;')\n   608→                  .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')\n   609→                  .replace(/\"/g, '&quot;')\n   610→                  .replace(/'/g, '&#039;');\n   611→    }\n   612→};\n   613→\n   614→// Export for use in templates\n   615→if (typeof module !== 'undefined' && module.exports) {\n   616→    module.exports = ArchChat;\n   617→}\n   618→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LpsTfCbnvthknh6XjnhhgC","session_id":"5856037d-22b3-414c-9b3a-aae0b154d72e","uuid":"b5a91ac2-7171-47d4-8e00-400f7ebe7b18"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LpsTfCbnvthknh6XjnhhgC","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile a comprehensive analysis of these components.\n\n---\n\n## Analysis: Architecture Diagram Viewer & Chat System\n\n### Overview\n\nThe architecture diagram viewer (`/project/{project_id}/arch/{feature_name}`) is a full-featured web application that displays Mermaid and Draw.io diagrams from a feature's `arch/` directory, with an integrated AI chat panel for discussing diagrams. The system uses Server-Sent Events (SSE) for real-time streaming of chat responses and live diagram updates via filesystem watching.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Schema Definition: `vista/templates/arch-schema.json`\n\n### Current Structure (Lines 1-64)\n\n**Required Fields:**\n- `feature` (string): Feature name matching directory name\n- `diagrams` (array): List of diagram file references\n\n**Diagram Entry Schema (Lines 15-60):**\n- `name` (string): Human-readable diagram name\n- `file` (string): Filename relative to `arch/` directory\n- `type` (enum): `\"mermaid\"` or `\"drawio\"` (line 29)\n- `diagramType` (enum, lines 35-46): Specific diagram subtype with 11 values:\n  - `flowchart`, `sequence`, `state`, `er`, `gantt`\n  - `architecture`, `wireframe`, `custom`\n  - `logic-flow`, `decision-tree`, `test-contract`\n- `category` (enum, optional, lines 49-53): \n  - `\"architecture\"` (default)\n  - `\"tdd\"`\n- `description` (string): Brief description\n\n---\n\n## 2. Main Template: `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\n### Page Structure (Lines 1-2418)\n\n**Template Inheritance (Line 1):**\n```jinja\n{% extends \"_base.html\" %}\n```\n\n**External Dependencies (Lines 6-7):**\n- Mermaid v11: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.min.js`\n- Marked v15: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@15/marked.min.js`\n- Custom CSS: `/static/arch-chat.css`\n\n---\n\n### A. Diagram Rendering System\n\n#### Mermaid Initialization (Lines 1224-1238)\n\n```javascript\nmermaid.initialize({\n    startOnLoad: false,\n    theme: 'dark',\n    themeVariables: {\n        darkMode: true,\n        background: '#0f172a',\n        primaryColor: '#1e3a5f',\n        // ... 7 more color variables\n    }\n});\n```\n\n**Theme Toggle Support (Lines 1240-1261):**\n- Light theme variables defined at lines 1240-1249\n- Dark theme variables defined at lines 1251-1261\n- Theme toggle buttons in diagram headers (lines 1016-1023)\n\n#### Diagram Loading Flow (Lines 1270-1286)\n\n**Entry Point:** `loadDiagrams()` function\n1. Iterates through `DIAGRAMS` array (from server-side template variable)\n2. Fetches each diagram file via API: `/api/projects/{PROJECT_ID}/features/{FEATURE_NAME}/arch/{diagram.file}`\n3. Calls `renderDiagramContent()` for each file\n4. Initializes pan/zoom viewport\n\n#### Rendering Dispatch (Lines 1288-1311)\n\n**Function:** `renderDiagramContent(el, filename, content, idx)`\n\n**Mermaid Path (Lines 1289-1307):**\n- Checks `filename.endsWith('.mmd')` (line 1289)\n- Calls `mermaid.render(id, content)` at line 1292\n- Returns `{ svg }` object, injected via `el.innerHTML = svg` (line 1293)\n- Attaches click handlers to `.node` elements for selection (lines 1295-1302)\n- Reapplies existing selections (line 1304)\n- Error handling: displays parse error message (lines 1305-1307)\n\n**Fallback Path (Lines 1308-1310):**\n- Non-Mermaid files rendered as escaped plain text in `<pre>` tag\n\n**No Draw.io Renderer:** Despite schema supporting `type: \"drawio\"`, there's no dedicated Draw.io rendering logic. Draw.io files would display as escaped XML via the fallback path.\n\n---\n\n### B. Interactive Features\n\n#### Pan & Zoom (Lines 1323-1375)\n\n**Initialization:** `initViewport(idx)` sets up per-diagram viewport state at line 1326:\n```javascript\nviewportState[idx] = { scale: 1, panX: 0, panY: 0, dragging: false, startX: 0, startY: 0 };\n```\n\n**Event Handlers:**\n- **Wheel:** Zoom in/out on scroll (lines 1327-1331)\n- **Mousedown:** Start drag operation (lines 1332-1339)\n- **Mousemove:** Pan diagram while dragging (lines 1340-1346)\n- **Mouseup/Mouseleave:** Stop dragging (lines 1347-1353)\n\n**Transform Application (Lines 1356-1361):**\n```javascript\nvp.style.transform = `translate(${st.panX}px, ${st.panY}px) scale(${st.scale})`;\n```\n\n**Zoom Controls (Lines 1033-1041):**\n- Zoom out button: `zoomDiagram(idx, -0.2)` (line 1034)\n- Reset button: `resetZoom(idx)` (line 1035)\n- Zoom in button: `zoomDiagram(idx, 0.2)` (line 1036)\n- Expand button: Links to full-page view `/project/{id}/arch/{feature}/diagram/{file}` (lines 1037-1040)\n\n#### Element Selection (Lines 1629-1726)\n\n**Node Click Handler (Lines 1295-1302):**\n- Attached to every `.node` element in rendered SVG\n- Calls `toggleElementSelection(filename, nodeId, node)` on click\n- Stops propagation to prevent card-level events\n\n**Node ID Extraction (Lines 1631-1641):**\n- **Mermaid v11 pattern:** Matches `flowchart-NodeId-123` format (line 1633)\n- **Fallback 1:** Splits on hyphens, takes all but last part (line 1636)\n- **Fallback 2:** Uses node's text content (line 1639)\n\n**Selection State (Lines 1643-1664):**\n- Stored in `selectedElements` Map: `filename -> Set<nodeId>`\n- Toggles `.node-selected` CSS class on SVG element (lines 1651, 1656)\n- Auto-attaches diagram if not already attached (lines 1658-1661)\n- Updates UI bar showing selected elements (line 1663)\n\n**Connection Extraction (Lines 1666-1678):**\n`getNodeConnections(filename, nodeId)` parses diagram source:\n- Splits content by lines\n- Matches lines containing nodeId AND arrow patterns `[-=.]+>` or `[-=.]+\\|` (line 1673)\n- Returns array of connection lines for context\n\n**Selection Persistence (Lines 1680-1689):**\n`reapplySelections(el, filename)` called after diagram re-render to restore `.node-selected` classes\n\n---\n\n### C. Chat Panel Implementation\n\n#### Panel Structure (Lines 1054-1201)\n\n**Floating Panel (Lines 1146-176):**\n- Fixed position: `bottom: 24px, right: 24px`\n- Dimensions: `width: 480px`, `height: 60vh`\n- Resizable: `resize: both` CSS property\n- Draggable: Via header when unlocked (lines 1400-1462)\n- Lock toggle: Controls draggability and resize (lines 1518-1539)\n\n**Header Components (Lines 1056-1080):**\n- Session dropdown (lines 1058-1061)\n- Window size controls (S/M/L buttons, lines 1064-1068)\n- Lock/unlock button (line 1069-1072)\n- New session button (line 1073-1075)\n- Close button (lines 1076-1078)\n\n**Configuration Bars:**\n- **Provider/Model selects** (lines 1097-1110): Rendered if `providers` length > 1\n- **Service status indicators** (lines 1113-1122): Shows online/offline dots for Claude/OpenCode\n- **Attached context bar** (lines 1125-1128): Lists attached diagram files\n- **Selected elements bar** (lines 1130-1134): Shows selected nodes with \"Clear\" button\n\n#### Session Management (Lines 1828-2008)\n\n**Session Storage:** Files at `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json` (per `chat_session_service.py` lines 14, 26)\n\n**Load Sessions (Lines 1830-1844):**\n- Fetches `/api/projects/{PROJECT_ID}/chat/sessions?feature={FEATURE_NAME}` (line 1832)\n- Auto-selects most recent if no current session (lines 1838-1840)\n\n**Session Rendering (Lines 1846-1870):**\n- Displays session name, message count, updated date\n- Shows delete button on hover\n- Active session highlighted with `.active` class\n\n**Load Session (Lines 1905-1952):**\n- Cancels previous session's chat if switching (lines 1907-1909)\n- Fetches session data (line 1911)\n- Updates header name (line 1919)\n- Syncs provider/model dropdowns (lines 1922-1933)\n- Renders message history (lines 1942-1944)\n- Connects SSE stream (line 1947)\n\n#### Messaging Flow (Lines 2074-2278)\n\n**Send Chat (Lines 2219-2278):**\n\n1. **Validation:** Checks message not empty and session exists (lines 2220-2222)\n2. **UI Update:** Clears input, appends user message bubble (lines 2224-2226), shows thinking indicator (line 2229)\n3. **Context Assembly (lines 2232-2250):**\n   - Iterates attached diagrams\n   - Includes full diagram content\n   - For selected elements: adds node ID + connections extracted via `getNodeConnections()`\n   - Format: `--- SELECTED ELEMENTS in {file} ---\\nFocus: {nodeId}\\nConnections:\\n  {line}\\n--- END SELECTED ---`\n4. **API Call:** POST to `/api/projects/{PROJECT_ID}/chat/sessions/{SESSION_ID}/messages` (line 2255)\n5. **Request Body (lines 2258-2263):**\n   ```json\n   {\n       \"message\": \"user's text\",\n       \"context\": \"diagram content + selections\",\n       \"provider\": \"claude\",\n       \"model\": \"sonnet\"\n   }\n   ```\n6. **Streaming:** Response arrives via SSE connection (line 2272)\n\n**SSE Connection (Lines 2021-2062):**\n\n**Event Types Handled:**\n- `token` (lines 2026-2029): Appends streaming text token-by-token\n- `message_done` (lines 2031-2034): Finalizes message with full content\n- `chat_error` (lines 2036-2040): Displays error message\n- `diagram_changed` (lines 2042-2045): Updates diagram in place\n- `diagram_added` (lines 2047-2050): Adds new diagram card\n- `diagram_removed` (lines 2052-2055): Removes diagram card\n- `ping` (line 2057): Keepalive, no-op\n\n**Streaming Message Rendering (Lines 2144-2183):**\n- Creates `.chat-msg.assistant` div with avatar on first token (lines 2154-2162)\n- Accumulates text in `streamingText` variable (line 2166)\n- Re-renders with `marked.parse(streamingText)` after each token (line 2170)\n- Auto-scrolls to bottom (line 2172)\n- Finalizes on `message_done` event (lines 2175-2183)\n\n---\n\n### D. Live Diagram Updates (Lines 2283-2369)\n\n**Update Existing Diagram (Lines 2284-2302):**\n- Finds diagram by filename in `DIAGRAMS` array (line 2288)\n- Adds `.diagram-updating` class for visual feedback (lines 2296-2299)\n- Re-renders via `renderDiagramContent()` (line 2301)\n\n**Add New Diagram (Lines 2304-2356):**\n- Creates diagram object `{ file, name, category: 'architecture' }` (line 2311)\n- Appends to `DIAGRAMS` array (line 2312)\n- Builds HTML card with full structure (lines 2319-2346)\n- Renders content and initializes viewport (lines 2349-2351)\n- Flashes update animation (lines 2354-2355)\n\n**Remove Diagram (Lines 2358-2369):**\n- Fades out card with `opacity: 0.3` (line 2361)\n- Removes after 500ms (line 2362)\n- Cleans up state: `diagramContents`, `attachedDiagrams`, `selectedElements` (lines 2364-2366)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Backend Services\n\n### A. Progress Service: `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n\n**Read Manifest (Lines 50-63):**\n```python\ndef read_arch_manifest(project_path: str, feature_name: str) -> Optional[dict]:\n    arch_file = Path(project_path) / \".vista\" / \"features\" / feature_name / \"arch\" / \"_arch.json\"\n    if not arch_file.exists():\n        return None\n    try:\n        data = json.loads(arch_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        # Legacy format migration: bare list -> dict\n        if isinstance(data, list):\n            data = {\"feature\": feature_name, \"diagrams\": data}\n        return data\n    except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):\n        return None\n```\n\n**Read Diagram File (Lines 77-97):**\n\n**Path Traversal Protection (Lines 80-92):**\n1. Extracts filename only: `safe_name = Path(filename).name` (line 81)\n2. Rejects if mismatch or contains `..` (line 82)\n3. Constructs target path (line 86)\n4. Resolves and validates within `arch_dir`: `target.resolve().relative_to(arch_dir.resolve())` (line 90)\n5. Returns `None` on `ValueError` (line 92)\n\n---\n\n### B. Architecture Routes: `vista/server/routes/architecture.py`\n\n**API Endpoints:**\n\n1. **GET `/api/projects/{project_id}/features/{feature_name}/arch`** (lines 15-26)\n   - Returns `_arch.json` manifest\n   - Uses `ProgressService.read_arch_manifest()`\n\n2. **GET `/api/projects/{project_id}/features/{feature_name}/arch/{filename}`** (lines 29-48)\n   - Returns raw diagram file content\n   - Uses `ProgressService.read_arch_file()` with path traversal protection\n   - Content-Type: `text/plain` for `.mmd`, `application/xml` for `.drawio`\n\n**Page Routes:**\n\n3. **GET `/project/{project_id}/arch/{feature_name}`** (lines 51-66)\n   - Renders `architecture.html` template\n   - Template context: `{ project, feature_name, manifest, providers }`\n\n4. **GET `/project/{project_id}/arch/{feature_name}/diagram/{filename}`** (lines 69-91)\n   - Full-page diagram view\n   - Renders `diagram_expand.html` template\n   - Derives diagram name: `filename.rsplit('.', 1)[0].replace('-', ' ').title()` (line 82)\n\n---\n\n### C. Chat Session Service: `vista/server/services/chat_session_service.py`\n\n**Session Files (Lines 14, 21-26):**\n- Directory: `server/data/sessions/{project_id}/`\n- Filename: `{session_id}.json`\n\n**Create Session (Lines 28-46):**\n- Generates UUID session ID via `ChatSession.generate_id()` (line 38)\n- Default name: `\"New Chat\"` (line 42)\n- Saves to disk immediately (line 45)\n\n**List Sessions (Lines 48-65):**\n- Sorted by modified time descending: `sorted(..., key=lambda p: p.stat().st_mtime, reverse=True)` (line 57)\n- Optionally filters by `feature_name` (lines 60-61)\n- Returns summary dicts (line 62)\n\n**Add Message (Lines 82-96):**\n- Appends `ChatMessage` to session's `messages` array (lines 89-90)\n- Updates `updated_at` timestamp (line 91)\n- Auto-names session from first user message: `ChatSession.auto_name(content)` (lines 93-94)\n\n---\n\n### D. Chat Session Routes: `vista/server/routes/chat_sessions.py`\n\n**SSE Broadcasting (Lines 27-58):**\n\n**Subscriber Pattern:**\n- Global dict `_session_subscribers: dict[str, list[asyncio.Queue]]` (line 27)\n- `_subscribe()`: Creates queue, adds to session's subscriber list (lines 30-35)\n- `_unsubscribe()`: Removes queue, deletes session key if empty (lines 38-44)\n- `_broadcast()`: Sends message to all subscribers, removes dead queues (lines 47-58)\n\n**Send Message Endpoint (Lines 159-242):**\n\n**Flow:**\n1. **Validation:** Project, session, message checks (lines 162-171)\n2. **Provider/Model Selection:** Uses request override or session defaults (lines 174-181)\n3. **Save User Message:** Calls `ChatSessionService.add_message()` (lines 184-189)\n4. **Build Context:** Uses `ContextAssembler.build_system_prompt()` and `build_full_prompt()` (lines 198-208)\n5. **Backend Session Creation:** If first message, creates protocol-native session via `provider_router.create_backend_session()` (lines 216-230)\n6. **Async Streaming:** Launches `_stream_response_router()` task (lines 232-241)\n\n**Streaming Handler (Lines 250-313):**\n\n**Event Processing:**\n- `type: \"token\"` → Broadcast `event: token` to SSE (lines 269-277)\n- `type: \"done\"` → Save assistant message, broadcast `event: message_done` (lines 278-289)\n- `type: \"result\"` → Broadcast `event: result` (lines 290-297)\n- `type: \"error\"` → Broadcast `event: chat_error` (lines 298-305)\n\n**SSE Endpoint (Lines 351-399):**\n\n**Multi-Queue Merge (lines 363-377):**\n1. Subscribe to chat events: `_subscribe(session_id)` (line 363)\n2. Subscribe to diagram watcher: `diagram_watcher.subscribe(project_id, feature_name, arch_dir)` (lines 369-371)\n3. Merge both queues into one: `_forward_queue()` helper tasks (lines 377-378)\n\n**Generator (Lines 379-398):**\n- Waits for events with 30s timeout (line 384)\n- Sends `event: ping` on timeout (line 390)\n- Handles disconnection (line 381)\n- Cleanup: Cancels forwarders, unsubscribes from both sources (lines 394-397)\n\n---\n\n### E. Diagram Watcher: `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n\n**Filesystem Monitoring (Lines 1-268):**\n\n**Watchdog Integration (Lines 23-93):**\n- Uses `watchdog.observers.Observer` for native filesystem events\n- Event handler: `_DiagramEventHandler` processes `.mmd` and `.drawio` files (line 26)\n- Events: `on_created`, `on_modified`, `on_deleted` (lines 40-50)\n\n**Debouncing (Lines 52-68):**\n- 100ms debounce via `threading.Timer` (line 52)\n- Coalesces rapid file saves (common in editors that save on every keystroke)\n- Pending events stored in dict: `path -> (event_type, filename)` (line 34)\n- Flush timer restarts on each event (lines 57-60)\n\n**Event Broadcasting (Lines 69-85):**\n- Reads file content for `diagram_changed` and `diagram_added` (line 75)\n- Schedules broadcast to async event loop via `loop.call_soon_threadsafe()` (lines 206-210)\n- Updates manifest on add/remove events (lines 84-85)\n\n**Manifest Auto-Update (Lines 232-256):**\n`_update_manifest_sync(arch_dir)`:\n1. Scans directory for `.mmd` and `.drawio` files (line 238)\n2. Detects Mermaid diagram type from first line (lines 102-118)\n3. Builds manifest entry: `{ name, file, type, diagramType }` (lines 241-247)\n4. Writes to `_arch.json` (lines 252-254)\n\n**Observer Lifecycle (Lines 176-202):**\n- Starts on first subscriber: `observer.start()` at line 186\n- Stops when last subscriber unsubscribes (lines 192-202)\n- Daemon thread (line 185) ensures cleanup on shutdown\n\n---\n\n## 4. FastAPI Application: `vista/server/app.py`\n\n**Router Registration (Lines 56-85):**\n\nAll routers included:\n- `architecture` (line 64, 79)\n- `chat_sessions` (line 65, 80)\n- `projects`, `loops`, `stream`, `plans`, `providers`, `shutdown`, `ralph`, `ralph_settings`, `sandbox`, `service_status`, `export` (lines 58-71, 73-85)\n\n**Static Files (Lines 49-51):**\n- Mounted at `/static` route\n- Directory: `vista/server/views/static/`\n\n---\n\n## 5. Settings Files\n\n### User Settings: `~/.vista/settings.json`\n\n**Structure (Lines 1-65):**\n\n**Server Config (Lines 2-7):**\n```json\n\"server\": {\n  \"auto_start\": true,\n  \"auto_open_browser\": true,\n  \"host\": \"127.0.0.1\",\n  \"port\": 3456\n}\n```\n\n**Providers (Lines 8-17):**\n```json\n\"providers\": {\n  \"claude\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"Claude Code\" },\n  \"opencode\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"OpenCode\" }\n}\n```\n\n**Ralph Settings (Lines 18-60):**\n- Defaults: `provider: \"claude\"`, `model: \"sonnet\"`, `iterations: 3` (lines 19-23)\n- Summarizer: `provider: \"claude\"`, `model: \"haiku\"` (lines 24-27)\n- Per-provider model metadata (lines 28-59)\n\n**Tools (Lines 61-64):**\n```json\n\"tools\": {\n  \"teams\": { \"enabled\": true },\n  \"ralph\": { \"enabled\": true }\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** Both `~/.vista/settings.json` and `vista/settings.json` contain identical content. Per `CLAUDE.md` line 31, persistent settings are at `~/.vista/settings.json` with legacy fallback at `vista/settings.json`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Static Assets: `vista/server/views/static/`\n\n**Files:**\n1. `app.js` - General dashboard JavaScript\n2. `arch-chat.css` - Chat panel styles (787 lines)\n3. `arch-chat.js` - Reusable chat module (618 lines)\n4. `style.css` - Global styles\n\n### Shared Chat Module: `arch-chat.js`\n\n**Purpose:** Reusable chat implementation for both `architecture.html` and `diagram_expand.html`\n\n**API (Lines 10-612):**\n\n**Initialization (Lines 32-46):**\n```javascript\nArchChat.init({\n    projectId: '...',\n    featureName: '...',\n    providers: [...]\n});\n```\n\n**Key Methods:**\n- `togglePanel()` - Show/hide chat panel (lines 106-112)\n- `loadSessions()` - Fetch and render session list (lines 129-142)\n- `createNewSession()` - Create new chat session (lines 218-239)\n- `sendChat()` - Send message with context (lines 534-574)\n- `appendMessage(role, content, scroll)` - Render chat bubble (lines 420-452)\n- `connectSSE(sessionId)` - Establish SSE connection (lines 360-407)\n\n**Extensibility:**\n- `buildContext()` - Override in page-specific code to provide diagram context (line 545)\n- Callbacks: `onDiagramChanged()`, `onDiagramAdded()`, `onDiagramRemoved()` (lines 383-399)\n\n---\n\n## Key Data Flow Patterns\n\n### 1. Diagram Display Flow\n```\nBrowser → GET /project/{id}/arch/{feature}\n       → architecture.html renders\n       → JavaScript loadDiagrams()\n       → Fetches each file: GET /api/projects/{id}/features/{feature}/arch/{file}\n       → ProgressService.read_arch_file() (path traversal check)\n       → Returns content\n       → renderDiagramContent() dispatches:\n          - .mmd → mermaid.render() → SVG injection\n          - other → <pre> tag with escaped text\n```\n\n### 2. Chat Message Flow\n```\nUser types message → sendChat()\n                  → POST /api/projects/{id}/chat/sessions/{sid}/messages\n                     { message, context, provider, model }\n                  → chat_sessions.py::send_message()\n                  → ContextAssembler.build_full_prompt()\n                  → provider_router.create_backend_session() (if first message)\n                  → _stream_response_router() async task\n                  → provider_router.send_message() yields events\n                  → _broadcast() to SSE subscribers\n                  → EventSourceResponse at /stream endpoint\n                  → Browser receives SSE events\n                  → appendStreamToken() updates UI\n                  → message_done event finalizes\n```\n\n### 3. Live Diagram Update Flow\n```\nUser edits diagram file in filesystem\n       → Watchdog Observer detects filesystem event\n       → _DiagramEventHandler.on_modified()\n       → _debounced_notify() (100ms delay)\n       → _flush() reads file content\n       → watcher._schedule_broadcast() (cross-thread)\n       → loop.call_soon_threadsafe()\n       → _broadcast() to diagram queue\n       → Merged into SSE stream\n       → EventSource 'diagram_changed' event\n       → updateDiagram() re-renders\n       → Visual pulse animation\n```\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Points\n\n### Diagram Type Detection (diagram_watcher.py lines 102-118)\nDetects from first line: `graph`, `flowchart`, `sequence`, `class`, `state`, `er`, `gantt`, `pie`, etc.\n\n### Theme Configuration (architecture.html lines 1224-1261)\n- Dark theme (default): `background: #0f172a`, `primaryColor: #1e3a5f`\n- Light theme: `background: #ffffff`, `primaryColor: #dbeafe`\n\n### SSE Timeout (chat_sessions.py line 384)\n30-second keepalive ping interval\n\n### Debounce Delay (diagram_watcher.py line 52)\n100ms filesystem event coalescing\n\n### Queue Limits\n- Chat subscribers: `maxsize=500` (chat_sessions.py line 33)\n- Diagram subscribers: `maxsize=200` (diagram_watcher.py line 159)\n- Merged queue: `maxsize=500` (chat_sessions.py line 374)\n\n---\n\n## File References Summary\n\n| Component | File Path |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| Schema | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/templates/arch-schema.json` |\n| Main Template | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/views/architecture.html` |\n| Progress Service | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/services/progress_service.py` |\n| Architecture Routes | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/routes/architecture.py` |\n| FastAPI App | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/app.py` |\n| Chat Session Service | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/services/chat_session_service.py` |\n| Chat Routes | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/routes/chat_sessions.py` |\n| Diagram Watcher | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py` |\n| Settings | `C:/Users/Grove/.vista/settings.json` |\n| Static CSS | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` |\n| Static JS | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.js` |"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: acaf8c9 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 83586\ntool_uses: 13\nduration_ms: 165480</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5856037d-22b3-414c-9b3a-aae0b154d72e","uuid":"669e5ac0-c7af-4f49-9a38-7c81f80060ba","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need detailed information about these specific files and components in the vista-expanded-visualization project at C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/\n\n1. **vista/templates/arch-schema.json** — Read the full file. I need the current schema definition, especially the `type` enum values and any `diagramType` or `category` fields.\n\n2. **vista/server/views/architecture.html** — Read the full file. I need to understand:\n   - How diagrams are currently rendered (the renderer dispatch logic)\n   - The mermaid rendering code\n   - The drawio rendering code (if any)\n   - How the chat panel works\n   - The overall page structure\n\n3. **vista/server/services/progress_service.py** — Read the methods related to arch files: `read_arch_manifest()`, `read_arch_file()`, and any path traversal protection.\n\n4. **vista/server/routes/architecture.py** — Read the full file. I need all route definitions.\n\n5. **vista/server/app.py** — Read the full file. I need to see all registered routers.\n\n6. **vista/server/services/chat_session_service.py** — If it exists, read the full file.\n\n7. **vista/server/routes/chat_sessions.py** — If it exists, read the full file.\n\n8. **vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py** — Read the full file.\n\n9. **~/.vista/settings.json** or **vista/settings.json** — Check if there's any existing settings structure.\n\n10. **vista/server/views/static/** — List all files in this directory.\n\nPlease provide the complete contents of each file found, or note if any don't exist.","agentId":"acaf8c9","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile a comprehensive analysis of these components.\n\n---\n\n## Analysis: Architecture Diagram Viewer & Chat System\n\n### Overview\n\nThe architecture diagram viewer (`/project/{project_id}/arch/{feature_name}`) is a full-featured web application that displays Mermaid and Draw.io diagrams from a feature's `arch/` directory, with an integrated AI chat panel for discussing diagrams. The system uses Server-Sent Events (SSE) for real-time streaming of chat responses and live diagram updates via filesystem watching.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Schema Definition: `vista/templates/arch-schema.json`\n\n### Current Structure (Lines 1-64)\n\n**Required Fields:**\n- `feature` (string): Feature name matching directory name\n- `diagrams` (array): List of diagram file references\n\n**Diagram Entry Schema (Lines 15-60):**\n- `name` (string): Human-readable diagram name\n- `file` (string): Filename relative to `arch/` directory\n- `type` (enum): `\"mermaid\"` or `\"drawio\"` (line 29)\n- `diagramType` (enum, lines 35-46): Specific diagram subtype with 11 values:\n  - `flowchart`, `sequence`, `state`, `er`, `gantt`\n  - `architecture`, `wireframe`, `custom`\n  - `logic-flow`, `decision-tree`, `test-contract`\n- `category` (enum, optional, lines 49-53): \n  - `\"architecture\"` (default)\n  - `\"tdd\"`\n- `description` (string): Brief description\n\n---\n\n## 2. Main Template: `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\n### Page Structure (Lines 1-2418)\n\n**Template Inheritance (Line 1):**\n```jinja\n{% extends \"_base.html\" %}\n```\n\n**External Dependencies (Lines 6-7):**\n- Mermaid v11: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.min.js`\n- Marked v15: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@15/marked.min.js`\n- Custom CSS: `/static/arch-chat.css`\n\n---\n\n### A. Diagram Rendering System\n\n#### Mermaid Initialization (Lines 1224-1238)\n\n```javascript\nmermaid.initialize({\n    startOnLoad: false,\n    theme: 'dark',\n    themeVariables: {\n        darkMode: true,\n        background: '#0f172a',\n        primaryColor: '#1e3a5f',\n        // ... 7 more color variables\n    }\n});\n```\n\n**Theme Toggle Support (Lines 1240-1261):**\n- Light theme variables defined at lines 1240-1249\n- Dark theme variables defined at lines 1251-1261\n- Theme toggle buttons in diagram headers (lines 1016-1023)\n\n#### Diagram Loading Flow (Lines 1270-1286)\n\n**Entry Point:** `loadDiagrams()` function\n1. Iterates through `DIAGRAMS` array (from server-side template variable)\n2. Fetches each diagram file via API: `/api/projects/{PROJECT_ID}/features/{FEATURE_NAME}/arch/{diagram.file}`\n3. Calls `renderDiagramContent()` for each file\n4. Initializes pan/zoom viewport\n\n#### Rendering Dispatch (Lines 1288-1311)\n\n**Function:** `renderDiagramContent(el, filename, content, idx)`\n\n**Mermaid Path (Lines 1289-1307):**\n- Checks `filename.endsWith('.mmd')` (line 1289)\n- Calls `mermaid.render(id, content)` at line 1292\n- Returns `{ svg }` object, injected via `el.innerHTML = svg` (line 1293)\n- Attaches click handlers to `.node` elements for selection (lines 1295-1302)\n- Reapplies existing selections (line 1304)\n- Error handling: displays parse error message (lines 1305-1307)\n\n**Fallback Path (Lines 1308-1310):**\n- Non-Mermaid files rendered as escaped plain text in `<pre>` tag\n\n**No Draw.io Renderer:** Despite schema supporting `type: \"drawio\"`, there's no dedicated Draw.io rendering logic. Draw.io files would display as escaped XML via the fallback path.\n\n---\n\n### B. Interactive Features\n\n#### Pan & Zoom (Lines 1323-1375)\n\n**Initialization:** `initViewport(idx)` sets up per-diagram viewport state at line 1326:\n```javascript\nviewportState[idx] = { scale: 1, panX: 0, panY: 0, dragging: false, startX: 0, startY: 0 };\n```\n\n**Event Handlers:**\n- **Wheel:** Zoom in/out on scroll (lines 1327-1331)\n- **Mousedown:** Start drag operation (lines 1332-1339)\n- **Mousemove:** Pan diagram while dragging (lines 1340-1346)\n- **Mouseup/Mouseleave:** Stop dragging (lines 1347-1353)\n\n**Transform Application (Lines 1356-1361):**\n```javascript\nvp.style.transform = `translate(${st.panX}px, ${st.panY}px) scale(${st.scale})`;\n```\n\n**Zoom Controls (Lines 1033-1041):**\n- Zoom out button: `zoomDiagram(idx, -0.2)` (line 1034)\n- Reset button: `resetZoom(idx)` (line 1035)\n- Zoom in button: `zoomDiagram(idx, 0.2)` (line 1036)\n- Expand button: Links to full-page view `/project/{id}/arch/{feature}/diagram/{file}` (lines 1037-1040)\n\n#### Element Selection (Lines 1629-1726)\n\n**Node Click Handler (Lines 1295-1302):**\n- Attached to every `.node` element in rendered SVG\n- Calls `toggleElementSelection(filename, nodeId, node)` on click\n- Stops propagation to prevent card-level events\n\n**Node ID Extraction (Lines 1631-1641):**\n- **Mermaid v11 pattern:** Matches `flowchart-NodeId-123` format (line 1633)\n- **Fallback 1:** Splits on hyphens, takes all but last part (line 1636)\n- **Fallback 2:** Uses node's text content (line 1639)\n\n**Selection State (Lines 1643-1664):**\n- Stored in `selectedElements` Map: `filename -> Set<nodeId>`\n- Toggles `.node-selected` CSS class on SVG element (lines 1651, 1656)\n- Auto-attaches diagram if not already attached (lines 1658-1661)\n- Updates UI bar showing selected elements (line 1663)\n\n**Connection Extraction (Lines 1666-1678):**\n`getNodeConnections(filename, nodeId)` parses diagram source:\n- Splits content by lines\n- Matches lines containing nodeId AND arrow patterns `[-=.]+>` or `[-=.]+\\|` (line 1673)\n- Returns array of connection lines for context\n\n**Selection Persistence (Lines 1680-1689):**\n`reapplySelections(el, filename)` called after diagram re-render to restore `.node-selected` classes\n\n---\n\n### C. Chat Panel Implementation\n\n#### Panel Structure (Lines 1054-1201)\n\n**Floating Panel (Lines 1146-176):**\n- Fixed position: `bottom: 24px, right: 24px`\n- Dimensions: `width: 480px`, `height: 60vh`\n- Resizable: `resize: both` CSS property\n- Draggable: Via header when unlocked (lines 1400-1462)\n- Lock toggle: Controls draggability and resize (lines 1518-1539)\n\n**Header Components (Lines 1056-1080):**\n- Session dropdown (lines 1058-1061)\n- Window size controls (S/M/L buttons, lines 1064-1068)\n- Lock/unlock button (line 1069-1072)\n- New session button (line 1073-1075)\n- Close button (lines 1076-1078)\n\n**Configuration Bars:**\n- **Provider/Model selects** (lines 1097-1110): Rendered if `providers` length > 1\n- **Service status indicators** (lines 1113-1122): Shows online/offline dots for Claude/OpenCode\n- **Attached context bar** (lines 1125-1128): Lists attached diagram files\n- **Selected elements bar** (lines 1130-1134): Shows selected nodes with \"Clear\" button\n\n#### Session Management (Lines 1828-2008)\n\n**Session Storage:** Files at `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json` (per `chat_session_service.py` lines 14, 26)\n\n**Load Sessions (Lines 1830-1844):**\n- Fetches `/api/projects/{PROJECT_ID}/chat/sessions?feature={FEATURE_NAME}` (line 1832)\n- Auto-selects most recent if no current session (lines 1838-1840)\n\n**Session Rendering (Lines 1846-1870):**\n- Displays session name, message count, updated date\n- Shows delete button on hover\n- Active session highlighted with `.active` class\n\n**Load Session (Lines 1905-1952):**\n- Cancels previous session's chat if switching (lines 1907-1909)\n- Fetches session data (line 1911)\n- Updates header name (line 1919)\n- Syncs provider/model dropdowns (lines 1922-1933)\n- Renders message history (lines 1942-1944)\n- Connects SSE stream (line 1947)\n\n#### Messaging Flow (Lines 2074-2278)\n\n**Send Chat (Lines 2219-2278):**\n\n1. **Validation:** Checks message not empty and session exists (lines 2220-2222)\n2. **UI Update:** Clears input, appends user message bubble (lines 2224-2226), shows thinking indicator (line 2229)\n3. **Context Assembly (lines 2232-2250):**\n   - Iterates attached diagrams\n   - Includes full diagram content\n   - For selected elements: adds node ID + connections extracted via `getNodeConnections()`\n   - Format: `--- SELECTED ELEMENTS in {file} ---\\nFocus: {nodeId}\\nConnections:\\n  {line}\\n--- END SELECTED ---`\n4. **API Call:** POST to `/api/projects/{PROJECT_ID}/chat/sessions/{SESSION_ID}/messages` (line 2255)\n5. **Request Body (lines 2258-2263):**\n   ```json\n   {\n       \"message\": \"user's text\",\n       \"context\": \"diagram content + selections\",\n       \"provider\": \"claude\",\n       \"model\": \"sonnet\"\n   }\n   ```\n6. **Streaming:** Response arrives via SSE connection (line 2272)\n\n**SSE Connection (Lines 2021-2062):**\n\n**Event Types Handled:**\n- `token` (lines 2026-2029): Appends streaming text token-by-token\n- `message_done` (lines 2031-2034): Finalizes message with full content\n- `chat_error` (lines 2036-2040): Displays error message\n- `diagram_changed` (lines 2042-2045): Updates diagram in place\n- `diagram_added` (lines 2047-2050): Adds new diagram card\n- `diagram_removed` (lines 2052-2055): Removes diagram card\n- `ping` (line 2057): Keepalive, no-op\n\n**Streaming Message Rendering (Lines 2144-2183):**\n- Creates `.chat-msg.assistant` div with avatar on first token (lines 2154-2162)\n- Accumulates text in `streamingText` variable (line 2166)\n- Re-renders with `marked.parse(streamingText)` after each token (line 2170)\n- Auto-scrolls to bottom (line 2172)\n- Finalizes on `message_done` event (lines 2175-2183)\n\n---\n\n### D. Live Diagram Updates (Lines 2283-2369)\n\n**Update Existing Diagram (Lines 2284-2302):**\n- Finds diagram by filename in `DIAGRAMS` array (line 2288)\n- Adds `.diagram-updating` class for visual feedback (lines 2296-2299)\n- Re-renders via `renderDiagramContent()` (line 2301)\n\n**Add New Diagram (Lines 2304-2356):**\n- Creates diagram object `{ file, name, category: 'architecture' }` (line 2311)\n- Appends to `DIAGRAMS` array (line 2312)\n- Builds HTML card with full structure (lines 2319-2346)\n- Renders content and initializes viewport (lines 2349-2351)\n- Flashes update animation (lines 2354-2355)\n\n**Remove Diagram (Lines 2358-2369):**\n- Fades out card with `opacity: 0.3` (line 2361)\n- Removes after 500ms (line 2362)\n- Cleans up state: `diagramContents`, `attachedDiagrams`, `selectedElements` (lines 2364-2366)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Backend Services\n\n### A. Progress Service: `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n\n**Read Manifest (Lines 50-63):**\n```python\ndef read_arch_manifest(project_path: str, feature_name: str) -> Optional[dict]:\n    arch_file = Path(project_path) / \".vista\" / \"features\" / feature_name / \"arch\" / \"_arch.json\"\n    if not arch_file.exists():\n        return None\n    try:\n        data = json.loads(arch_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        # Legacy format migration: bare list -> dict\n        if isinstance(data, list):\n            data = {\"feature\": feature_name, \"diagrams\": data}\n        return data\n    except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):\n        return None\n```\n\n**Read Diagram File (Lines 77-97):**\n\n**Path Traversal Protection (Lines 80-92):**\n1. Extracts filename only: `safe_name = Path(filename).name` (line 81)\n2. Rejects if mismatch or contains `..` (line 82)\n3. Constructs target path (line 86)\n4. Resolves and validates within `arch_dir`: `target.resolve().relative_to(arch_dir.resolve())` (line 90)\n5. Returns `None` on `ValueError` (line 92)\n\n---\n\n### B. Architecture Routes: `vista/server/routes/architecture.py`\n\n**API Endpoints:**\n\n1. **GET `/api/projects/{project_id}/features/{feature_name}/arch`** (lines 15-26)\n   - Returns `_arch.json` manifest\n   - Uses `ProgressService.read_arch_manifest()`\n\n2. **GET `/api/projects/{project_id}/features/{feature_name}/arch/{filename}`** (lines 29-48)\n   - Returns raw diagram file content\n   - Uses `ProgressService.read_arch_file()` with path traversal protection\n   - Content-Type: `text/plain` for `.mmd`, `application/xml` for `.drawio`\n\n**Page Routes:**\n\n3. **GET `/project/{project_id}/arch/{feature_name}`** (lines 51-66)\n   - Renders `architecture.html` template\n   - Template context: `{ project, feature_name, manifest, providers }`\n\n4. **GET `/project/{project_id}/arch/{feature_name}/diagram/{filename}`** (lines 69-91)\n   - Full-page diagram view\n   - Renders `diagram_expand.html` template\n   - Derives diagram name: `filename.rsplit('.', 1)[0].replace('-', ' ').title()` (line 82)\n\n---\n\n### C. Chat Session Service: `vista/server/services/chat_session_service.py`\n\n**Session Files (Lines 14, 21-26):**\n- Directory: `server/data/sessions/{project_id}/`\n- Filename: `{session_id}.json`\n\n**Create Session (Lines 28-46):**\n- Generates UUID session ID via `ChatSession.generate_id()` (line 38)\n- Default name: `\"New Chat\"` (line 42)\n- Saves to disk immediately (line 45)\n\n**List Sessions (Lines 48-65):**\n- Sorted by modified time descending: `sorted(..., key=lambda p: p.stat().st_mtime, reverse=True)` (line 57)\n- Optionally filters by `feature_name` (lines 60-61)\n- Returns summary dicts (line 62)\n\n**Add Message (Lines 82-96):**\n- Appends `ChatMessage` to session's `messages` array (lines 89-90)\n- Updates `updated_at` timestamp (line 91)\n- Auto-names session from first user message: `ChatSession.auto_name(content)` (lines 93-94)\n\n---\n\n### D. Chat Session Routes: `vista/server/routes/chat_sessions.py`\n\n**SSE Broadcasting (Lines 27-58):**\n\n**Subscriber Pattern:**\n- Global dict `_session_subscribers: dict[str, list[asyncio.Queue]]` (line 27)\n- `_subscribe()`: Creates queue, adds to session's subscriber list (lines 30-35)\n- `_unsubscribe()`: Removes queue, deletes session key if empty (lines 38-44)\n- `_broadcast()`: Sends message to all subscribers, removes dead queues (lines 47-58)\n\n**Send Message Endpoint (Lines 159-242):**\n\n**Flow:**\n1. **Validation:** Project, session, message checks (lines 162-171)\n2. **Provider/Model Selection:** Uses request override or session defaults (lines 174-181)\n3. **Save User Message:** Calls `ChatSessionService.add_message()` (lines 184-189)\n4. **Build Context:** Uses `ContextAssembler.build_system_prompt()` and `build_full_prompt()` (lines 198-208)\n5. **Backend Session Creation:** If first message, creates protocol-native session via `provider_router.create_backend_session()` (lines 216-230)\n6. **Async Streaming:** Launches `_stream_response_router()` task (lines 232-241)\n\n**Streaming Handler (Lines 250-313):**\n\n**Event Processing:**\n- `type: \"token\"` → Broadcast `event: token` to SSE (lines 269-277)\n- `type: \"done\"` → Save assistant message, broadcast `event: message_done` (lines 278-289)\n- `type: \"result\"` → Broadcast `event: result` (lines 290-297)\n- `type: \"error\"` → Broadcast `event: chat_error` (lines 298-305)\n\n**SSE Endpoint (Lines 351-399):**\n\n**Multi-Queue Merge (lines 363-377):**\n1. Subscribe to chat events: `_subscribe(session_id)` (line 363)\n2. Subscribe to diagram watcher: `diagram_watcher.subscribe(project_id, feature_name, arch_dir)` (lines 369-371)\n3. Merge both queues into one: `_forward_queue()` helper tasks (lines 377-378)\n\n**Generator (Lines 379-398):**\n- Waits for events with 30s timeout (line 384)\n- Sends `event: ping` on timeout (line 390)\n- Handles disconnection (line 381)\n- Cleanup: Cancels forwarders, unsubscribes from both sources (lines 394-397)\n\n---\n\n### E. Diagram Watcher: `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n\n**Filesystem Monitoring (Lines 1-268):**\n\n**Watchdog Integration (Lines 23-93):**\n- Uses `watchdog.observers.Observer` for native filesystem events\n- Event handler: `_DiagramEventHandler` processes `.mmd` and `.drawio` files (line 26)\n- Events: `on_created`, `on_modified`, `on_deleted` (lines 40-50)\n\n**Debouncing (Lines 52-68):**\n- 100ms debounce via `threading.Timer` (line 52)\n- Coalesces rapid file saves (common in editors that save on every keystroke)\n- Pending events stored in dict: `path -> (event_type, filename)` (line 34)\n- Flush timer restarts on each event (lines 57-60)\n\n**Event Broadcasting (Lines 69-85):**\n- Reads file content for `diagram_changed` and `diagram_added` (line 75)\n- Schedules broadcast to async event loop via `loop.call_soon_threadsafe()` (lines 206-210)\n- Updates manifest on add/remove events (lines 84-85)\n\n**Manifest Auto-Update (Lines 232-256):**\n`_update_manifest_sync(arch_dir)`:\n1. Scans directory for `.mmd` and `.drawio` files (line 238)\n2. Detects Mermaid diagram type from first line (lines 102-118)\n3. Builds manifest entry: `{ name, file, type, diagramType }` (lines 241-247)\n4. Writes to `_arch.json` (lines 252-254)\n\n**Observer Lifecycle (Lines 176-202):**\n- Starts on first subscriber: `observer.start()` at line 186\n- Stops when last subscriber unsubscribes (lines 192-202)\n- Daemon thread (line 185) ensures cleanup on shutdown\n\n---\n\n## 4. FastAPI Application: `vista/server/app.py`\n\n**Router Registration (Lines 56-85):**\n\nAll routers included:\n- `architecture` (line 64, 79)\n- `chat_sessions` (line 65, 80)\n- `projects`, `loops`, `stream`, `plans`, `providers`, `shutdown`, `ralph`, `ralph_settings`, `sandbox`, `service_status`, `export` (lines 58-71, 73-85)\n\n**Static Files (Lines 49-51):**\n- Mounted at `/static` route\n- Directory: `vista/server/views/static/`\n\n---\n\n## 5. Settings Files\n\n### User Settings: `~/.vista/settings.json`\n\n**Structure (Lines 1-65):**\n\n**Server Config (Lines 2-7):**\n```json\n\"server\": {\n  \"auto_start\": true,\n  \"auto_open_browser\": true,\n  \"host\": \"127.0.0.1\",\n  \"port\": 3456\n}\n```\n\n**Providers (Lines 8-17):**\n```json\n\"providers\": {\n  \"claude\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"Claude Code\" },\n  \"opencode\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"OpenCode\" }\n}\n```\n\n**Ralph Settings (Lines 18-60):**\n- Defaults: `provider: \"claude\"`, `model: \"sonnet\"`, `iterations: 3` (lines 19-23)\n- Summarizer: `provider: \"claude\"`, `model: \"haiku\"` (lines 24-27)\n- Per-provider model metadata (lines 28-59)\n\n**Tools (Lines 61-64):**\n```json\n\"tools\": {\n  \"teams\": { \"enabled\": true },\n  \"ralph\": { \"enabled\": true }\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** Both `~/.vista/settings.json` and `vista/settings.json` contain identical content. Per `CLAUDE.md` line 31, persistent settings are at `~/.vista/settings.json` with legacy fallback at `vista/settings.json`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Static Assets: `vista/server/views/static/`\n\n**Files:**\n1. `app.js` - General dashboard JavaScript\n2. `arch-chat.css` - Chat panel styles (787 lines)\n3. `arch-chat.js` - Reusable chat module (618 lines)\n4. `style.css` - Global styles\n\n### Shared Chat Module: `arch-chat.js`\n\n**Purpose:** Reusable chat implementation for both `architecture.html` and `diagram_expand.html`\n\n**API (Lines 10-612):**\n\n**Initialization (Lines 32-46):**\n```javascript\nArchChat.init({\n    projectId: '...',\n    featureName: '...',\n    providers: [...]\n});\n```\n\n**Key Methods:**\n- `togglePanel()` - Show/hide chat panel (lines 106-112)\n- `loadSessions()` - Fetch and render session list (lines 129-142)\n- `createNewSession()` - Create new chat session (lines 218-239)\n- `sendChat()` - Send message with context (lines 534-574)\n- `appendMessage(role, content, scroll)` - Render chat bubble (lines 420-452)\n- `connectSSE(sessionId)` - Establish SSE connection (lines 360-407)\n\n**Extensibility:**\n- `buildContext()` - Override in page-specific code to provide diagram context (line 545)\n- Callbacks: `onDiagramChanged()`, `onDiagramAdded()`, `onDiagramRemoved()` (lines 383-399)\n\n---\n\n## Key Data Flow Patterns\n\n### 1. Diagram Display Flow\n```\nBrowser → GET /project/{id}/arch/{feature}\n       → architecture.html renders\n       → JavaScript loadDiagrams()\n       → Fetches each file: GET /api/projects/{id}/features/{feature}/arch/{file}\n       → ProgressService.read_arch_file() (path traversal check)\n       → Returns content\n       → renderDiagramContent() dispatches:\n          - .mmd → mermaid.render() → SVG injection\n          - other → <pre> tag with escaped text\n```\n\n### 2. Chat Message Flow\n```\nUser types message → sendChat()\n                  → POST /api/projects/{id}/chat/sessions/{sid}/messages\n                     { message, context, provider, model }\n                  → chat_sessions.py::send_message()\n                  → ContextAssembler.build_full_prompt()\n                  → provider_router.create_backend_session() (if first message)\n                  → _stream_response_router() async task\n                  → provider_router.send_message() yields events\n                  → _broadcast() to SSE subscribers\n                  → EventSourceResponse at /stream endpoint\n                  → Browser receives SSE events\n                  → appendStreamToken() updates UI\n                  → message_done event finalizes\n```\n\n### 3. Live Diagram Update Flow\n```\nUser edits diagram file in filesystem\n       → Watchdog Observer detects filesystem event\n       → _DiagramEventHandler.on_modified()\n       → _debounced_notify() (100ms delay)\n       → _flush() reads file content\n       → watcher._schedule_broadcast() (cross-thread)\n       → loop.call_soon_threadsafe()\n       → _broadcast() to diagram queue\n       → Merged into SSE stream\n       → EventSource 'diagram_changed' event\n       → updateDiagram() re-renders\n       → Visual pulse animation\n```\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Points\n\n### Diagram Type Detection (diagram_watcher.py lines 102-118)\nDetects from first line: `graph`, `flowchart`, `sequence`, `class`, `state`, `er`, `gantt`, `pie`, etc.\n\n### Theme Configuration (architecture.html lines 1224-1261)\n- Dark theme (default): `background: #0f172a`, `primaryColor: #1e3a5f`\n- Light theme: `background: #ffffff`, `primaryColor: #dbeafe`\n\n### SSE Timeout (chat_sessions.py line 384)\n30-second keepalive ping interval\n\n### Debounce Delay (diagram_watcher.py line 52)\n100ms filesystem event coalescing\n\n### Queue Limits\n- Chat subscribers: `maxsize=500` (chat_sessions.py line 33)\n- Diagram subscribers: `maxsize=200` (diagram_watcher.py line 159)\n- Merged queue: `maxsize=500` (chat_sessions.py line 374)\n\n---\n\n## File References Summary\n\n| Component | File Path |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| Schema | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/templates/arch-schema.json` |\n| Main Template | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/views/architecture.html` |\n| Progress Service | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/services/progress_service.py` |\n| Architecture Routes | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/routes/architecture.py` |\n| FastAPI App | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/app.py` |\n| Chat Session Service | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/services/chat_session_service.py` |\n| Chat Routes | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/routes/chat_sessions.py` |\n| Diagram Watcher | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py` |\n| Settings | `C:/Users/Grove/.vista/settings.json` |\n| Static CSS | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` |\n| Static JS | `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.js` |"}],"totalDurationMs":165480,"totalTokens":83586,"totalToolUseCount":