{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DZFexq5xSGwKtmMJ7nsLW1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Hq9ZRFYGvAtNq8meApnTz5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/.vista/ralph/diagram-repr-spec-planning/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Multi-Format Diagram Support & Markdown Editing\n\n**Status:** PLANNING — New feature expansion for diagram_representations\n**Created:** 2026-02-15\n**Spec Source:** `domain-requirements.md` Expansion section (added 2026-02-15)\n**Parent Feature:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/`\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\nThe existing diagram_representations feature is largely delivered (Phases 1-4 complete, Phase 5 partial). The domain-requirements.md has been expanded with three new areas:\n\n1. **Multi-Format Rendering** — PlantUML (.puml), D2 (.d2), Graphviz (.dot), Markdown (.md)\n2. **Markdown Inline Editing** — View/edit toggle, save to disk via PUT API, cancel/discard\n3. **Manifest & Type System Updates** — Extended type enum, renderer dispatch, file extension mapping\n\nThis plan covers implementing these expansion requirements on top of the existing codebase.\n\n---\n\n## Current State Assessment\n\n### What Exists (Working)\n\n| Component | Status | Location |\n|-----------|--------|----------|\n| Mermaid rendering | Complete | `architecture.html:1289-1307` — `mermaid.render()` |\n| Renderer dispatch | Partial — only `.mmd` check + fallback `<pre>` | `architecture.html:1288-1311` |\n| `_arch.json` schema | `type` enum: `[\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]` only | `arch-schema.json:29` |\n| Diagram watcher | Watches `.mmd` and `.drawio` only | `diagram_watcher.py:26` — `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` |\n| Manifest auto-update | Detects diagram type for mermaid files only | `diagram_watcher.py:102-118` |\n| API: GET manifest | Complete | `architecture.py:15-26` |\n| API: GET file | Complete (read-only, text/plain or application/xml) | `architecture.py:29-48` |\n| API: PUT file | **Does not exist** | Needed for markdown save |\n| Path traversal protection | Complete | `progress_service.py:80-92` |\n| Pan/zoom per diagram | Complete | `architecture.html:1323-1375` |\n| Settings file | No `plantuml_server_url` field | `~/.vista/settings.json` |\n\n### What Needs to Change\n\n1. **arch-schema.json** — Extend `type` enum from 2 to 6 values\n2. **diagram_watcher.py** — Extend `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` and `_detect_diagram_type()` for new formats\n3. **progress_service.py** — Add `write_arch_file()` method for markdown save\n4. **architecture.py** — Add `PUT` endpoint, update content-type mapping for new extensions\n5. **architecture.html** — Add 4 new renderers + markdown edit mode\n6. **Settings** — Add `plantuml_server_url` default\n7. **Tests** — Cover all new renderers, PUT endpoint, security\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Schema & Backend Foundation\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — All other phases depend on this\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n\n### 1.1 Extend arch-schema.json Type Enum\n\n**File:** `vista/templates/arch-schema.json`\n\nChange line 29:\n```json\n\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]\n```\nTo:\n```json\n\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\", \"plantuml\", \"d2\", \"graphviz\", \"markdown\"]\n```\n\nNo other schema changes needed — `diagramType` enum already has `\"custom\"` as a catch-all for non-Mermaid diagrams. The `category` field is already optional with `architecture` and `tdd` values.\n\n### 1.2 Add write_arch_file() to ProgressService\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n\nAdd new static method after `read_arch_file()`:\n\n```python\n@staticmethod\ndef write_arch_file(project_path: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, content: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Write content to a diagram file in arch/ with path traversal prevention.\n\n    Only allows writing to files with extensions: .md\n    Returns True on success, False on validation failure.\n    \"\"\"\n    WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS = {\".md\"}\n\n    safe_name = Path(filename).name\n    if safe_name != filename or \"..\" in filename:\n        return False\n\n    if Path(safe_name).suffix not in WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS:\n        return False\n\n    arch_dir = Path(project_path) / \".vista\" / \"features\" / feature_name / \"arch\"\n    target = arch_dir / safe_name\n\n    try:\n        target.resolve().relative_to(arch_dir.resolve())\n    except ValueError:\n        return False\n\n    if not arch_dir.exists():\n        return False\n\n    target.write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return True\n```\n\n**Key decisions:**\n- **Writable extensions restricted to `.md` only** — Diagram files (.mmd, .puml, .d2, .dot, .drawio) are NOT writable through this API. Only markdown documentation files are editable inline.\n- **Same path traversal protection** as `read_arch_file()`.\n- **File must be in an existing arch/ directory** — won't create directories.\n\n### 1.3 Add PUT Endpoint for File Writing\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py`\n\nAdd new route:\n\n```python\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nclass FileContent(BaseModel):\n    content: str\n\n@router.put(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/features/{feature_name}/arch/{filename}\")\nasync def put_arch_file(project_id: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, body: FileContent):\n    \"\"\"Write content to a markdown file in arch/.\"\"\"\n    project = ProjectService.get_by_id(project_id)\n    if not project:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Project not found\")\n\n    success = ProgressService.write_arch_file(project.path, feature_name, filename, body.content)\n    if not success:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Cannot write to this file\")\n\n    return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"filename\": filename}\n```\n\n### 1.4 Update Content-Type Mapping in GET Endpoint\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` — `get_arch_file()` function\n\nUpdate the content-type section (lines 41-46):\n\n```python\next = filename.rsplit(\".\", 1)[-1] if \".\" in filename else \"\"\nCONTENT_TYPES = {\n    \"mmd\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"drawio\": \"application/xml\",\n    \"puml\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"d2\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"dot\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"md\": \"text/markdown\",\n}\nmedia_type = CONTENT_TYPES.get(ext, \"text/plain\")\n```\n\n### 1.5 Add PlantUML Server URL to Settings\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/settings_service.py` (or wherever defaults are defined)\n\nAdd default `plantuml_server_url` to settings schema:\n```json\n\"plantuml_server_url\": \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\"\n```\n\n**Also update:** `~/.vista/settings.json` default initialization if a settings template exists.\n\n**Server-side API:** Add a `GET /api/settings/plantuml-server` endpoint (or include in existing settings response) so the frontend can discover the configured PlantUML server URL.\n\n### 1.6 Extend Diagram Watcher Extensions\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n\nUpdate `_DiagramEventHandler` class:\n\n```python\nWATCH_EXTENSIONS = {\".mmd\", \".drawio\", \".puml\", \".d2\", \".dot\", \".md\"}\n```\n\nUpdate `_detect_diagram_type()` to return type based on extension (not just mermaid content parsing):\n\n```python\ndef _detect_file_type(path: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Detect diagram type from file extension.\"\"\"\n    EXT_TO_TYPE = {\n        \".mmd\": \"mermaid\",\n        \".drawio\": \"drawio\",\n        \".puml\": \"plantuml\",\n        \".d2\": \"d2\",\n        \".dot\": \"graphviz\",\n        \".md\": \"markdown\",\n    }\n    return EXT_TO_TYPE.get(path.suffix.lower(), \"mermaid\")\n```\n\nUpdate `_update_manifest_sync()` to use `_detect_file_type()` for the `type` field and retain `_detect_diagram_type()` for the `diagramType` field (mermaid subtypes). For non-mermaid formats, set `diagramType: \"custom\"`.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 1)\n\n- [ ] `arch-schema.json` validates manifests with all 6 type values\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` writes `.md` files successfully\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns 400 for non-`.md` files\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` blocks path traversal attempts\n- [ ] `GET /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns correct Content-Type for all 6 extensions\n- [ ] Diagram watcher detects changes in all 6 file types\n- [ ] Manifest auto-update correctly identifies file types by extension\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Client-Side Renderer Infrastructure\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Core rendering dispatch\n**Depends on:** Phase 1\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n\n### 2.1 Refactor Renderer Dispatch\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\nCurrently, `renderDiagramContent()` (line 1288) checks `filename.endsWith('.mmd')` and falls back to `<pre>`. Refactor to a renderer map pattern:\n\n```javascript\nconst RENDERERS = {\n    mermaid:  renderMermaid,\n    plantuml: renderPlantUML,\n    d2:       renderD2,\n    graphviz: renderGraphviz,\n    drawio:   renderDrawio,\n    markdown: renderMarkdown,\n};\n\nfunction renderDiagramContent(el, filename, content, idx, diagramType) {\n    // diagramType is the 'type' field from manifest (mermaid, plantuml, etc.)\n    // NOT diagramType (flowchart, sequence, etc.)\n    const renderer = RENDERERS[diagramType];\n    if (renderer) {\n        return renderer(el, content, idx, filename);\n    }\n    // Unknown type fallback\n    el.innerHTML = `<pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n}\n```\n\n**Change needed:** The template must pass the manifest `type` field to `renderDiagramContent()`. Currently, `loadDiagrams()` only passes filename/content/idx. Update to also pass `diagram.type` from the manifest `DIAGRAMS` array.\n\n### 2.2 Mermaid Renderer (Existing — No Changes)\n\nStays as-is: `mermaid.render(id, content)` → SVG injection → click handlers for element selection.\n\n### 2.3 PlantUML Renderer\n\n**Dependencies:** `plantuml-encoder` library (CDN or bundled)\n\n**Rendering flow:**\n1. Encode PlantUML source to deflate+base64 using `plantuml-encoder` algorithm\n2. Construct URL: `${PLANTUML_SERVER_URL}/svg/${encoded}`\n3. Fetch SVG from PlantUML server\n4. Inject SVG into card container\n\n**Library loading:** CDN — `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js`\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nasync function renderPlantUML(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const encoded = plantumlEncoder.encode(content);\n        const serverUrl = PLANTUML_SERVER_URL;  // From server template var or settings API\n        const svgUrl = `${serverUrl}/svg/${encoded}`;\n        const resp = await fetch(svgUrl);\n        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`PlantUML server error: ${resp.status}`);\n        const svg = await resp.text();\n        el.innerHTML = svg;\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>PlantUML render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Error handling:**\n- Server unreachable → Show error + raw source as fallback\n- Invalid syntax → PlantUML server returns error image; detect via content-type or error body\n\n**Template variable:** Pass `PLANTUML_SERVER_URL` from server context (read from settings).\n\n### 2.4 D2 Renderer\n\n**Dependencies:** `@terrastruct/d2` WASM package\n\n**Loading strategy:** Lazy-load — only fetch WASM when a D2 diagram appears.\n\n**Implementation approach:**\n```javascript\nlet d2Module = null;\n\nasync function loadD2() {\n    if (d2Module) return d2Module;\n    // Dynamic import from CDN\n    d2Module = await import('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@anthropic-ai/d2-wasm/...');\n    return d2Module;\n}\n\nasync function renderD2(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const d2 = await loadD2();\n        const svg = await d2.compile(content, { layout: 'dagre' });\n        el.innerHTML = svg;\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>D2 render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** D2 WASM availability needs verification. If `@terrastruct/d2` doesn't provide a browser-compatible WASM, an alternative approach is needed:\n- **Fallback option A:** Server-side rendering via `d2` CLI (similar to how PlantUML uses a server)\n- **Fallback option B:** Use a simpler D2 rendering library if available\n- **Minimum viable:** Show raw D2 source with syntax highlighting as placeholder, with a note that D2 rendering requires server-side support\n\n### 2.5 Graphviz Renderer\n\n**Dependencies:** `@viz-js/viz` WASM package\n\n**Loading strategy:** Lazy-load — only fetch WASM when a Graphviz diagram appears.\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nlet vizInstance = null;\n\nasync function loadViz() {\n    if (vizInstance) return vizInstance;\n    const { instance } = await import('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@viz-js/viz/...');\n    vizInstance = await instance();\n    return vizInstance;\n}\n\nasync function renderGraphviz(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const viz = await loadViz();\n        const svg = viz.renderSVGElement(content, { engine: 'dot' });\n        el.innerHTML = '';\n        el.appendChild(svg);\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>Graphviz render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Engine selection:** Default to `dot` layout engine. Could expose engine selection per-diagram via a `layoutEngine` field in manifest (future enhancement — not in scope now).\n\n### 2.6 Draw.io Renderer (Existing Gap — Implement Now)\n\n**Current state:** Falls through to `<pre>` tag with escaped XML content.\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nfunction renderDrawio(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        // Use Draw.io's public viewer with inline XML\n        const encoded = encodeURIComponent(content);\n        const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');\n        iframe.src = `https://viewer.diagrams.net/?highlight=0000ff&nav=1&title=${filename}#R${encoded}`;\n        iframe.style.width = '100%';\n        iframe.style.height = '500px';\n        iframe.style.border = 'none';\n        iframe.setAttribute('sandbox', 'allow-scripts allow-same-origin');\n        el.innerHTML = '';\n        el.appendChild(iframe);\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>Draw.io render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Alternative:** For large `.drawio` files, the URL-encoded approach may exceed URL limits. Use `postMessage` API instead:\n1. Create iframe pointing to `https://viewer.diagrams.net/`\n2. Send diagram XML via `iframe.contentWindow.postMessage()` after iframe loads\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 2)\n\n- [ ] Mermaid diagrams continue to render correctly (no regression)\n- [ ] PlantUML diagrams render as SVG via server fetch\n- [ ] D2 diagrams render via WASM (or show fallback with raw source)\n- [ ] Graphviz diagrams render via `@viz-js/viz` WASM\n- [ ] Draw.io diagrams render in iframe (not raw XML)\n- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML\n- [ ] Each renderer shows error + raw source on failure\n- [ ] WASM modules load lazily (only when diagram type appears on page)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Markdown Renderer & Inline Editor\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Key new user interaction\n**Depends on:** Phase 1 (PUT endpoint), Phase 2 (renderer infrastructure)\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium-High\n\n### 3.1 Markdown Renderer\n\n**Library:** `marked.js` — already loaded in architecture.html (line 7, used for chat streaming).\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nfunction renderMarkdown(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const html = marked.parse(content);\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"markdown-content\">${html}</div>`;\n        // Store original content for edit mode\n        el.dataset.rawContent = content;\n        el.dataset.filename = filename;\n        el.dataset.idx = idx;\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3.2 Edit Button on Markdown Cards\n\nFor diagram cards where `type === \"markdown\"`, add a pencil icon button in the card header (alongside existing zoom controls).\n\n**Placement:** In the diagram card header template (around line 1016-1041 in architecture.html), conditionally add:\n\n```html\n{% if diagram.type == 'markdown' %}\n<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(idx)\" title=\"Edit markdown\">\n    ✎\n</button>\n{% endif %}\n```\n\n**Note:** Since diagrams are rendered client-side from the DIAGRAMS array, the edit button must be added in JavaScript during card construction, not in Jinja2. Check the type from the manifest entry.\n\n### 3.3 Edit Mode State Machine\n\n**States:** `view` → `editing` → `saving` → `view`\n\n```javascript\nconst markdownEditState = {};  // idx -> { editing: bool, saving: bool, originalContent: string }\n\nfunction toggleMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx] || { editing: false };\n\n    if (state.editing) {\n        cancelMarkdownEdit(idx);\n    } else {\n        enterMarkdownEdit(idx);\n    }\n}\n\nfunction enterMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n    const content = el.dataset.rawContent || diagramContents[DIAGRAMS[idx].file];\n\n    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: true, saving: false, originalContent: content };\n\n    el.innerHTML = `\n        <div class=\"md-editor-container\">\n            <div class=\"md-editor-toolbar\">\n                <button class=\"md-save-btn\" onclick=\"saveMarkdown(${idx})\" title=\"Save\">✓ Save</button>\n                <button class=\"md-cancel-btn\" onclick=\"cancelMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Cancel\">✕ Cancel</button>\n                <span class=\"md-save-indicator\" id=\"md-indicator-${idx}\"></span>\n            </div>\n            <textarea class=\"md-editor\" id=\"md-textarea-${idx}\" spellcheck=\"false\">${escapeHtml(content)}</textarea>\n        </div>\n    `;\n\n    // Focus and auto-resize\n    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n    textarea.focus();\n    autoResizeTextarea(textarea);\n    textarea.addEventListener('input', () => autoResizeTextarea(textarea));\n\n    // Update card header button state\n    updateEditButton(idx, true);\n}\n\nfunction cancelMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n    if (!state) return;\n\n    // Re-render the markdown view\n    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n    renderMarkdown(el, state.originalContent, idx, DIAGRAMS[idx].file);\n\n    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n    updateEditButton(idx, false);\n}\n\nasync function saveMarkdown(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n    if (!state || state.saving) return;\n\n    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n    const newContent = textarea.value;\n    const filename = DIAGRAMS[idx].file;\n    const indicator = document.getElementById(`md-indicator-${idx}`);\n\n    state.saving = true;\n    indicator.textContent = 'Saving...';\n    indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saving';\n\n    try {\n        const resp = await fetch(\n            `/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${filename}`,\n            {\n                method: 'PUT',\n                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n                body: JSON.stringify({ content: newContent }),\n            }\n        );\n\n        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`Save failed: ${resp.status}`);\n\n        indicator.textContent = 'Saved!';\n        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saved';\n\n        // Update stored content\n        diagramContents[filename] = newContent;\n\n        // Return to view mode after brief success indicator\n        setTimeout(() => {\n            const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n            renderMarkdown(el, newContent, idx, filename);\n            markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n            updateEditButton(idx, false);\n        }, 800);\n\n    } catch (err) {\n        indicator.textContent = `Error: ${err.message}`;\n        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator error';\n        state.saving = false;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3.4 Editor Styles\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` (or inline in architecture.html)\n\n```css\n.md-editor-container {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    height: 100%;\n    min-height: 200px;\n}\n\n.md-editor-toolbar {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 8px;\n    padding: 8px 12px;\n    background: var(--surface-2);\n    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n}\n\n.md-editor {\n    flex: 1;\n    resize: vertical;\n    min-height: 200px;\n    padding: 16px;\n    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    background: var(--surface-1);\n    color: var(--text-primary);\n    border: none;\n    outline: none;\n}\n\n.md-save-btn { color: #4ade80; }\n.md-cancel-btn { color: #f87171; }\n.md-save-indicator.saving { color: #facc15; }\n.md-save-indicator.saved { color: #4ade80; }\n.md-save-indicator.error { color: #f87171; }\n\n.markdown-content {\n    padding: 16px;\n    line-height: 1.7;\n}\n.markdown-content h1, .markdown-content h2, .markdown-content h3 {\n    margin-top: 1.5em;\n    margin-bottom: 0.5em;\n}\n.markdown-content pre {\n    background: var(--surface-2);\n    padding: 12px;\n    border-radius: 6px;\n    overflow-x: auto;\n}\n.markdown-content code {\n    background: var(--surface-2);\n    padding: 2px 6px;\n    border-radius: 3px;\n    font-size: 0.9em;\n}\n.markdown-content table {\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    width: 100%;\n}\n.markdown-content th, .markdown-content td {\n    border: 1px solid var(--border);\n    padding: 8px 12px;\n    text-align: left;\n}\n```\n\n### 3.5 Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+S` / `Cmd+S` in edit mode → Save\n- `Escape` in edit mode → Cancel\n\n```javascript\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n    // Find any active markdown editor\n    for (const [idx, state] of Object.entries(markdownEditState)) {\n        if (state.editing) {\n            if ((e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) && e.key === 's') {\n                e.preventDefault();\n                saveMarkdown(parseInt(idx));\n            } else if (e.key === 'Escape') {\n                e.preventDefault();\n                cancelMarkdownEdit(parseInt(idx));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n});\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 3)\n\n- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML with GFM support (tables, code blocks, task lists)\n- [ ] Edit button appears only on markdown-type diagram cards\n- [ ] Clicking edit switches to textarea with raw content\n- [ ] Save writes content to disk via PUT API and returns to rendered view\n- [ ] Cancel discards changes and returns to rendered view\n- [ ] Save indicator shows progress (saving → saved → hidden)\n- [ ] Save failure shows error message\n- [ ] Ctrl+S saves, Escape cancels\n- [ ] Content stored in `diagramContents` is updated after successful save\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Template & Watcher Integration\n\n**Priority:** MEDIUM\n**Depends on:** Phases 1-3\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low-Medium\n\n### 4.1 Pass Manifest Type to Renderers\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\nUpdate `loadDiagrams()` to pass the manifest `type` field:\n\n```javascript\nasync function loadDiagrams() {\n    for (let i = 0; i < DIAGRAMS.length; i++) {\n        const diagram = DIAGRAMS[i];\n        const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${diagram.file}`);\n        const content = await resp.text();\n        diagramContents[diagram.file] = content;\n\n        const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${i}`);\n        renderDiagramContent(el, diagram.file, content, i, diagram.type);  // Pass type!\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 4.2 Conditionally Show Edit Button in Card Header\n\nWhen building diagram cards (JavaScript, not Jinja2), check the diagram type:\n\n```javascript\nfunction buildDiagramCard(diagram, idx) {\n    // ... existing card structure ...\n\n    const editButton = diagram.type === 'markdown'\n        ? `<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Edit\">✎</button>`\n        : '';\n\n    // Insert into card header alongside zoom controls\n}\n```\n\n### 4.3 Update Diagram Watcher Manifest Auto-Update\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n\nThe `_update_manifest_sync()` function currently scans for `.mmd` and `.drawio` only. Update to scan all supported extensions and set the `type` field correctly:\n\n```python\nEXT_TO_TYPE = {\n    \".mmd\": \"mermaid\",\n    \".drawio\": \"drawio\",\n    \".puml\": \"plantuml\",\n    \".d2\": \"d2\",\n    \".dot\": \"graphviz\",\n    \".md\": \"markdown\",\n}\n\n# In _update_manifest_sync():\nfor f in sorted(arch_dir.iterdir()):\n    if f.suffix in EXT_TO_TYPE and not f.name.startswith(\"_\"):\n        file_type = EXT_TO_TYPE[f.suffix]\n        diagram_type = _detect_diagram_type(f) if file_type == \"mermaid\" else \"custom\"\n        entry = {\n            \"name\": f.stem.replace(\"-\", \" \").replace(\"_\", \" \").title(),\n            \"file\": f.name,\n            \"type\": file_type,\n            \"diagramType\": diagram_type,\n            \"description\": f\"Auto-detected {file_type} diagram\",\n        }\n        diagrams.append(entry)\n```\n\n### 4.4 CDN Script Loading\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\nAdd CDN scripts in the `<head>` section. WASM-based renderers should lazy-load, but the encoder library can be loaded eagerly (small):\n\n```html\n<!-- PlantUML encoder (small, ~10KB) -->\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder@1.4.0/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js\"></script>\n\n<!-- D2 and Graphviz loaded lazily by their respective renderers -->\n```\n\nFor `@viz-js/viz`, the CDN approach:\n```html\n<!-- Loaded dynamically in renderGraphviz() -->\n<!-- https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@viz-js/viz@3/lib/viz-standalone.js -->\n```\n\n### 4.5 PlantUML Server URL Injection\n\nThe architecture page template needs to know the PlantUML server URL. Options:\n\n**Option A (recommended):** Pass from server context:\n```python\n# In architecture_viewer_page():\nfrom server.services.settings_service import get_settings\nsettings = get_settings()\nplantuml_url = settings.get(\"plantuml_server_url\", \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\")\n```\n\nAnd in the template:\n```html\n<script>\n    const PLANTUML_SERVER_URL = {{ plantuml_url | tojson }};\n</script>\n```\n\n**Option B:** Fetch from settings API client-side. Less efficient.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 4)\n\n- [ ] All 6 diagram types dispatch to their correct renderer\n- [ ] Edit button only appears on markdown cards\n- [ ] Watcher detects changes in all 6 file types\n- [ ] Manifest auto-update correctly assigns type from extension\n- [ ] PlantUML server URL passed from settings to frontend\n- [ ] CDN scripts loaded (eagerly for small libs, lazily for WASM)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Tests\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Must validate security and correctness\n**Depends on:** Phases 1-4\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n\n### 5.1 PUT Endpoint Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestArchWriteAPI:\n    def test_put_markdown_file_success(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT .md file writes content and returns 200.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_non_markdown_file_rejected(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT .mmd file returns 400.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_path_traversal_blocked(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT ../../evil.md returns 400.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_project_not_found(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT to nonexistent project returns 404.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_no_arch_directory(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT to feature without arch/ returns 400.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### 5.2 ProgressService Write Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestProgressServiceWrite:\n    def test_write_arch_file_md_success(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() writes .md content to arch/.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_mmd_rejected(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() rejects .mmd files.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_path_traversal(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() blocks ../evil path.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_no_arch_dir(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() returns False when arch/ doesn't exist.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### 5.3 Schema Validation Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestExtendedSchemaValidation:\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_plantuml_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_d2_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_graphviz_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_markdown_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_rejects_unknown_type(self):\n```\n\n### 5.4 Content-Type Tests\n\n```python\nclass TestContentTypes:\n    def test_get_puml_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_d2_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_dot_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_md_returns_text_markdown(self, api_env):\n```\n\n### 5.5 Diagram Watcher Extension Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestExtendedFileTypes:\n    def test_watches_puml_files(self):\n    def test_watches_d2_files(self):\n    def test_watches_dot_files(self):\n    def test_watches_md_files(self):\n    def test_manifest_update_assigns_correct_type(self):\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 5)\n\n- [ ] All PUT endpoint tests pass (including security: path traversal, extension whitelist)\n- [ ] All schema validation tests pass for 6 types\n- [ ] Content-type tests pass for all new extensions\n- [ ] Watcher tests pass for all 6 file types\n- [ ] No regressions in existing 139 tests\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Documentation & Skill Updates\n\n**Priority:** LOW\n**Depends on:** All prior phases\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n\n### 6.1 Update Plan Skill SKILL.md\n\n**File:** `vista/skills/plan/SKILL.md`\n\nUpdate Step 3 (architecture generation) to mention all supported formats:\n- Default: Mermaid (.mmd) for all diagram types\n- Optional: PlantUML (.puml) for detailed UML class/sequence diagrams\n- Optional: D2 (.d2) for architecture diagrams with auto-layout\n- Optional: Graphviz (.dot) for dependency graphs\n- Optional: Markdown (.md) for prose documentation (design rationale, ADRs)\n\n### 6.2 Update Diagrams Skill\n\n**File:** `vista/skills/diagrams/SKILL.md` (if exists)\n\nDocument the expanded format support.\n\n### 6.3 Update arch-directory.md Spec\n\n**File:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/specs/arch-directory.md`\n\nUpdate to reflect the expanded type enum, new file extensions, and markdown editing capability.\n\n### 6.4 Update rendering-pipeline.md Spec\n\n**File:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/specs/rendering-pipeline.md`\n\nUpdate renderer table to include all 6 renderers.\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|-----------|--------|------------|\n| D2 WASM not available as browser-compatible package | Medium | Medium | Fall back to raw source display with syntax highlighting |\n| PlantUML server rate limiting | Low | Low | Self-hosted server option in settings |\n| @viz-js/viz WASM too large (>5MB) | Low | Medium | Lazy load only when Graphviz diagram appears |\n| Draw.io viewer URL encoding exceeds limits for large files | Medium | Medium | Use postMessage API instead of URL params |\n| Markdown editor unsaved changes lost on navigation | Low | Medium | Add `beforeunload` warning when editing |\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Order (Recommended)\n\n1. **Phase 1** — Backend foundation (schema, PUT endpoint, watcher extensions, settings)\n2. **Phase 2** — Renderer infrastructure (dispatch refactor + all 6 renderers)\n3. **Phase 3** — Markdown editor (edit mode, save/cancel, keyboard shortcuts)\n4. **Phase 4** — Template integration (type passing, CDN loading, watcher updates)\n5. **Phase 5** — Tests (PUT security, schema, content types, watcher)\n6. **Phase 6** — Documentation\n\n**Estimated total:** ~3-4 build iterations\n\n---\n\n## Files Summary\n\n### Files to Modify\n\n| File | Changes |\n|------|---------|\n| `vista/templates/arch-schema.json` | Extend `type` enum: add `plantuml`, `d2`, `graphviz`, `markdown` |\n| `vista/server/services/progress_service.py` | Add `write_arch_file()` method |\n| `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` | Add PUT endpoint, update content-type mapping |\n| `vista/server/views/architecture.html` | Refactor renderer dispatch, add 5 new renderers, add markdown editor |\n| `vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` | Add markdown editor styles |\n| `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py` | Extend `WATCH_EXTENSIONS`, update manifest type detection |\n| `vista/tests/test_architecture.py` | Add ~15 new tests for PUT, schema, content types |\n| `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py` | Add ~5 new tests for extended file types |\n\n### Files to Create\n\nNone — all changes are modifications to existing files.\n\n### Settings Changes\n\n| Setting | Value | Location |\n|---------|-------|----------|\n| `plantuml_server_url` | `\"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\"` | `~/.vista/settings.json` |\n\n---\n\n## Spec Versions\n\n| Spec File | Latest Changelog Date | Notes |\n|-----------|-----------------------|-------|\n| `specs/arch-directory.md` | 2026-02-15 | `diagramType` enum and category aligned with arch-schema.json |\n| `specs/rendering-pipeline.md` | 2026-02-15 | Draw.io status clarified, acceptance criteria updated |\n| `specs/chat-review.md` | 2026-02-15 | Protocol-native streaming alignment |\n| `specs/migration-cleanup.md` | 2026-02-15 | All acceptance criteria verified complete |\n| `domain-requirements.md` (Expansion) | 2026-02-15 | Multi-format diagrams, markdown editing, type system updates |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2910,"cache_read_input_tokens":87924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2910},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5856037d-22b3-414c-9b3a-aae0b154d72e","uuid":"0ea58a1c-a00d-49ca-8461-868bee283d5b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hq9ZRFYGvAtNq8meApnTz5","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/.vista/ralph/diagram-repr-spec-planning/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5856037d-22b3-414c-9b3a-aae0b154d72e","uuid":"37abce40-3539-41af-abe5-9e4b0bc8adfe","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/.vista/ralph/diagram-repr-spec-planning/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Multi-Format Diagram Support & Markdown Editing\n\n**Status:** PLANNING — New feature expansion for diagram_representations\n**Created:** 2026-02-15\n**Spec Source:** `domain-requirements.md` Expansion section (added 2026-02-15)\n**Parent Feature:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/`\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\nThe existing diagram_representations feature is largely delivered (Phases 1-4 complete, Phase 5 partial). The domain-requirements.md has been expanded with three new areas:\n\n1. **Multi-Format Rendering** — PlantUML (.puml), D2 (.d2), Graphviz (.dot), Markdown (.md)\n2. **Markdown Inline Editing** — View/edit toggle, save to disk via PUT API, cancel/discard\n3. **Manifest & Type System Updates** — Extended type enum, renderer dispatch, file extension mapping\n\nThis plan covers implementing these expansion requirements on top of the existing codebase.\n\n---\n\n## Current State Assessment\n\n### What Exists (Working)\n\n| Component | Status | Location |\n|-----------|--------|----------|\n| Mermaid rendering | Complete | `architecture.html:1289-1307` — `mermaid.render()` |\n| Renderer dispatch | Partial — only `.mmd` check + fallback `<pre>` | `architecture.html:1288-1311` |\n| `_arch.json` schema | `type` enum: `[\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]` only | `arch-schema.json:29` |\n| Diagram watcher | Watches `.mmd` and `.drawio` only | `diagram_watcher.py:26` — `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` |\n| Manifest auto-update | Detects diagram type for mermaid files only | `diagram_watcher.py:102-118` |\n| API: GET manifest | Complete | `architecture.py:15-26` |\n| API: GET file | Complete (read-only, text/plain or application/xml) | `architecture.py:29-48` |\n| API: PUT file | **Does not exist** | Needed for markdown save |\n| Path traversal protection | Complete | `progress_service.py:80-92` |\n| Pan/zoom per diagram | Complete | `architecture.html:1323-1375` |\n| Settings file | No `plantuml_server_url` field | `~/.vista/settings.json` |\n\n### What Needs to Change\n\n1. **arch-schema.json** — Extend `type` enum from 2 to 6 values\n2. **diagram_watcher.py** — Extend `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` and `_detect_diagram_type()` for new formats\n3. **progress_service.py** — Add `write_arch_file()` method for markdown save\n4. **architecture.py** — Add `PUT` endpoint, update content-type mapping for new extensions\n5. **architecture.html** — Add 4 new renderers + markdown edit mode\n6. **Settings** — Add `plantuml_server_url` default\n7. **Tests** — Cover all new renderers, PUT endpoint, security\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Schema & Backend Foundation\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — All other phases depend on this\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n\n### 1.1 Extend arch-schema.json Type Enum\n\n**File:** `vista/templates/arch-schema.json`\n\nChange line 29:\n```json\n\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]\n```\nTo:\n```json\n\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\", \"plantuml\", \"d2\", \"graphviz\", \"markdown\"]\n```\n\nNo other schema changes needed — `diagramType` enum already has `\"custom\"` as a catch-all for non-Mermaid diagrams. The `category` field is already optional with `architecture` and `tdd` values.\n\n### 1.2 Add write_arch_file() to ProgressService\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n\nAdd new static method after `read_arch_file()`:\n\n```python\n@staticmethod\ndef write_arch_file(project_path: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, content: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Write content to a diagram file in arch/ with path traversal prevention.\n\n    Only allows writing to files with extensions: .md\n    Returns True on success, False on validation failure.\n    \"\"\"\n    WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS = {\".md\"}\n\n    safe_name = Path(filename).name\n    if safe_name != filename or \"..\" in filename:\n        return False\n\n    if Path(safe_name).suffix not in WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS:\n        return False\n\n    arch_dir = Path(project_path) / \".vista\" / \"features\" / feature_name / \"arch\"\n    target = arch_dir / safe_name\n\n    try:\n        target.resolve().relative_to(arch_dir.resolve())\n    except ValueError:\n        return False\n\n    if not arch_dir.exists():\n        return False\n\n    target.write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return True\n```\n\n**Key decisions:**\n- **Writable extensions restricted to `.md` only** — Diagram files (.mmd, .puml, .d2, .dot, .drawio) are NOT writable through this API. Only markdown documentation files are editable inline.\n- **Same path traversal protection** as `read_arch_file()`.\n- **File must be in an existing arch/ directory** — won't create directories.\n\n### 1.3 Add PUT Endpoint for File Writing\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py`\n\nAdd new route:\n\n```python\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nclass FileContent(BaseModel):\n    content: str\n\n@router.put(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/features/{feature_name}/arch/{filename}\")\nasync def put_arch_file(project_id: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, body: FileContent):\n    \"\"\"Write content to a markdown file in arch/.\"\"\"\n    project = ProjectService.get_by_id(project_id)\n    if not project:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Project not found\")\n\n    success = ProgressService.write_arch_file(project.path, feature_name, filename, body.content)\n    if not success:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Cannot write to this file\")\n\n    return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"filename\": filename}\n```\n\n### 1.4 Update Content-Type Mapping in GET Endpoint\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` — `get_arch_file()` function\n\nUpdate the content-type section (lines 41-46):\n\n```python\next = filename.rsplit(\".\", 1)[-1] if \".\" in filename else \"\"\nCONTENT_TYPES = {\n    \"mmd\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"drawio\": \"application/xml\",\n    \"puml\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"d2\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"dot\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"md\": \"text/markdown\",\n}\nmedia_type = CONTENT_TYPES.get(ext, \"text/plain\")\n```\n\n### 1.5 Add PlantUML Server URL to Settings\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/settings_service.py` (or wherever defaults are defined)\n\nAdd default `plantuml_server_url` to settings schema:\n```json\n\"plantuml_server_url\": \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\"\n```\n\n**Also update:** `~/.vista/settings.json` default initialization if a settings template exists.\n\n**Server-side API:** Add a `GET /api/settings/plantuml-server` endpoint (or include in existing settings response) so the frontend can discover the configured PlantUML server URL.\n\n### 1.6 Extend Diagram Watcher Extensions\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n\nUpdate `_DiagramEventHandler` class:\n\n```python\nWATCH_EXTENSIONS = {\".mmd\", \".drawio\", \".puml\", \".d2\", \".dot\", \".md\"}\n```\n\nUpdate `_detect_diagram_type()` to return type based on extension (not just mermaid content parsing):\n\n```python\ndef _detect_file_type(path: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Detect diagram type from file extension.\"\"\"\n    EXT_TO_TYPE = {\n        \".mmd\": \"mermaid\",\n        \".drawio\": \"drawio\",\n        \".puml\": \"plantuml\",\n        \".d2\": \"d2\",\n        \".dot\": \"graphviz\",\n        \".md\": \"markdown\",\n    }\n    return EXT_TO_TYPE.get(path.suffix.lower(), \"mermaid\")\n```\n\nUpdate `_update_manifest_sync()` to use `_detect_file_type()` for the `type` field and retain `_detect_diagram_type()` for the `diagramType` field (mermaid subtypes). For non-mermaid formats, set `diagramType: \"custom\"`.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 1)\n\n- [ ] `arch-schema.json` validates manifests with all 6 type values\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` writes `.md` files successfully\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns 400 for non-`.md` files\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` blocks path traversal attempts\n- [ ] `GET /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns correct Content-Type for all 6 extensions\n- [ ] Diagram watcher detects changes in all 6 file types\n- [ ] Manifest auto-update correctly identifies file types by extension\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Client-Side Renderer Infrastructure\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Core rendering dispatch\n**Depends on:** Phase 1\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n\n### 2.1 Refactor Renderer Dispatch\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\nCurrently, `renderDiagramContent()` (line 1288) checks `filename.endsWith('.mmd')` and falls back to `<pre>`. Refactor to a renderer map pattern:\n\n```javascript\nconst RENDERERS = {\n    mermaid:  renderMermaid,\n    plantuml: renderPlantUML,\n    d2:       renderD2,\n    graphviz: renderGraphviz,\n    drawio:   renderDrawio,\n    markdown: renderMarkdown,\n};\n\nfunction renderDiagramContent(el, filename, content, idx, diagramType) {\n    // diagramType is the 'type' field from manifest (mermaid, plantuml, etc.)\n    // NOT diagramType (flowchart, sequence, etc.)\n    const renderer = RENDERERS[diagramType];\n    if (renderer) {\n        return renderer(el, content, idx, filename);\n    }\n    // Unknown type fallback\n    el.innerHTML = `<pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n}\n```\n\n**Change needed:** The template must pass the manifest `type` field to `renderDiagramContent()`. Currently, `loadDiagrams()` only passes filename/content/idx. Update to also pass `diagram.type` from the manifest `DIAGRAMS` array.\n\n### 2.2 Mermaid Renderer (Existing — No Changes)\n\nStays as-is: `mermaid.render(id, content)` → SVG injection → click handlers for element selection.\n\n### 2.3 PlantUML Renderer\n\n**Dependencies:** `plantuml-encoder` library (CDN or bundled)\n\n**Rendering flow:**\n1. Encode PlantUML source to deflate+base64 using `plantuml-encoder` algorithm\n2. Construct URL: `${PLANTUML_SERVER_URL}/svg/${encoded}`\n3. Fetch SVG from PlantUML server\n4. Inject SVG into card container\n\n**Library loading:** CDN — `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js`\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nasync function renderPlantUML(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const encoded = plantumlEncoder.encode(content);\n        const serverUrl = PLANTUML_SERVER_URL;  // From server template var or settings API\n        const svgUrl = `${serverUrl}/svg/${encoded}`;\n        const resp = await fetch(svgUrl);\n        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`PlantUML server error: ${resp.status}`);\n        const svg = await resp.text();\n        el.innerHTML = svg;\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>PlantUML render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Error handling:**\n- Server unreachable → Show error + raw source as fallback\n- Invalid syntax → PlantUML server returns error image; detect via content-type or error body\n\n**Template variable:** Pass `PLANTUML_SERVER_URL` from server context (read from settings).\n\n### 2.4 D2 Renderer\n\n**Dependencies:** `@terrastruct/d2` WASM package\n\n**Loading strategy:** Lazy-load — only fetch WASM when a D2 diagram appears.\n\n**Implementation approach:**\n```javascript\nlet d2Module = null;\n\nasync function loadD2() {\n    if (d2Module) return d2Module;\n    // Dynamic import from CDN\n    d2Module = await import('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@anthropic-ai/d2-wasm/...');\n    return d2Module;\n}\n\nasync function renderD2(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const d2 = await loadD2();\n        const svg = await d2.compile(content, { layout: 'dagre' });\n        el.innerHTML = svg;\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>D2 render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** D2 WASM availability needs verification. If `@terrastruct/d2` doesn't provide a browser-compatible WASM, an alternative approach is needed:\n- **Fallback option A:** Server-side rendering via `d2` CLI (similar to how PlantUML uses a server)\n- **Fallback option B:** Use a simpler D2 rendering library if available\n- **Minimum viable:** Show raw D2 source with syntax highlighting as placeholder, with a note that D2 rendering requires server-side support\n\n### 2.5 Graphviz Renderer\n\n**Dependencies:** `@viz-js/viz` WASM package\n\n**Loading strategy:** Lazy-load — only fetch WASM when a Graphviz diagram appears.\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nlet vizInstance = null;\n\nasync function loadViz() {\n    if (vizInstance) return vizInstance;\n    const { instance } = await import('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@viz-js/viz/...');\n    vizInstance = await instance();\n    return vizInstance;\n}\n\nasync function renderGraphviz(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const viz = await loadViz();\n        const svg = viz.renderSVGElement(content, { engine: 'dot' });\n        el.innerHTML = '';\n        el.appendChild(svg);\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>Graphviz render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Engine selection:** Default to `dot` layout engine. Could expose engine selection per-diagram via a `layoutEngine` field in manifest (future enhancement — not in scope now).\n\n### 2.6 Draw.io Renderer (Existing Gap — Implement Now)\n\n**Current state:** Falls through to `<pre>` tag with escaped XML content.\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nfunction renderDrawio(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        // Use Draw.io's public viewer with inline XML\n        const encoded = encodeURIComponent(content);\n        const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');\n        iframe.src = `https://viewer.diagrams.net/?highlight=0000ff&nav=1&title=${filename}#R${encoded}`;\n        iframe.style.width = '100%';\n        iframe.style.height = '500px';\n        iframe.style.border = 'none';\n        iframe.setAttribute('sandbox', 'allow-scripts allow-same-origin');\n        el.innerHTML = '';\n        el.appendChild(iframe);\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>Draw.io render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Alternative:** For large `.drawio` files, the URL-encoded approach may exceed URL limits. Use `postMessage` API instead:\n1. Create iframe pointing to `https://viewer.diagrams.net/`\n2. Send diagram XML via `iframe.contentWindow.postMessage()` after iframe loads\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 2)\n\n- [ ] Mermaid diagrams continue to render correctly (no regression)\n- [ ] PlantUML diagrams render as SVG via server fetch\n- [ ] D2 diagrams render via WASM (or show fallback with raw source)\n- [ ] Graphviz diagrams render via `@viz-js/viz` WASM\n- [ ] Draw.io diagrams render in iframe (not raw XML)\n- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML\n- [ ] Each renderer shows error + raw source on failure\n- [ ] WASM modules load lazily (only when diagram type appears on page)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Markdown Renderer & Inline Editor\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Key new user interaction\n**Depends on:** Phase 1 (PUT endpoint), Phase 2 (renderer infrastructure)\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium-High\n\n### 3.1 Markdown Renderer\n\n**Library:** `marked.js` — already loaded in architecture.html (line 7, used for chat streaming).\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nfunction renderMarkdown(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const html = marked.parse(content);\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"markdown-content\">${html}</div>`;\n        // Store original content for edit mode\n        el.dataset.rawContent = content;\n        el.dataset.filename = filename;\n        el.dataset.idx = idx;\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3.2 Edit Button on Markdown Cards\n\nFor diagram cards where `type === \"markdown\"`, add a pencil icon button in the card header (alongside existing zoom controls).\n\n**Placement:** In the diagram card header template (around line 1016-1041 in architecture.html), conditionally add:\n\n```html\n{% if diagram.type == 'markdown' %}\n<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(idx)\" title=\"Edit markdown\">\n    ✎\n</button>\n{% endif %}\n```\n\n**Note:** Since diagrams are rendered client-side from the DIAGRAMS array, the edit button must be added in JavaScript during card construction, not in Jinja2. Check the type from the manifest entry.\n\n### 3.3 Edit Mode State Machine\n\n**States:** `view` → `editing` → `saving` → `view`\n\n```javascript\nconst markdownEditState = {};  // idx -> { editing: bool, saving: bool, originalContent: string }\n\nfunction toggleMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx] || { editing: false };\n\n    if (state.editing) {\n        cancelMarkdownEdit(idx);\n    } else {\n        enterMarkdownEdit(idx);\n    }\n}\n\nfunction enterMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n    const content = el.dataset.rawContent || diagramContents[DIAGRAMS[idx].file];\n\n    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: true, saving: false, originalContent: content };\n\n    el.innerHTML = `\n        <div class=\"md-editor-container\">\n            <div class=\"md-editor-toolbar\">\n                <button class=\"md-save-btn\" onclick=\"saveMarkdown(${idx})\" title=\"Save\">✓ Save</button>\n                <button class=\"md-cancel-btn\" onclick=\"cancelMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Cancel\">✕ Cancel</button>\n                <span class=\"md-save-indicator\" id=\"md-indicator-${idx}\"></span>\n            </div>\n            <textarea class=\"md-editor\" id=\"md-textarea-${idx}\" spellcheck=\"false\">${escapeHtml(content)}</textarea>\n        </div>\n    `;\n\n    // Focus and auto-resize\n    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n    textarea.focus();\n    autoResizeTextarea(textarea);\n    textarea.addEventListener('input', () => autoResizeTextarea(textarea));\n\n    // Update card header button state\n    updateEditButton(idx, true);\n}\n\nfunction cancelMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n    if (!state) return;\n\n    // Re-render the markdown view\n    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n    renderMarkdown(el, state.originalContent, idx, DIAGRAMS[idx].file);\n\n    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n    updateEditButton(idx, false);\n}\n\nasync function saveMarkdown(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n    if (!state || state.saving) return;\n\n    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n    const newContent = textarea.value;\n    const filename = DIAGRAMS[idx].file;\n    const indicator = document.getElementById(`md-indicator-${idx}`);\n\n    state.saving = true;\n    indicator.textContent = 'Saving...';\n    indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saving';\n\n    try {\n        const resp = await fetch(\n            `/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${filename}`,\n            {\n                method: 'PUT',\n                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n                body: JSON.stringify({ content: newContent }),\n            }\n        );\n\n        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`Save failed: ${resp.status}`);\n\n        indicator.textContent = 'Saved!';\n        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saved';\n\n        // Update stored content\n        diagramContents[filename] = newContent;\n\n        // Return to view mode after brief success indicator\n        setTimeout(() => {\n            const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n            renderMarkdown(el, newContent, idx, filename);\n            markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n            updateEditButton(idx, false);\n        }, 800);\n\n    } catch (err) {\n        indicator.textContent = `Error: ${err.message}`;\n        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator error';\n        state.saving = false;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3.4 Editor Styles\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` (or inline in architecture.html)\n\n```css\n.md-editor-container {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    height: 100%;\n    min-height: 200px;\n}\n\n.md-editor-toolbar {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 8px;\n    padding: 8px 12px;\n    background: var(--surface-2);\n    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n}\n\n.md-editor {\n    flex: 1;\n    resize: vertical;\n    min-height: 200px;\n    padding: 16px;\n    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    background: var(--surface-1);\n    color: var(--text-primary);\n    border: none;\n    outline: none;\n}\n\n.md-save-btn { color: #4ade80; }\n.md-cancel-btn { color: #f87171; }\n.md-save-indicator.saving { color: #facc15; }\n.md-save-indicator.saved { color: #4ade80; }\n.md-save-indicator.error { color: #f87171; }\n\n.markdown-content {\n    padding: 16px;\n    line-height: 1.7;\n}\n.markdown-content h1, .markdown-content h2, .markdown-content h3 {\n    margin-top: 1.5em;\n    margin-bottom: 0.5em;\n}\n.markdown-content pre {\n    background: var(--surface-2);\n    padding: 12px;\n    border-radius: 6px;\n    overflow-x: auto;\n}\n.markdown-content code {\n    background: var(--surface-2);\n    padding: 2px 6px;\n    border-radius: 3px;\n    font-size: 0.9em;\n}\n.markdown-content table {\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    width: 100%;\n}\n.markdown-content th, .markdown-content td {\n    border: 1px solid var(--border);\n    padding: 8px 12px;\n    text-align: left;\n}\n```\n\n### 3.5 Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+S` / `Cmd+S` in edit mode → Save\n- `Escape` in edit mode → Cancel\n\n```javascript\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n    // Find any active markdown editor\n    for (const [idx, state] of Object.entries(markdownEditState)) {\n        if (state.editing) {\n            if ((e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) && e.key === 's') {\n                e.preventDefault();\n                saveMarkdown(parseInt(idx));\n            } else if (e.key === 'Escape') {\n                e.preventDefault();\n                cancelMarkdownEdit(parseInt(idx));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n});\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 3)\n\n- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML with GFM support (tables, code blocks, task lists)\n- [ ] Edit button appears only on markdown-type diagram cards\n- [ ] Clicking edit switches to textarea with raw content\n- [ ] Save writes content to disk via PUT API and returns to rendered view\n- [ ] Cancel discards changes and returns to rendered view\n- [ ] Save indicator shows progress (saving → saved → hidden)\n- [ ] Save failure shows error message\n- [ ] Ctrl+S saves, Escape cancels\n- [ ] Content stored in `diagramContents` is updated after successful save\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Template & Watcher Integration\n\n**Priority:** MEDIUM\n**Depends on:** Phases 1-3\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low-Medium\n\n### 4.1 Pass Manifest Type to Renderers\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\nUpdate `loadDiagrams()` to pass the manifest `type` field:\n\n```javascript\nasync function loadDiagrams() {\n    for (let i = 0; i < DIAGRAMS.length; i++) {\n        const diagram = DIAGRAMS[i];\n        const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${diagram.file}`);\n        const content = await resp.text();\n        diagramContents[diagram.file] = content;\n\n        const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${i}`);\n        renderDiagramContent(el, diagram.file, content, i, diagram.type);  // Pass type!\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 4.2 Conditionally Show Edit Button in Card Header\n\nWhen building diagram cards (JavaScript, not Jinja2), check the diagram type:\n\n```javascript\nfunction buildDiagramCard(diagram, idx) {\n    // ... existing card structure ...\n\n    const editButton = diagram.type === 'markdown'\n        ? `<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Edit\">✎</button>`\n        : '';\n\n    // Insert into card header alongside zoom controls\n}\n```\n\n### 4.3 Update Diagram Watcher Manifest Auto-Update\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n\nThe `_update_manifest_sync()` function currently scans for `.mmd` and `.drawio` only. Update to scan all supported extensions and set the `type` field correctly:\n\n```python\nEXT_TO_TYPE = {\n    \".mmd\": \"mermaid\",\n    \".drawio\": \"drawio\",\n    \".puml\": \"plantuml\",\n    \".d2\": \"d2\",\n    \".dot\": \"graphviz\",\n    \".md\": \"markdown\",\n}\n\n# In _update_manifest_sync():\nfor f in sorted(arch_dir.iterdir()):\n    if f.suffix in EXT_TO_TYPE and not f.name.startswith(\"_\"):\n        file_type = EXT_TO_TYPE[f.suffix]\n        diagram_type = _detect_diagram_type(f) if file_type == \"mermaid\" else \"custom\"\n        entry = {\n            \"name\": f.stem.replace(\"-\", \" \").replace(\"_\", \" \").title(),\n            \"file\": f.name,\n            \"type\": file_type,\n            \"diagramType\": diagram_type,\n            \"description\": f\"Auto-detected {file_type} diagram\",\n        }\n        diagrams.append(entry)\n```\n\n### 4.4 CDN Script Loading\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\nAdd CDN scripts in the `<head>` section. WASM-based renderers should lazy-load, but the encoder library can be loaded eagerly (small):\n\n```html\n<!-- PlantUML encoder (small, ~10KB) -->\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder@1.4.0/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js\"></script>\n\n<!-- D2 and Graphviz loaded lazily by their respective renderers -->\n```\n\nFor `@viz-js/viz`, the CDN approach:\n```html\n<!-- Loaded dynamically in renderGraphviz() -->\n<!-- https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@viz-js/viz@3/lib/viz-standalone.js -->\n```\n\n### 4.5 PlantUML Server URL Injection\n\nThe architecture page template needs to know the PlantUML server URL. Options:\n\n**Option A (recommended):** Pass from server context:\n```python\n# In architecture_viewer_page():\nfrom server.services.settings_service import get_settings\nsettings = get_settings()\nplantuml_url = settings.get(\"plantuml_server_url\", \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\")\n```\n\nAnd in the template:\n```html\n<script>\n    const PLANTUML_SERVER_URL = {{ plantuml_url | tojson }};\n</script>\n```\n\n**Option B:** Fetch from settings API client-side. Less efficient.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 4)\n\n- [ ] All 6 diagram types dispatch to their correct renderer\n- [ ] Edit button only appears on markdown cards\n- [ ] Watcher detects changes in all 6 file types\n- [ ] Manifest auto-update correctly assigns type from extension\n- [ ] PlantUML server URL passed from settings to frontend\n- [ ] CDN scripts loaded (eagerly for small libs, lazily for WASM)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Tests\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Must validate security and correctness\n**Depends on:** Phases 1-4\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n\n### 5.1 PUT Endpoint Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestArchWriteAPI:\n    def test_put_markdown_file_success(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT .md file writes content and returns 200.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_non_markdown_file_rejected(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT .mmd file returns 400.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_path_traversal_blocked(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT ../../evil.md returns 400.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_project_not_found(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT to nonexistent project returns 404.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_no_arch_directory(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT to feature without arch/ returns 400.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### 5.2 ProgressService Write Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestProgressServiceWrite:\n    def test_write_arch_file_md_success(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() writes .md content to arch/.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_mmd_rejected(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() rejects .mmd files.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_path_traversal(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() blocks ../evil path.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_no_arch_dir(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() returns False when arch/ doesn't exist.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### 5.3 Schema Validation Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestExtendedSchemaValidation:\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_plantuml_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_d2_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_graphviz_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_markdown_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_rejects_unknown_type(self):\n```\n\n### 5.4 Content-Type Tests\n\n```python\nclass TestContentTypes:\n    def test_get_puml_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_d2_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_dot_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_md_returns_text_markdown(self, api_env):\n```\n\n### 5.5 Diagram Watcher Extension Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestExtendedFileTypes:\n    def test_watches_puml_files(self):\n    def test_watches_d2_files(self):\n    def test_watches_dot_files(self):\n    def test_watches_md_files(self):\n    def test_manifest_update_assigns_correct_type(self):\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 5)\n\n- [ ] All PUT endpoint tests pass (including security: path traversal, extension whitelist)\n- [ ] All schema validation tests pass for 6 types\n- [ ] Content-type tests pass for all new extensions\n- [ ] Watcher tests pass for all 6 file types\n- [ ] No regressions in existing 139 tests\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Documentation & Skill Updates\n\n**Priority:** LOW\n**Depends on:** All prior phases\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n\n### 6.1 Update Plan Skill SKILL.md\n\n**File:** `vista/skills/plan/SKILL.md`\n\nUpdate Step 3 (architecture generation) to mention all supported formats:\n- Default: Mermaid (.mmd) for all diagram types\n- Optional: PlantUML (.puml) for detailed UML class/sequence diagrams\n- Optional: D2 (.d2) for architecture diagrams with auto-layout\n- Optional: Graphviz (.dot) for dependency graphs\n- Optional: Markdown (.md) for prose documentation (design rationale, ADRs)\n\n### 6.2 Update Diagrams Skill\n\n**File:** `vista/skills/diagrams/SKILL.md` (if exists)\n\nDocument the expanded format support.\n\n### 6.3 Update arch-directory.md Spec\n\n**File:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/specs/arch-directory.md`\n\nUpdate to reflect the expanded type enum, new file extensions, and markdown editing capability.\n\n### 6.4 Update rendering-pipeline.md Spec\n\n**File:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/specs/rendering-pipeline.md`\n\nUpdate renderer table to include all 6 renderers.\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|-----------|--------|------------|\n| D2 WASM not available as browser-compatible package | Medium | Medium | Fall back to raw source display with syntax highlighting |\n| PlantUML server rate limiting | Low | Low | Self-hosted server option in settings |\n| @viz-js/viz WASM too large (>5MB) | Low | Medium | Lazy load only when Graphviz diagram appears |\n| Draw.io viewer URL encoding exceeds limits for large files | Medium | Medium | Use postMessage API instead of URL params |\n| Markdown editor unsaved changes lost on navigation | Low | Medium | Add `beforeunload` warning when editing |\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Order (Recommended)\n\n1. **Phase 1** — Backend foundation (schema, PUT endpoint, watcher extensions, settings)\n2. **Phase 2** — Renderer infrastructure (dispatch refactor + all 6 renderers)\n3. **Phase 3** — Markdown editor (edit mode, save/cancel, keyboard shortcuts)\n4. **Phase 4** — Template integration (type passing, CDN loading, watcher updates)\n5. **Phase 5** — Tests (PUT security, schema, content types, watcher)\n6. **Phase 6** — Documentation\n\n**Estimated total:** ~3-4 build iterations\n\n---\n\n## Files Summary\n\n### Files to Modify\n\n| File | Changes |\n|------|---------|\n| `vista/templates/arch-schema.json` | Extend `type` enum: add `plantuml`, `d2`, `graphviz`, `markdown` |\n| `vista/server/services/progress_service.py` | Add `write_arch_file()` method |\n| `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` | Add PUT endpoint, update content-type mapping |\n| `vista/server/views/architecture.html` | Refactor renderer dispatch, add 5 new renderers, add markdown editor |\n| `vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` | Add markdown editor styles |\n| `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py` | Extend `WATCH_EXTENSIONS`, update manifest type detection |\n| `vista/tests/test_architecture.py` | Add ~15 new tests for PUT, schema, content types |\n| `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py` | Add ~5 new tests for extended file types |\n\n### Files to Create\n\nNone — all changes are modifications to existing files.\n\n### Settings Changes\n\n| Setting | Value | Location |\n|---------|-------|----------|\n| `plantuml_server_url` | `\"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\"` | `~/.vista/settings.json` |\n\n---\n\n## Spec Versions\n\n| Spec File | Latest Changelog Date | Notes |\n|-----------|-----------------------|-------|\n| `specs/arch-directory.md` | 2026-02-15 | `diagramType` enum and category aligned with arch-schema.json |\n| `specs/rendering-pipeline.md` | 2026-02-15 | Draw.io status clarified, acceptance criteria updated |\n| `specs/chat-review.md` | 2026-02-15 | Protocol-native streaming alignment |\n| `specs/migration-cleanup.md` | 2026-02-15 | All acceptance criteria verified complete |\n| `domain-requirements.md` (Expansion) | 2026-02-15 | Multi-format diagrams, markdown editing, type system updates |\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
