{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KWgAJoLmVoqmsgbso9ZB4i","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation Plan: Multi-Format Diagram Support & Markdown Editing\n     2→\n     3→**Status:** PLANNING — New feature expansion for diagram_representations\n     4→**Created:** 2026-02-15\n     5→**Spec Source:** `domain-requirements.md` Expansion section (added 2026-02-15)\n     6→**Parent Feature:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/`\n     7→\n     8→---\n     9→\n    10→## Context\n    11→\n    12→The existing diagram_representations feature is largely delivered (Phases 1-4 complete, Phase 5 partial). The domain-requirements.md has been expanded with three new areas:\n    13→\n    14→1. **Multi-Format Rendering** — PlantUML (.puml), D2 (.d2), Graphviz (.dot), Markdown (.md)\n    15→2. **Markdown Inline Editing** — View/edit toggle, save to disk via PUT API, cancel/discard\n    16→3. **Manifest & Type System Updates** — Extended type enum, renderer dispatch, file extension mapping\n    17→\n    18→This plan covers implementing these expansion requirements on top of the existing codebase.\n    19→\n    20→---\n    21→\n    22→## Current State Assessment\n    23→\n    24→### What Exists (Working)\n    25→\n    26→| Component | Status | Location |\n    27→|-----------|--------|----------|\n    28→| Mermaid rendering | Complete | `architecture.html:1289-1307` — `mermaid.render()` |\n    29→| Renderer dispatch | Partial — only `.mmd` check + fallback `<pre>` | `architecture.html:1288-1311` |\n    30→| `_arch.json` schema | `type` enum: `[\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]` only | `arch-schema.json:29` |\n    31→| Diagram watcher | Watches `.mmd` and `.drawio` only | `diagram_watcher.py:26` — `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` |\n    32→| Manifest auto-update | Detects diagram type for mermaid files only | `diagram_watcher.py:102-118` |\n    33→| API: GET manifest | Complete | `architecture.py:15-26` |\n    34→| API: GET file | Complete (read-only, text/plain or application/xml) | `architecture.py:29-48` |\n    35→| API: PUT file | **Does not exist** | Needed for markdown save |\n    36→| Path traversal protection | Complete | `progress_service.py:80-92` |\n    37→| Pan/zoom per diagram | Complete | `architecture.html:1323-1375` |\n    38→| Settings file | No `plantuml_server_url` field | `~/.vista/settings.json` |\n    39→\n    40→### What Needs to Change\n    41→\n    42→1. **arch-schema.json** — Extend `type` enum from 2 to 6 values\n    43→2. **diagram_watcher.py** — Extend `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` and `_detect_diagram_type()` for new formats\n    44→3. **progress_service.py** — Add `write_arch_file()` method for markdown save\n    45→4. **architecture.py** — Add `PUT` endpoint, update content-type mapping for new extensions\n    46→5. **architecture.html** — Add 4 new renderers + markdown edit mode\n    47→6. **Settings** — Add `plantuml_server_url` default\n    48→7. **Tests** — Cover all new renderers, PUT endpoint, security\n    49→\n    50→---\n    51→\n    52→## Phase 1: Schema & Backend Foundation\n    53→\n    54→**Priority:** HIGH — All other phases depend on this\n    55→**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n    56→\n    57→### 1.1 Extend arch-schema.json Type Enum\n    58→\n    59→**File:** `vista/templates/arch-schema.json`\n    60→\n    61→Change line 29:\n    62→```json\n    63→\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]\n    64→```\n    65→To:\n    66→```json\n    67→\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\", \"plantuml\", \"d2\", \"graphviz\", \"markdown\"]\n    68→```\n    69→\n    70→No other schema changes needed — `diagramType` enum already has `\"custom\"` as a catch-all for non-Mermaid diagrams. The `category` field is already optional with `architecture` and `tdd` values.\n    71→\n    72→### 1.2 Add write_arch_file() to ProgressService\n    73→\n    74→**File:** `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n    75→\n    76→Add new static method after `read_arch_file()`:\n    77→\n    78→```python\n    79→@staticmethod\n    80→def write_arch_file(project_path: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, content: str) -> bool:\n    81→    \"\"\"Write content to a diagram file in arch/ with path traversal prevention.\n    82→\n    83→    Only allows writing to files with extensions: .md\n    84→    Returns True on success, False on validation failure.\n    85→    \"\"\"\n    86→    WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS = {\".md\"}\n    87→\n    88→    safe_name = Path(filename).name\n    89→    if safe_name != filename or \"..\" in filename:\n    90→        return False\n    91→\n    92→    if Path(safe_name).suffix not in WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS:\n    93→        return False\n    94→\n    95→    arch_dir = Path(project_path) / \".vista\" / \"features\" / feature_name / \"arch\"\n    96→    target = arch_dir / safe_name\n    97→\n    98→    try:\n    99→        target.resolve().relative_to(arch_dir.resolve())\n   100→    except ValueError:\n   101→        return False\n   102→\n   103→    if not arch_dir.exists():\n   104→        return False\n   105→\n   106→    target.write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n   107→    return True\n   108→```\n   109→\n   110→**Key decisions:**\n   111→- **Writable extensions restricted to `.md` only** — Diagram files (.mmd, .puml, .d2, .dot, .drawio) are NOT writable through this API. Only markdown documentation files are editable inline.\n   112→- **Same path traversal protection** as `read_arch_file()`.\n   113→- **File must be in an existing arch/ directory** — won't create directories.\n   114→\n   115→### 1.3 Add PUT Endpoint for File Writing\n   116→\n   117→**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py`\n   118→\n   119→Add new route:\n   120→\n   121→```python\n   122→from pydantic import BaseModel\n   123→\n   124→class FileContent(BaseModel):\n   125→    content: str\n   126→\n   127→@router.put(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/features/{feature_name}/arch/{filename}\")\n   128→async def put_arch_file(project_id: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, body: FileContent):\n   129→    \"\"\"Write content to a markdown file in arch/.\"\"\"\n   130→    project = ProjectService.get_by_id(project_id)\n   131→    if not project:\n   132→        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Project not found\")\n   133→\n   134→    success = ProgressService.write_arch_file(project.path, feature_name, filename, body.content)\n   135→    if not success:\n   136→        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Cannot write to this file\")\n   137→\n   138→    return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"filename\": filename}\n   139→```\n   140→\n   141→### 1.4 Update Content-Type Mapping in GET Endpoint\n   142→\n   143→**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` — `get_arch_file()` function\n   144→\n   145→Update the content-type section (lines 41-46):\n   146→\n   147→```python\n   148→ext = filename.rsplit(\".\", 1)[-1] if \".\" in filename else \"\"\n   149→CONTENT_TYPES = {\n   150→    \"mmd\": \"text/plain\",\n   151→    \"drawio\": \"application/xml\",\n   152→    \"puml\": \"text/plain\",\n   153→    \"d2\": \"text/plain\",\n   154→    \"dot\": \"text/plain\",\n   155→    \"md\": \"text/markdown\",\n   156→}\n   157→media_type = CONTENT_TYPES.get(ext, \"text/plain\")\n   158→```\n   159→\n   160→### 1.5 Add PlantUML Server URL to Settings\n   161→\n   162→**File:** `vista/server/services/settings_service.py` (or wherever defaults are defined)\n   163→\n   164→Add default `plantuml_server_url` to settings schema:\n   165→```json\n   166→\"plantuml_server_url\": \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\"\n   167→```\n   168→\n   169→**Also update:** `~/.vista/settings.json` default initialization if a settings template exists.\n   170→\n   171→**Server-side API:** Add a `GET /api/settings/plantuml-server` endpoint (or include in existing settings response) so the frontend can discover the configured PlantUML server URL.\n   172→\n   173→### 1.6 Extend Diagram Watcher Extensions\n   174→\n   175→**File:** `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n   176→\n   177→Update `_DiagramEventHandler` class:\n   178→\n   179→```python\n   180→WATCH_EXTENSIONS = {\".mmd\", \".drawio\", \".puml\", \".d2\", \".dot\", \".md\"}\n   181→```\n   182→\n   183→Update `_detect_diagram_type()` to return type based on extension (not just mermaid content parsing):\n   184→\n   185→```python\n   186→def _detect_file_type(path: Path) -> str:\n   187→    \"\"\"Detect diagram type from file extension.\"\"\"\n   188→    EXT_TO_TYPE = {\n   189→        \".mmd\": \"mermaid\",\n   190→        \".drawio\": \"drawio\",\n   191→        \".puml\": \"plantuml\",\n   192→        \".d2\": \"d2\",\n   193→        \".dot\": \"graphviz\",\n   194→        \".md\": \"markdown\",\n   195→    }\n   196→    return EXT_TO_TYPE.get(path.suffix.lower(), \"mermaid\")\n   197→```\n   198→\n   199→Update `_update_manifest_sync()` to use `_detect_file_type()` for the `type` field and retain `_detect_diagram_type()` for the `diagramType` field (mermaid subtypes). For non-mermaid formats, set `diagramType: \"custom\"`.\n   200→\n   201→### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 1)\n   202→\n   203→- [ ] `arch-schema.json` validates manifests with all 6 type values\n   204→- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` writes `.md` files successfully\n   205→- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns 400 for non-`.md` files\n   206→- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` blocks path traversal attempts\n   207→- [ ] `GET /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns correct Content-Type for all 6 extensions\n   208→- [ ] Diagram watcher detects changes in all 6 file types\n   209→- [ ] Manifest auto-update correctly identifies file types by extension\n   210→\n   211→---\n   212→\n   213→## Phase 2: Client-Side Renderer Infrastructure\n   214→\n   215→**Priority:** HIGH — Core rendering dispatch\n   216→**Depends on:** Phase 1\n   217→**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n   218→\n   219→### 2.1 Refactor Renderer Dispatch\n   220→\n   221→**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n   222→\n   223→Currently, `renderDiagramContent()` (line 1288) checks `filename.endsWith('.mmd')` and falls back to `<pre>`. Refactor to a renderer map pattern:\n   224→\n   225→```javascript\n   226→const RENDERERS = {\n   227→    mermaid:  renderMermaid,\n   228→    plantuml: renderPlantUML,\n   229→    d2:       renderD2,\n   230→    graphviz: renderGraphviz,\n   231→    drawio:   renderDrawio,\n   232→    markdown: renderMarkdown,\n   233→};\n   234→\n   235→function renderDiagramContent(el, filename, content, idx, diagramType) {\n   236→    // diagramType is the 'type' field from manifest (mermaid, plantuml, etc.)\n   237→    // NOT diagramType (flowchart, sequence, etc.)\n   238→    const renderer = RENDERERS[diagramType];\n   239→    if (renderer) {\n   240→        return renderer(el, content, idx, filename);\n   241→    }\n   242→    // Unknown type fallback\n   243→    el.innerHTML = `<pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n   244→}\n   245→```\n   246→\n   247→**Change needed:** The template must pass the manifest `type` field to `renderDiagramContent()`. Currently, `loadDiagrams()` only passes filename/content/idx. Update to also pass `diagram.type` from the manifest `DIAGRAMS` array.\n   248→\n   249→### 2.2 Mermaid Renderer (Existing — No Changes)\n   250→\n   251→Stays as-is: `mermaid.render(id, content)` → SVG injection → click handlers for element selection.\n   252→\n   253→### 2.3 PlantUML Renderer\n   254→\n   255→**Dependencies:** `plantuml-encoder` library (CDN or bundled)\n   256→\n   257→**Rendering flow:**\n   258→1. Encode PlantUML source to deflate+base64 using `plantuml-encoder` algorithm\n   259→2. Construct URL: `${PLANTUML_SERVER_URL}/svg/${encoded}`\n   260→3. Fetch SVG from PlantUML server\n   261→4. Inject SVG into card container\n   262→\n   263→**Library loading:** CDN — `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js`\n   264→\n   265→**Implementation:**\n   266→```javascript\n   267→async function renderPlantUML(el, content, idx, filename) {\n   268→    try {\n   269→        const encoded = plantumlEncoder.encode(content);\n   270→        const serverUrl = PLANTUML_SERVER_URL;  // From server template var or settings API\n   271→        const svgUrl = `${serverUrl}/svg/${encoded}`;\n   272→        const resp = await fetch(svgUrl);\n   273→        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`PlantUML server error: ${resp.status}`);\n   274→        const svg = await resp.text();\n   275→        el.innerHTML = svg;\n   276→    } catch (err) {\n   277→        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n   278→            <p>PlantUML render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n   279→            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n   280→        </div>`;\n   281→    }\n   282→}\n   283→```\n   284→\n   285→**Error handling:**\n   286→- Server unreachable → Show error + raw source as fallback\n   287→- Invalid syntax → PlantUML server returns error image; detect via content-type or error body\n   288→\n   289→**Template variable:** Pass `PLANTUML_SERVER_URL` from server context (read from settings).\n   290→\n   291→### 2.4 D2 Renderer\n   292→\n   293→**Dependencies:** `@terrastruct/d2` WASM package\n   294→\n   295→**Loading strategy:** Lazy-load — only fetch WASM when a D2 diagram appears.\n   296→\n   297→**Implementation approach:**\n   298→```javascript\n   299→let d2Module = null;\n   300→\n   301→async function loadD2() {\n   302→    if (d2Module) return d2Module;\n   303→    // Dynamic import from CDN\n   304→    d2Module = await import('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@anthropic-ai/d2-wasm/...');\n   305→    return d2Module;\n   306→}\n   307→\n   308→async function renderD2(el, content, idx, filename) {\n   309→    try {\n   310→        const d2 = await loadD2();\n   311→        const svg = await d2.compile(content, { layout: 'dagre' });\n   312→        el.innerHTML = svg;\n   313→    } catch (err) {\n   314→        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n   315→            <p>D2 render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n   316→            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n   317→        </div>`;\n   318→    }\n   319→}\n   320→```\n   321→\n   322→**Note:** D2 WASM availability needs verification. If `@terrastruct/d2` doesn't provide a browser-compatible WASM, an alternative approach is needed:\n   323→- **Fallback option A:** Server-side rendering via `d2` CLI (similar to how PlantUML uses a server)\n   324→- **Fallback option B:** Use a simpler D2 rendering library if available\n   325→- **Minimum viable:** Show raw D2 source with syntax highlighting as placeholder, with a note that D2 rendering requires server-side support\n   326→\n   327→### 2.5 Graphviz Renderer\n   328→\n   329→**Dependencies:** `@viz-js/viz` WASM package\n   330→\n   331→**Loading strategy:** Lazy-load — only fetch WASM when a Graphviz diagram appears.\n   332→\n   333→**Implementation:**\n   334→```javascript\n   335→let vizInstance = null;\n   336→\n   337→async function loadViz() {\n   338→    if (vizInstance) return vizInstance;\n   339→    const { instance } = await import('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@viz-js/viz/...');\n   340→    vizInstance = await instance();\n   341→    return vizInstance;\n   342→}\n   343→\n   344→async function renderGraphviz(el, content, idx, filename) {\n   345→    try {\n   346→        const viz = await loadViz();\n   347→        const svg = viz.renderSVGElement(content, { engine: 'dot' });\n   348→        el.innerHTML = '';\n   349→        el.appendChild(svg);\n   350→    } catch (err) {\n   351→        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n   352→            <p>Graphviz render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n   353→            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n   354→        </div>`;\n   355→    }\n   356→}\n   357→```\n   358→\n   359→**Engine selection:** Default to `dot` layout engine. Could expose engine selection per-diagram via a `layoutEngine` field in manifest (future enhancement — not in scope now).\n   360→\n   361→### 2.6 Draw.io Renderer (Existing Gap — Implement Now)\n   362→\n   363→**Current state:** Falls through to `<pre>` tag with escaped XML content.\n   364→\n   365→**Implementation:**\n   366→```javascript\n   367→function renderDrawio(el, content, idx, filename) {\n   368→    try {\n   369→        // Use Draw.io's public viewer with inline XML\n   370→        const encoded = encodeURIComponent(content);\n   371→        const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');\n   372→        iframe.src = `https://viewer.diagrams.net/?highlight=0000ff&nav=1&title=${filename}#R${encoded}`;\n   373→        iframe.style.width = '100%';\n   374→        iframe.style.height = '500px';\n   375→        iframe.style.border = 'none';\n   376→        iframe.setAttribute('sandbox', 'allow-scripts allow-same-origin');\n   377→        el.innerHTML = '';\n   378→        el.appendChild(iframe);\n   379→    } catch (err) {\n   380→        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n   381→            <p>Draw.io render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n   382→            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n   383→        </div>`;\n   384→    }\n   385→}\n   386→```\n   387→\n   388→**Alternative:** For large `.drawio` files, the URL-encoded approach may exceed URL limits. Use `postMessage` API instead:\n   389→1. Create iframe pointing to `https://viewer.diagrams.net/`\n   390→2. Send diagram XML via `iframe.contentWindow.postMessage()` after iframe loads\n   391→\n   392→### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 2)\n   393→\n   394→- [ ] Mermaid diagrams continue to render correctly (no regression)\n   395→- [ ] PlantUML diagrams render as SVG via server fetch\n   396→- [ ] D2 diagrams render via WASM (or show fallback with raw source)\n   397→- [ ] Graphviz diagrams render via `@viz-js/viz` WASM\n   398→- [ ] Draw.io diagrams render in iframe (not raw XML)\n   399→- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML\n   400→- [ ] Each renderer shows error + raw source on failure\n   401→- [ ] WASM modules load lazily (only when diagram type appears on page)\n   402→\n   403→---\n   404→\n   405→## Phase 3: Markdown Renderer & Inline Editor\n   406→\n   407→**Priority:** HIGH — Key new user interaction\n   408→**Depends on:** Phase 1 (PUT endpoint), Phase 2 (renderer infrastructure)\n   409→**Estimated Complexity:** Medium-High\n   410→\n   411→### 3.1 Markdown Renderer\n   412→\n   413→**Library:** `marked.js` — already loaded in architecture.html (line 7, used for chat streaming).\n   414→\n   415→**Implementation:**\n   416→```javascript\n   417→function renderMarkdown(el, content, idx, filename) {\n   418→    try {\n   419→        const html = marked.parse(content);\n   420→        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"markdown-content\">${html}</div>`;\n   421→        // Store original content for edit mode\n   422→        el.dataset.rawContent = content;\n   423→        el.dataset.filename = filename;\n   424→        el.dataset.idx = idx;\n   425→    } catch (err) {\n   426→        el.innerHTML = `<pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n   427→    }\n   428→}\n   429→```\n   430→\n   431→### 3.2 Edit Button on Markdown Cards\n   432→\n   433→For diagram cards where `type === \"markdown\"`, add a pencil icon button in the card header (alongside existing zoom controls).\n   434→\n   435→**Placement:** In the diagram card header template (around line 1016-1041 in architecture.html), conditionally add:\n   436→\n   437→```html\n   438→{% if diagram.type == 'markdown' %}\n   439→<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(idx)\" title=\"Edit markdown\">\n   440→    ✎\n   441→</button>\n   442→{% endif %}\n   443→```\n   444→\n   445→**Note:** Since diagrams are rendered client-side from the DIAGRAMS array, the edit button must be added in JavaScript during card construction, not in Jinja2. Check the type from the manifest entry.\n   446→\n   447→### 3.3 Edit Mode State Machine\n   448→\n   449→**States:** `view` → `editing` → `saving` → `view`\n   450→\n   451→```javascript\n   452→const markdownEditState = {};  // idx -> { editing: bool, saving: bool, originalContent: string }\n   453→\n   454→function toggleMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n   455→    const state = markdownEditState[idx] || { editing: false };\n   456→\n   457→    if (state.editing) {\n   458→        cancelMarkdownEdit(idx);\n   459→    } else {\n   460→        enterMarkdownEdit(idx);\n   461→    }\n   462→}\n   463→\n   464→function enterMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n   465→    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n   466→    const content = el.dataset.rawContent || diagramContents[DIAGRAMS[idx].file];\n   467→\n   468→    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: true, saving: false, originalContent: content };\n   469→\n   470→    el.innerHTML = `\n   471→        <div class=\"md-editor-container\">\n   472→            <div class=\"md-editor-toolbar\">\n   473→                <button class=\"md-save-btn\" onclick=\"saveMarkdown(${idx})\" title=\"Save\">✓ Save</button>\n   474→                <button class=\"md-cancel-btn\" onclick=\"cancelMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Cancel\">✕ Cancel</button>\n   475→                <span class=\"md-save-indicator\" id=\"md-indicator-${idx}\"></span>\n   476→            </div>\n   477→            <textarea class=\"md-editor\" id=\"md-textarea-${idx}\" spellcheck=\"false\">${escapeHtml(content)}</textarea>\n   478→        </div>\n   479→    `;\n   480→\n   481→    // Focus and auto-resize\n   482→    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n   483→    textarea.focus();\n   484→    autoResizeTextarea(textarea);\n   485→    textarea.addEventListener('input', () => autoResizeTextarea(textarea));\n   486→\n   487→    // Update card header button state\n   488→    updateEditButton(idx, true);\n   489→}\n   490→\n   491→function cancelMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n   492→    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n   493→    if (!state) return;\n   494→\n   495→    // Re-render the markdown view\n   496→    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n   497→    renderMarkdown(el, state.originalContent, idx, DIAGRAMS[idx].file);\n   498→\n   499→    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n   500→    updateEditButton(idx, false);\n   501→}\n   502→\n   503→async function saveMarkdown(idx) {\n   504→    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n   505→    if (!state || state.saving) return;\n   506→\n   507→    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n   508→    const newContent = textarea.value;\n   509→    const filename = DIAGRAMS[idx].file;\n   510→    const indicator = document.getElementById(`md-indicator-${idx}`);\n   511→\n   512→    state.saving = true;\n   513→    indicator.textContent = 'Saving...';\n   514→    indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saving';\n   515→\n   516→    try {\n   517→        const resp = await fetch(\n   518→            `/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${filename}`,\n   519→            {\n   520→                method: 'PUT',\n   521→                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n   522→                body: JSON.stringify({ content: newContent }),\n   523→            }\n   524→        );\n   525→\n   526→        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`Save failed: ${resp.status}`);\n   527→\n   528→        indicator.textContent = 'Saved!';\n   529→        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saved';\n   530→\n   531→        // Update stored content\n   532→        diagramContents[filename] = newContent;\n   533→\n   534→        // Return to view mode after brief success indicator\n   535→        setTimeout(() => {\n   536→            const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n   537→            renderMarkdown(el, newContent, idx, filename);\n   538→            markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n   539→            updateEditButton(idx, false);\n   540→        }, 800);\n   541→\n   542→    } catch (err) {\n   543→        indicator.textContent = `Error: ${err.message}`;\n   544→        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator error';\n   545→        state.saving = false;\n   546→    }\n   547→}\n   548→```\n   549→\n   550→### 3.4 Editor Styles\n   551→\n   552→**File:** `vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` (or inline in architecture.html)\n   553→\n   554→```css\n   555→.md-editor-container {\n   556→    display: flex;\n   557→    flex-direction: column;\n   558→    height: 100%;\n   559→    min-height: 200px;\n   560→}\n   561→\n   562→.md-editor-toolbar {\n   563→    display: flex;\n   564→    align-items: center;\n   565→    gap: 8px;\n   566→    padding: 8px 12px;\n   567→    background: var(--surface-2);\n   568→    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n   569→}\n   570→\n   571→.md-editor {\n   572→    flex: 1;\n   573→    resize: vertical;\n   574→    min-height: 200px;\n   575→    padding: 16px;\n   576→    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace;\n   577→    font-size: 14px;\n   578→    line-height: 1.6;\n   579→    background: var(--surface-1);\n   580→    color: var(--text-primary);\n   581→    border: none;\n   582→    outline: none;\n   583→}\n   584→\n   585→.md-save-btn { color: #4ade80; }\n   586→.md-cancel-btn { color: #f87171; }\n   587→.md-save-indicator.saving { color: #facc15; }\n   588→.md-save-indicator.saved { color: #4ade80; }\n   589→.md-save-indicator.error { color: #f87171; }\n   590→\n   591→.markdown-content {\n   592→    padding: 16px;\n   593→    line-height: 1.7;\n   594→}\n   595→.markdown-content h1, .markdown-content h2, .markdown-content h3 {\n   596→    margin-top: 1.5em;\n   597→    margin-bottom: 0.5em;\n   598→}\n   599→.markdown-content pre {\n   600→    background: var(--surface-2);\n   601→    padding: 12px;\n   602→    border-radius: 6px;\n   603→    overflow-x: auto;\n   604→}\n   605→.markdown-content code {\n   606→    background: var(--surface-2);\n   607→    padding: 2px 6px;\n   608→    border-radius: 3px;\n   609→    font-size: 0.9em;\n   610→}\n   611→.markdown-content table {\n   612→    border-collapse: collapse;\n   613→    width: 100%;\n   614→}\n   615→.markdown-content th, .markdown-content td {\n   616→    border: 1px solid var(--border);\n   617→    padding: 8px 12px;\n   618→    text-align: left;\n   619→}\n   620→```\n   621→\n   622→### 3.5 Keyboard Shortcuts\n   623→\n   624→- `Ctrl+S` / `Cmd+S` in edit mode → Save\n   625→- `Escape` in edit mode → Cancel\n   626→\n   627→```javascript\n   628→document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n   629→    // Find any active markdown editor\n   630→    for (const [idx, state] of Object.entries(markdownEditState)) {\n   631→        if (state.editing) {\n   632→            if ((e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) && e.key === 's') {\n   633→                e.preventDefault();\n   634→                saveMarkdown(parseInt(idx));\n   635→            } else if (e.key === 'Escape') {\n   636→                e.preventDefault();\n   637→                cancelMarkdownEdit(parseInt(idx));\n   638→            }\n   639→        }\n   640→    }\n   641→});\n   642→```\n   643→\n   644→### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 3)\n   645→\n   646→- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML with GFM support (tables, code blocks, task lists)\n   647→- [ ] Edit button appears only on markdown-type diagram cards\n   648→- [ ] Clicking edit switches to textarea with raw content\n   649→- [ ] Save writes content to disk via PUT API and returns to rendered view\n   650→- [ ] Cancel discards changes and returns to rendered view\n   651→- [ ] Save indicator shows progress (saving → saved → hidden)\n   652→- [ ] Save failure shows error message\n   653→- [ ] Ctrl+S saves, Escape cancels\n   654→- [ ] Content stored in `diagramContents` is updated after successful save\n   655→\n   656→---\n   657→\n   658→## Phase 4: Template & Watcher Integration\n   659→\n   660→**Priority:** MEDIUM\n   661→**Depends on:** Phases 1-3\n   662→**Estimated Complexity:** Low-Medium\n   663→\n   664→### 4.1 Pass Manifest Type to Renderers\n   665→\n   666→**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n   667→\n   668→Update `loadDiagrams()` to pass the manifest `type` field:\n   669→\n   670→```javascript\n   671→async function loadDiagrams() {\n   672→    for (let i = 0; i < DIAGRAMS.length; i++) {\n   673→        const diagram = DIAGRAMS[i];\n   674→        const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${diagram.file}`);\n   675→        const content = await resp.text();\n   676→        diagramContents[diagram.file] = content;\n   677→\n   678→        const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${i}`);\n   679→        renderDiagramContent(el, diagram.file, content, i, diagram.type);  // Pass type!\n   680→    }\n   681→}\n   682→```\n   683→\n   684→### 4.2 Conditionally Show Edit Button in Card Header\n   685→\n   686→When building diagram cards (JavaScript, not Jinja2), check the diagram type:\n   687→\n   688→```javascript\n   689→function buildDiagramCard(diagram, idx) {\n   690→    // ... existing card structure ...\n   691→\n   692→    const editButton = diagram.type === 'markdown'\n   693→        ? `<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Edit\">✎</button>`\n   694→        : '';\n   695→\n   696→    // Insert into card header alongside zoom controls\n   697→}\n   698→```\n   699→\n   700→### 4.3 Update Diagram Watcher Manifest Auto-Update\n   701→\n   702→**File:** `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n   703→\n   704→The `_update_manifest_sync()` function currently scans for `.mmd` and `.drawio` only. Update to scan all supported extensions and set the `type` field correctly:\n   705→\n   706→```python\n   707→EXT_TO_TYPE = {\n   708→    \".mmd\": \"mermaid\",\n   709→    \".drawio\": \"drawio\",\n   710→    \".puml\": \"plantuml\",\n   711→    \".d2\": \"d2\",\n   712→    \".dot\": \"graphviz\",\n   713→    \".md\": \"markdown\",\n   714→}\n   715→\n   716→# In _update_manifest_sync():\n   717→for f in sorted(arch_dir.iterdir()):\n   718→    if f.suffix in EXT_TO_TYPE and not f.name.startswith(\"_\"):\n   719→        file_type = EXT_TO_TYPE[f.suffix]\n   720→        diagram_type = _detect_diagram_type(f) if file_type == \"mermaid\" else \"custom\"\n   721→        entry = {\n   722→            \"name\": f.stem.replace(\"-\", \" \").replace(\"_\", \" \").title(),\n   723→            \"file\": f.name,\n   724→            \"type\": file_type,\n   725→            \"diagramType\": diagram_type,\n   726→            \"description\": f\"Auto-detected {file_type} diagram\",\n   727→        }\n   728→        diagrams.append(entry)\n   729→```\n   730→\n   731→### 4.4 CDN Script Loading\n   732→\n   733→**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n   734→\n   735→Add CDN scripts in the `<head>` section. WASM-based renderers should lazy-load, but the encoder library can be loaded eagerly (small):\n   736→\n   737→```html\n   738→<!-- PlantUML encoder (small, ~10KB) -->\n   739→<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder@1.4.0/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js\"></script>\n   740→\n   741→<!-- D2 and Graphviz loaded lazily by their respective renderers -->\n   742→```\n   743→\n   744→For `@viz-js/viz`, the CDN approach:\n   745→```html\n   746→<!-- Loaded dynamically in renderGraphviz() -->\n   747→<!-- https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@viz-js/viz@3/lib/viz-standalone.js -->\n   748→```\n   749→\n   750→### 4.5 PlantUML Server URL Injection\n   751→\n   752→The architecture page template needs to know the PlantUML server URL. Options:\n   753→\n   754→**Option A (recommended):** Pass from server context:\n   755→```python\n   756→# In architecture_viewer_page():\n   757→from server.services.settings_service import get_settings\n   758→settings = get_settings()\n   759→plantuml_url = settings.get(\"plantuml_server_url\", \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\")\n   760→```\n   761→\n   762→And in the template:\n   763→```html\n   764→<script>\n   765→    const PLANTUML_SERVER_URL = {{ plantuml_url | tojson }};\n   766→</script>\n   767→```\n   768→\n   769→**Option B:** Fetch from settings API client-side. Less efficient.\n   770→\n   771→### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 4)\n   772→\n   773→- [ ] All 6 diagram types dispatch to their correct renderer\n   774→- [ ] Edit button only appears on markdown cards\n   775→- [ ] Watcher detects changes in all 6 file types\n   776→- [ ] Manifest auto-update correctly assigns type from extension\n   777→- [ ] PlantUML server URL passed from settings to frontend\n   778→- [ ] CDN scripts loaded (eagerly for small libs, lazily for WASM)\n   779→\n   780→---\n   781→\n   782→## Phase 5: Tests\n   783→\n   784→**Priority:** HIGH — Must validate security and correctness\n   785→**Depends on:** Phases 1-4\n   786→**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n   787→\n   788→### 5.1 PUT Endpoint Tests\n   789→\n   790→**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n   791→\n   792→```python\n   793→class TestArchWriteAPI:\n   794→    def test_put_markdown_file_success(self, api_env):\n   795→        \"\"\"PUT .md file writes content and returns 200.\"\"\"\n   796→\n   797→    def test_put_non_markdown_file_rejected(self, api_env):\n   798→        \"\"\"PUT .mmd file returns 400.\"\"\"\n   799→\n   800→    def test_put_path_traversal_blocked(self, api_env):\n   801→        \"\"\"PUT ../../evil.md returns 400.\"\"\"\n   802→\n   803→    def test_put_project_not_found(self, api_env):\n   804→        \"\"\"PUT to nonexistent project returns 404.\"\"\"\n   805→\n   806→    def test_put_no_arch_directory(self, api_env):\n   807→        \"\"\"PUT to feature without arch/ returns 400.\"\"\"\n   808→```\n   809→\n   810→### 5.2 ProgressService Write Tests\n   811→\n   812→**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n   813→\n   814→```python\n   815→class TestProgressServiceWrite:\n   816→    def test_write_arch_file_md_success(self, tmp_path):\n   817→        \"\"\"write_arch_file() writes .md content to arch/.\"\"\"\n   818→\n   819→    def test_write_arch_file_mmd_rejected(self, tmp_path):\n   820→        \"\"\"write_arch_file() rejects .mmd files.\"\"\"\n   821→\n   822→    def test_write_arch_file_path_traversal(self, tmp_path):\n   823→        \"\"\"write_arch_file() blocks ../evil path.\"\"\"\n   824→\n   825→    def test_write_arch_file_no_arch_dir(self, tmp_path):\n   826→        \"\"\"write_arch_file() returns False when arch/ doesn't exist.\"\"\"\n   827→```\n   828→\n   829→### 5.3 Schema Validation Tests\n   830→\n   831→**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n   832→\n   833→```python\n   834→class TestExtendedSchemaValidation:\n   835→    def test_arch_schema_accepts_plantuml_type(self):\n   836→    def test_arch_schema_accepts_d2_type(self):\n   837→    def test_arch_schema_accepts_graphviz_type(self):\n   838→    def test_arch_schema_accepts_markdown_type(self):\n   839→    def test_arch_schema_rejects_unknown_type(self):\n   840→```\n   841→\n   842→### 5.4 Content-Type Tests\n   843→\n   844→```python\n   845→class TestContentTypes:\n   846→    def test_get_puml_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n   847→    def test_get_d2_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n   848→    def test_get_dot_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n   849→    def test_get_md_returns_text_markdown(self, api_env):\n   850→```\n   851→\n   852→### 5.5 Diagram Watcher Extension Tests\n   853→\n   854→**File:** `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py`\n   855→\n   856→```python\n   857→class TestExtendedFileTypes:\n   858→    def test_watches_puml_files(self):\n   859→    def test_watches_d2_files(self):\n   860→    def test_watches_dot_files(self):\n   861→    def test_watches_md_files(self):\n   862→    def test_manifest_update_assigns_correct_type(self):\n   863→```\n   864→\n   865→### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 5)\n   866→\n   867→- [ ] All PUT endpoint tests pass (including security: path traversal, extension whitelist)\n   868→- [ ] All schema validation tests pass for 6 types\n   869→- [ ] Content-type tests pass for all new extensions\n   870→- [ ] Watcher tests pass for all 6 file types\n   871→- [ ] No regressions in existing 139 tests\n   872→\n   873→---\n   874→\n   875→## Phase 6: Documentation & Skill Updates\n   876→\n   877→**Priority:** LOW\n   878→**Depends on:** All prior phases\n   879→**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n   880→\n   881→### 6.1 Update Plan Skill SKILL.md\n   882→\n   883→**File:** `vista/skills/plan/SKILL.md`\n   884→\n   885→Update Step 3 (architecture generation) to mention all supported formats:\n   886→- Default: Mermaid (.mmd) for all diagram types\n   887→- Optional: PlantUML (.puml) for detailed UML class/sequence diagrams\n   888→- Optional: D2 (.d2) for architecture diagrams with auto-layout\n   889→- Optional: Graphviz (.dot) for dependency graphs\n   890→- Optional: Markdown (.md) for prose documentation (design rationale, ADRs)\n   891→\n   892→### 6.2 Update Diagrams Skill\n   893→\n   894→**File:** `vista/skills/diagrams/SKILL.md` (if exists)\n   895→\n   896→Document the expanded format support.\n   897→\n   898→### 6.3 Update arch-directory.md Spec\n   899→\n   900→**File:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/specs/arch-directory.md`\n   901→\n   902→Update to reflect the expanded type enum, new file extensions, and markdown editing capability.\n   903→\n   904→### 6.4 Update rendering-pipeline.md Spec\n   905→\n   906→**File:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/specs/rendering-pipeline.md`\n   907→\n   908→Update renderer table to include all 6 renderers.\n   909→\n   910→---\n   911→\n   912→## Risk Assessment\n   913→\n   914→| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n   915→|------|-----------|--------|------------|\n   916→| D2 WASM not available as browser-compatible package | Medium | Medium | Fall back to raw source display with syntax highlighting |\n   917→| PlantUML server rate limiting | Low | Low | Self-hosted server option in settings |\n   918→| @viz-js/viz WASM too large (>5MB) | Low | Medium | Lazy load only when Graphviz diagram appears |\n   919→| Draw.io viewer URL encoding exceeds limits for large files | Medium | Medium | Use postMessage API instead of URL params |\n   920→| Markdown editor unsaved changes lost on navigation | Low | Medium | Add `beforeunload` warning when editing |\n   921→\n   922→---\n   923→\n   924→## Implementation Order (Recommended)\n   925→\n   926→1. **Phase 1** — Backend foundation (schema, PUT endpoint, watcher extensions, settings)\n   927→2. **Phase 2** — Renderer infrastructure (dispatch refactor + all 6 renderers)\n   928→3. **Phase 3** — Markdown editor (edit mode, save/cancel, keyboard shortcuts)\n   929→4. **Phase 4** — Template integration (type passing, CDN loading, watcher updates)\n   930→5. **Phase 5** — Tests (PUT security, schema, content types, watcher)\n   931→6. **Phase 6** — Documentation\n   932→\n   933→**Estimated total:** ~3-4 build iterations\n   934→\n   935→---\n   936→\n   937→## Files Summary\n   938→\n   939→### Files to Modify\n   940→\n   941→| File | Changes |\n   942→|------|---------|\n   943→| `vista/templates/arch-schema.json` | Extend `type` enum: add `plantuml`, `d2`, `graphviz`, `markdown` |\n   944→| `vista/server/services/progress_service.py` | Add `write_arch_file()` method |\n   945→| `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` | Add PUT endpoint, update content-type mapping |\n   946→| `vista/server/views/architecture.html` | Refactor renderer dispatch, add 5 new renderers, add markdown editor |\n   947→| `vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` | Add markdown editor styles |\n   948→| `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py` | Extend `WATCH_EXTENSIONS`, update manifest type detection |\n   949→| `vista/tests/test_architecture.py` | Add ~15 new tests for PUT, schema, content types |\n   950→| `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py` | Add ~5 new tests for extended file types |\n   951→\n   952→### Files to Create\n   953→\n   954→None — all changes are modifications to existing files.\n   955→\n   956→### Settings Changes\n   957→\n   958→| Setting | Value | Location |\n   959→|---------|-------|----------|\n   960→| `plantuml_server_url` | `\"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\"` | `~/.vista/settings.json` |\n   961→\n   962→---\n   963→\n   964→## Spec Versions\n   965→\n   966→| Spec File | Latest Changelog Date | Notes |\n   967→|-----------|-----------------------|-------|\n   968→| `specs/arch-directory.md` | 2026-02-15 | `diagramType` enum and category aligned with arch-schema.json |\n   969→| `specs/rendering-pipeline.md` | 2026-02-15 | Draw.io status clarified, acceptance criteria updated |\n   970→| `specs/chat-review.md` | 2026-02-15 | Protocol-native streaming alignment |\n   971→| `specs/migration-cleanup.md` | 2026-02-15 | All acceptance criteria verified complete |\n   972→| `domain-requirements.md` (Expansion) | 2026-02-15 | Multi-format diagrams, markdown editing, type system updates |\n   973→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e23a7aa2-5923-4855-9cc2-f80458cf6b25","uuid":"6765cf20-e755-4698-8717-175624bcbda1","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/.vista/ralph/diagram-repr-spec-planning/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Multi-Format Diagram Support & Markdown Editing\n\n**Status:** PLANNING — New feature expansion for diagram_representations\n**Created:** 2026-02-15\n**Spec Source:** `domain-requirements.md` Expansion section (added 2026-02-15)\n**Parent Feature:** `.vista/features/diagram_representations/`\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\nThe existing diagram_representations feature is largely delivered (Phases 1-4 complete, Phase 5 partial). The domain-requirements.md has been expanded with three new areas:\n\n1. **Multi-Format Rendering** — PlantUML (.puml), D2 (.d2), Graphviz (.dot), Markdown (.md)\n2. **Markdown Inline Editing** — View/edit toggle, save to disk via PUT API, cancel/discard\n3. **Manifest & Type System Updates** — Extended type enum, renderer dispatch, file extension mapping\n\nThis plan covers implementing these expansion requirements on top of the existing codebase.\n\n---\n\n## Current State Assessment\n\n### What Exists (Working)\n\n| Component | Status | Location |\n|-----------|--------|----------|\n| Mermaid rendering | Complete | `architecture.html:1289-1307` — `mermaid.render()` |\n| Renderer dispatch | Partial — only `.mmd` check + fallback `<pre>` | `architecture.html:1288-1311` |\n| `_arch.json` schema | `type` enum: `[\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]` only | `arch-schema.json:29` |\n| Diagram watcher | Watches `.mmd` and `.drawio` only | `diagram_watcher.py:26` — `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` |\n| Manifest auto-update | Detects diagram type for mermaid files only | `diagram_watcher.py:102-118` |\n| API: GET manifest | Complete | `architecture.py:15-26` |\n| API: GET file | Complete (read-only, text/plain or application/xml) | `architecture.py:29-48` |\n| API: PUT file | **Does not exist** | Needed for markdown save |\n| Path traversal protection | Complete | `progress_service.py:80-92` |\n| Pan/zoom per diagram | Complete | `architecture.html:1323-1375` |\n| Settings file | No `plantuml_server_url` field | `~/.vista/settings.json` |\n\n### What Needs to Change\n\n1. **arch-schema.json** — Extend `type` enum from 2 to 6 values\n2. **diagram_watcher.py** — Extend `WATCH_EXTENSIONS` and `_detect_diagram_type()` for new formats\n3. **progress_service.py** — Add `write_arch_file()` method for markdown save\n4. **architecture.py** — Add `PUT` endpoint, update content-type mapping for new extensions\n5. **architecture.html** — Add 4 new renderers + markdown edit mode\n6. **Settings** — Add `plantuml_server_url` default\n7. **Tests** — Cover all new renderers, PUT endpoint, security\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Schema & Backend Foundation\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — All other phases depend on this\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n\n### 1.1 Extend arch-schema.json Type Enum\n\n**File:** `vista/templates/arch-schema.json`\n\nChange line 29:\n```json\n\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\"]\n```\nTo:\n```json\n\"enum\": [\"mermaid\", \"drawio\", \"plantuml\", \"d2\", \"graphviz\", \"markdown\"]\n```\n\nNo other schema changes needed — `diagramType` enum already has `\"custom\"` as a catch-all for non-Mermaid diagrams. The `category` field is already optional with `architecture` and `tdd` values.\n\n### 1.2 Add write_arch_file() to ProgressService\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n\nAdd new static method after `read_arch_file()`:\n\n```python\n@staticmethod\ndef write_arch_file(project_path: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, content: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Write content to a diagram file in arch/ with path traversal prevention.\n\n    Only allows writing to files with extensions: .md\n    Returns True on success, False on validation failure.\n    \"\"\"\n    WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS = {\".md\"}\n\n    safe_name = Path(filename).name\n    if safe_name != filename or \"..\" in filename:\n        return False\n\n    if Path(safe_name).suffix not in WRITABLE_EXTENSIONS:\n        return False\n\n    arch_dir = Path(project_path) / \".vista\" / \"features\" / feature_name / \"arch\"\n    target = arch_dir / safe_name\n\n    try:\n        target.resolve().relative_to(arch_dir.resolve())\n    except ValueError:\n        return False\n\n    if not arch_dir.exists():\n        return False\n\n    target.write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return True\n```\n\n**Key decisions:**\n- **Writable extensions restricted to `.md` only** — Diagram files (.mmd, .puml, .d2, .dot, .drawio) are NOT writable through this API. Only markdown documentation files are editable inline.\n- **Same path traversal protection** as `read_arch_file()`.\n- **File must be in an existing arch/ directory** — won't create directories.\n\n### 1.3 Add PUT Endpoint for File Writing\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py`\n\nAdd new route:\n\n```python\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nclass FileContent(BaseModel):\n    content: str\n\n@router.put(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/features/{feature_name}/arch/{filename}\")\nasync def put_arch_file(project_id: str, feature_name: str, filename: str, body: FileContent):\n    \"\"\"Write content to a markdown file in arch/.\"\"\"\n    project = ProjectService.get_by_id(project_id)\n    if not project:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Project not found\")\n\n    success = ProgressService.write_arch_file(project.path, feature_name, filename, body.content)\n    if not success:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Cannot write to this file\")\n\n    return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"filename\": filename}\n```\n\n### 1.4 Update Content-Type Mapping in GET Endpoint\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/architecture.py` — `get_arch_file()` function\n\nUpdate the content-type section (lines 41-46):\n\n```python\next = filename.rsplit(\".\", 1)[-1] if \".\" in filename else \"\"\nCONTENT_TYPES = {\n    \"mmd\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"drawio\": \"application/xml\",\n    \"puml\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"d2\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"dot\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"md\": \"text/markdown\",\n}\nmedia_type = CONTENT_TYPES.get(ext, \"text/plain\")\n```\n\n### 1.5 Add PlantUML Server URL to Settings\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/settings_service.py` (or wherever defaults are defined)\n\nAdd default `plantuml_server_url` to settings schema:\n```json\n\"plantuml_server_url\": \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\"\n```\n\n**Also update:** `~/.vista/settings.json` default initialization if a settings template exists.\n\n**Server-side API:** Add a `GET /api/settings/plantuml-server` endpoint (or include in existing settings response) so the frontend can discover the configured PlantUML server URL.\n\n### 1.6 Extend Diagram Watcher Extensions\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n\nUpdate `_DiagramEventHandler` class:\n\n```python\nWATCH_EXTENSIONS = {\".mmd\", \".drawio\", \".puml\", \".d2\", \".dot\", \".md\"}\n```\n\nUpdate `_detect_diagram_type()` to return type based on extension (not just mermaid content parsing):\n\n```python\ndef _detect_file_type(path: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Detect diagram type from file extension.\"\"\"\n    EXT_TO_TYPE = {\n        \".mmd\": \"mermaid\",\n        \".drawio\": \"drawio\",\n        \".puml\": \"plantuml\",\n        \".d2\": \"d2\",\n        \".dot\": \"graphviz\",\n        \".md\": \"markdown\",\n    }\n    return EXT_TO_TYPE.get(path.suffix.lower(), \"mermaid\")\n```\n\nUpdate `_update_manifest_sync()` to use `_detect_file_type()` for the `type` field and retain `_detect_diagram_type()` for the `diagramType` field (mermaid subtypes). For non-mermaid formats, set `diagramType: \"custom\"`.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 1)\n\n- [ ] `arch-schema.json` validates manifests with all 6 type values\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` writes `.md` files successfully\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns 400 for non-`.md` files\n- [ ] `PUT /api/.../arch/{filename}` blocks path traversal attempts\n- [ ] `GET /api/.../arch/{filename}` returns correct Content-Type for all 6 extensions\n- [ ] Diagram watcher detects changes in all 6 file types\n- [ ] Manifest auto-update correctly identifies file types by extension\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Client-Side Renderer Infrastructure\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Core rendering dispatch\n**Depends on:** Phase 1\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n\n### 2.1 Refactor Renderer Dispatch\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\nCurrently, `renderDiagramContent()` (line 1288) checks `filename.endsWith('.mmd')` and falls back to `<pre>`. Refactor to a renderer map pattern:\n\n```javascript\nconst RENDERERS = {\n    mermaid:  renderMermaid,\n    plantuml: renderPlantUML,\n    d2:       renderD2,\n    graphviz: renderGraphviz,\n    drawio:   renderDrawio,\n    markdown: renderMarkdown,\n};\n\nfunction renderDiagramContent(el, filename, content, idx, diagramType) {\n    // diagramType is the 'type' field from manifest (mermaid, plantuml, etc.)\n    // NOT diagramType (flowchart, sequence, etc.)\n    const renderer = RENDERERS[diagramType];\n    if (renderer) {\n        return renderer(el, content, idx, filename);\n    }\n    // Unknown type fallback\n    el.innerHTML = `<pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n}\n```\n\n**Change needed:** The template must pass the manifest `type` field to `renderDiagramContent()`. Currently, `loadDiagrams()` only passes filename/content/idx. Update to also pass `diagram.type` from the manifest `DIAGRAMS` array.\n\n### 2.2 Mermaid Renderer (Existing — No Changes)\n\nStays as-is: `mermaid.render(id, content)` → SVG injection → click handlers for element selection.\n\n### 2.3 PlantUML Renderer\n\n**Dependencies:** `plantuml-encoder` library (CDN or bundled)\n\n**Rendering flow:**\n1. Encode PlantUML source to deflate+base64 using `plantuml-encoder` algorithm\n2. Construct URL: `${PLANTUML_SERVER_URL}/svg/${encoded}`\n3. Fetch SVG from PlantUML server\n4. Inject SVG into card container\n\n**Library loading:** CDN — `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js`\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nasync function renderPlantUML(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const encoded = plantumlEncoder.encode(content);\n        const serverUrl = PLANTUML_SERVER_URL;  // From server template var or settings API\n        const svgUrl = `${serverUrl}/svg/${encoded}`;\n        const resp = await fetch(svgUrl);\n        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`PlantUML server error: ${resp.status}`);\n        const svg = await resp.text();\n        el.innerHTML = svg;\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>PlantUML render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Error handling:**\n- Server unreachable → Show error + raw source as fallback\n- Invalid syntax → PlantUML server returns error image; detect via content-type or error body\n\n**Template variable:** Pass `PLANTUML_SERVER_URL` from server context (read from settings).\n\n### 2.4 D2 Renderer\n\n**Dependencies:** `@terrastruct/d2` WASM package\n\n**Loading strategy:** Lazy-load — only fetch WASM when a D2 diagram appears.\n\n**Implementation approach:**\n```javascript\nlet d2Module = null;\n\nasync function loadD2() {\n    if (d2Module) return d2Module;\n    // Dynamic import from CDN\n    d2Module = await import('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@anthropic-ai/d2-wasm/...');\n    return d2Module;\n}\n\nasync function renderD2(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const d2 = await loadD2();\n        const svg = await d2.compile(content, { layout: 'dagre' });\n        el.innerHTML = svg;\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>D2 render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** D2 WASM availability needs verification. If `@terrastruct/d2` doesn't provide a browser-compatible WASM, an alternative approach is needed:\n- **Fallback option A:** Server-side rendering via `d2` CLI (similar to how PlantUML uses a server)\n- **Fallback option B:** Use a simpler D2 rendering library if available\n- **Minimum viable:** Show raw D2 source with syntax highlighting as placeholder, with a note that D2 rendering requires server-side support\n\n### 2.5 Graphviz Renderer\n\n**Dependencies:** `@viz-js/viz` WASM package\n\n**Loading strategy:** Lazy-load — only fetch WASM when a Graphviz diagram appears.\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nlet vizInstance = null;\n\nasync function loadViz() {\n    if (vizInstance) return vizInstance;\n    const { instance } = await import('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@viz-js/viz/...');\n    vizInstance = await instance();\n    return vizInstance;\n}\n\nasync function renderGraphviz(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const viz = await loadViz();\n        const svg = viz.renderSVGElement(content, { engine: 'dot' });\n        el.innerHTML = '';\n        el.appendChild(svg);\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>Graphviz render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Engine selection:** Default to `dot` layout engine. Could expose engine selection per-diagram via a `layoutEngine` field in manifest (future enhancement — not in scope now).\n\n### 2.6 Draw.io Renderer (Existing Gap — Implement Now)\n\n**Current state:** Falls through to `<pre>` tag with escaped XML content.\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nfunction renderDrawio(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        // Use Draw.io's public viewer with inline XML\n        const encoded = encodeURIComponent(content);\n        const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');\n        iframe.src = `https://viewer.diagrams.net/?highlight=0000ff&nav=1&title=${filename}#R${encoded}`;\n        iframe.style.width = '100%';\n        iframe.style.height = '500px';\n        iframe.style.border = 'none';\n        iframe.setAttribute('sandbox', 'allow-scripts allow-same-origin');\n        el.innerHTML = '';\n        el.appendChild(iframe);\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"diagram-error\">\n            <p>Draw.io render error: ${escapeHtml(err.message)}</p>\n            <pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>\n        </div>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Alternative:** For large `.drawio` files, the URL-encoded approach may exceed URL limits. Use `postMessage` API instead:\n1. Create iframe pointing to `https://viewer.diagrams.net/`\n2. Send diagram XML via `iframe.contentWindow.postMessage()` after iframe loads\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 2)\n\n- [ ] Mermaid diagrams continue to render correctly (no regression)\n- [ ] PlantUML diagrams render as SVG via server fetch\n- [ ] D2 diagrams render via WASM (or show fallback with raw source)\n- [ ] Graphviz diagrams render via `@viz-js/viz` WASM\n- [ ] Draw.io diagrams render in iframe (not raw XML)\n- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML\n- [ ] Each renderer shows error + raw source on failure\n- [ ] WASM modules load lazily (only when diagram type appears on page)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Markdown Renderer & Inline Editor\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Key new user interaction\n**Depends on:** Phase 1 (PUT endpoint), Phase 2 (renderer infrastructure)\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium-High\n\n### 3.1 Markdown Renderer\n\n**Library:** `marked.js` — already loaded in architecture.html (line 7, used for chat streaming).\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\nfunction renderMarkdown(el, content, idx, filename) {\n    try {\n        const html = marked.parse(content);\n        el.innerHTML = `<div class=\"markdown-content\">${html}</div>`;\n        // Store original content for edit mode\n        el.dataset.rawContent = content;\n        el.dataset.filename = filename;\n        el.dataset.idx = idx;\n    } catch (err) {\n        el.innerHTML = `<pre>${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3.2 Edit Button on Markdown Cards\n\nFor diagram cards where `type === \"markdown\"`, add a pencil icon button in the card header (alongside existing zoom controls).\n\n**Placement:** In the diagram card header template (around line 1016-1041 in architecture.html), conditionally add:\n\n```html\n{% if diagram.type == 'markdown' %}\n<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(idx)\" title=\"Edit markdown\">\n    ✎\n</button>\n{% endif %}\n```\n\n**Note:** Since diagrams are rendered client-side from the DIAGRAMS array, the edit button must be added in JavaScript during card construction, not in Jinja2. Check the type from the manifest entry.\n\n### 3.3 Edit Mode State Machine\n\n**States:** `view` → `editing` → `saving` → `view`\n\n```javascript\nconst markdownEditState = {};  // idx -> { editing: bool, saving: bool, originalContent: string }\n\nfunction toggleMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx] || { editing: false };\n\n    if (state.editing) {\n        cancelMarkdownEdit(idx);\n    } else {\n        enterMarkdownEdit(idx);\n    }\n}\n\nfunction enterMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n    const content = el.dataset.rawContent || diagramContents[DIAGRAMS[idx].file];\n\n    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: true, saving: false, originalContent: content };\n\n    el.innerHTML = `\n        <div class=\"md-editor-container\">\n            <div class=\"md-editor-toolbar\">\n                <button class=\"md-save-btn\" onclick=\"saveMarkdown(${idx})\" title=\"Save\">✓ Save</button>\n                <button class=\"md-cancel-btn\" onclick=\"cancelMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Cancel\">✕ Cancel</button>\n                <span class=\"md-save-indicator\" id=\"md-indicator-${idx}\"></span>\n            </div>\n            <textarea class=\"md-editor\" id=\"md-textarea-${idx}\" spellcheck=\"false\">${escapeHtml(content)}</textarea>\n        </div>\n    `;\n\n    // Focus and auto-resize\n    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n    textarea.focus();\n    autoResizeTextarea(textarea);\n    textarea.addEventListener('input', () => autoResizeTextarea(textarea));\n\n    // Update card header button state\n    updateEditButton(idx, true);\n}\n\nfunction cancelMarkdownEdit(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n    if (!state) return;\n\n    // Re-render the markdown view\n    const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n    renderMarkdown(el, state.originalContent, idx, DIAGRAMS[idx].file);\n\n    markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n    updateEditButton(idx, false);\n}\n\nasync function saveMarkdown(idx) {\n    const state = markdownEditState[idx];\n    if (!state || state.saving) return;\n\n    const textarea = document.getElementById(`md-textarea-${idx}`);\n    const newContent = textarea.value;\n    const filename = DIAGRAMS[idx].file;\n    const indicator = document.getElementById(`md-indicator-${idx}`);\n\n    state.saving = true;\n    indicator.textContent = 'Saving...';\n    indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saving';\n\n    try {\n        const resp = await fetch(\n            `/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${filename}`,\n            {\n                method: 'PUT',\n                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n                body: JSON.stringify({ content: newContent }),\n            }\n        );\n\n        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`Save failed: ${resp.status}`);\n\n        indicator.textContent = 'Saved!';\n        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator saved';\n\n        // Update stored content\n        diagramContents[filename] = newContent;\n\n        // Return to view mode after brief success indicator\n        setTimeout(() => {\n            const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${idx}`);\n            renderMarkdown(el, newContent, idx, filename);\n            markdownEditState[idx] = { editing: false };\n            updateEditButton(idx, false);\n        }, 800);\n\n    } catch (err) {\n        indicator.textContent = `Error: ${err.message}`;\n        indicator.className = 'md-save-indicator error';\n        state.saving = false;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3.4 Editor Styles\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/static/arch-chat.css` (or inline in architecture.html)\n\n```css\n.md-editor-container {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    height: 100%;\n    min-height: 200px;\n}\n\n.md-editor-toolbar {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 8px;\n    padding: 8px 12px;\n    background: var(--surface-2);\n    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n}\n\n.md-editor {\n    flex: 1;\n    resize: vertical;\n    min-height: 200px;\n    padding: 16px;\n    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    background: var(--surface-1);\n    color: var(--text-primary);\n    border: none;\n    outline: none;\n}\n\n.md-save-btn { color: #4ade80; }\n.md-cancel-btn { color: #f87171; }\n.md-save-indicator.saving { color: #facc15; }\n.md-save-indicator.saved { color: #4ade80; }\n.md-save-indicator.error { color: #f87171; }\n\n.markdown-content {\n    padding: 16px;\n    line-height: 1.7;\n}\n.markdown-content h1, .markdown-content h2, .markdown-content h3 {\n    margin-top: 1.5em;\n    margin-bottom: 0.5em;\n}\n.markdown-content pre {\n    background: var(--surface-2);\n    padding: 12px;\n    border-radius: 6px;\n    overflow-x: auto;\n}\n.markdown-content code {\n    background: var(--surface-2);\n    padding: 2px 6px;\n    border-radius: 3px;\n    font-size: 0.9em;\n}\n.markdown-content table {\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    width: 100%;\n}\n.markdown-content th, .markdown-content td {\n    border: 1px solid var(--border);\n    padding: 8px 12px;\n    text-align: left;\n}\n```\n\n### 3.5 Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+S` / `Cmd+S` in edit mode → Save\n- `Escape` in edit mode → Cancel\n\n```javascript\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n    // Find any active markdown editor\n    for (const [idx, state] of Object.entries(markdownEditState)) {\n        if (state.editing) {\n            if ((e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) && e.key === 's') {\n                e.preventDefault();\n                saveMarkdown(parseInt(idx));\n            } else if (e.key === 'Escape') {\n                e.preventDefault();\n                cancelMarkdownEdit(parseInt(idx));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n});\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 3)\n\n- [ ] Markdown files render as formatted HTML with GFM support (tables, code blocks, task lists)\n- [ ] Edit button appears only on markdown-type diagram cards\n- [ ] Clicking edit switches to textarea with raw content\n- [ ] Save writes content to disk via PUT API and returns to rendered view\n- [ ] Cancel discards changes and returns to rendered view\n- [ ] Save indicator shows progress (saving → saved → hidden)\n- [ ] Save failure shows error message\n- [ ] Ctrl+S saves, Escape cancels\n- [ ] Content stored in `diagramContents` is updated after successful save\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Template & Watcher Integration\n\n**Priority:** MEDIUM\n**Depends on:** Phases 1-3\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low-Medium\n\n### 4.1 Pass Manifest Type to Renderers\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\nUpdate `loadDiagrams()` to pass the manifest `type` field:\n\n```javascript\nasync function loadDiagrams() {\n    for (let i = 0; i < DIAGRAMS.length; i++) {\n        const diagram = DIAGRAMS[i];\n        const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/features/${FEATURE_NAME}/arch/${diagram.file}`);\n        const content = await resp.text();\n        diagramContents[diagram.file] = content;\n\n        const el = document.getElementById(`diagram-viewport-${i}`);\n        renderDiagramContent(el, diagram.file, content, i, diagram.type);  // Pass type!\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 4.2 Conditionally Show Edit Button in Card Header\n\nWhen building diagram cards (JavaScript, not Jinja2), check the diagram type:\n\n```javascript\nfunction buildDiagramCard(diagram, idx) {\n    // ... existing card structure ...\n\n    const editButton = diagram.type === 'markdown'\n        ? `<button class=\"md-edit-btn\" onclick=\"toggleMarkdownEdit(${idx})\" title=\"Edit\">✎</button>`\n        : '';\n\n    // Insert into card header alongside zoom controls\n}\n```\n\n### 4.3 Update Diagram Watcher Manifest Auto-Update\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n\nThe `_update_manifest_sync()` function currently scans for `.mmd` and `.drawio` only. Update to scan all supported extensions and set the `type` field correctly:\n\n```python\nEXT_TO_TYPE = {\n    \".mmd\": \"mermaid\",\n    \".drawio\": \"drawio\",\n    \".puml\": \"plantuml\",\n    \".d2\": \"d2\",\n    \".dot\": \"graphviz\",\n    \".md\": \"markdown\",\n}\n\n# In _update_manifest_sync():\nfor f in sorted(arch_dir.iterdir()):\n    if f.suffix in EXT_TO_TYPE and not f.name.startswith(\"_\"):\n        file_type = EXT_TO_TYPE[f.suffix]\n        diagram_type = _detect_diagram_type(f) if file_type == \"mermaid\" else \"custom\"\n        entry = {\n            \"name\": f.stem.replace(\"-\", \" \").replace(\"_\", \" \").title(),\n            \"file\": f.name,\n            \"type\": file_type,\n            \"diagramType\": diagram_type,\n            \"description\": f\"Auto-detected {file_type} diagram\",\n        }\n        diagrams.append(entry)\n```\n\n### 4.4 CDN Script Loading\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/architecture.html`\n\nAdd CDN scripts in the `<head>` section. WASM-based renderers should lazy-load, but the encoder library can be loaded eagerly (small):\n\n```html\n<!-- PlantUML encoder (small, ~10KB) -->\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/plantuml-encoder@1.4.0/dist/plantuml-encoder.min.js\"></script>\n\n<!-- D2 and Graphviz loaded lazily by their respective renderers -->\n```\n\nFor `@viz-js/viz`, the CDN approach:\n```html\n<!-- Loaded dynamically in renderGraphviz() -->\n<!-- https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@viz-js/viz@3/lib/viz-standalone.js -->\n```\n\n### 4.5 PlantUML Server URL Injection\n\nThe architecture page template needs to know the PlantUML server URL. Options:\n\n**Option A (recommended):** Pass from server context:\n```python\n# In architecture_viewer_page():\nfrom server.services.settings_service import get_settings\nsettings = get_settings()\nplantuml_url = settings.get(\"plantuml_server_url\", \"https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml\")\n```\n\nAnd in the template:\n```html\n<script>\n    const PLANTUML_SERVER_URL = {{ plantuml_url | tojson }};\n</script>\n```\n\n**Option B:** Fetch from settings API client-side. Less efficient.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 4)\n\n- [ ] All 6 diagram types dispatch to their correct renderer\n- [ ] Edit button only appears on markdown cards\n- [ ] Watcher detects changes in all 6 file types\n- [ ] Manifest auto-update correctly assigns type from extension\n- [ ] PlantUML server URL passed from settings to frontend\n- [ ] CDN scripts loaded (eagerly for small libs, lazily for WASM)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Tests\n\n**Priority:** HIGH — Must validate security and correctness\n**Depends on:** Phases 1-4\n**Estimated Complexity:** Medium\n\n### 5.1 PUT Endpoint Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestArchWriteAPI:\n    def test_put_markdown_file_success(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT .md file writes content and returns 200.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_non_markdown_file_rejected(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT .mmd file returns 400.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_path_traversal_blocked(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT ../../evil.md returns 400.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_project_not_found(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT to nonexistent project returns 404.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_put_no_arch_directory(self, api_env):\n        \"\"\"PUT to feature without arch/ returns 400.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### 5.2 ProgressService Write Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestProgressServiceWrite:\n    def test_write_arch_file_md_success(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() writes .md content to arch/.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_mmd_rejected(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() rejects .mmd files.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_path_traversal(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() blocks ../evil path.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_write_arch_file_no_arch_dir(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"write_arch_file() returns False when arch/ doesn't exist.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### 5.3 Schema Validation Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestExtendedSchemaValidation:\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_plantuml_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_d2_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_graphviz_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_accepts_markdown_type(self):\n    def test_arch_schema_rejects_unknown_type(self):\n```\n\n### 5.4 Content-Type Tests\n\n```python\nclass TestContentTypes:\n    def test_get_puml_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_d2_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_dot_returns_text_plain(self, api_env):\n    def test_get_md_returns_text_markdown(self, api_env):\n```\n\n### 5.5 Diagram Watcher Extension Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py`\n\n```python\nclass TestExtendedFileTypes:\n    def test_watches_puml_files(self):\n    def test_watches_d2_files(self):\n    def test_watches_dot_files(self):\n    def test_watches_md_files(self):\n    def test_manifest_update_assigns_correct_type(self):\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria (Phase 5)\n\n- [ ] All PUT endpoint tests pass (including security: path traversal, extension whitelist)\n- [ ] All schema validation tests pass for 6 types\n- [ ] Content-type tests pass for all new extensions\n- [ ] Watcher tests pass for all 6 file types\n- [ ] No regressions in existing 139 tests\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Documentation & Skill Updates\n\n**Priority:** LOW\n**Depends on:** All prior phases\n**Estimated Complexity:** Low\n\n### 6.1 Update Plan Skill SKILL.md\n\n**File:** `vista/skills/plan/SKILL.md`\n\nUpdate Step 3 (architecture generation) to mention all supported formats:\n- Default: Mermaid (.mmd) for all diagram types\n- Optional: PlantUML (.puml) for detailed UML class/sequence diagrams\n- Optional: D2 (.d2) for architecture diagrams with auto-layout\n- Optional: Graphviz (.dot) for dependency graphs\n- Optional: