{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ELvf93DUQzjJH6s6hmLBnZ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Diagram Rendering Pipeline\n     2→\n     3→> Updated: 2026-02-15 — Draw.io status clarified, acceptance criteria updated\n     4→\n     5→## Overview\n     6→\n     7→Client-side rendering of native diagram files using type-specific libraries in the web dashboard.\n     8→\n     9→## Parent JTBD\n    10→\n    11→As a developer, I want to see my architecture diagrams rendered visually in the web dashboard without custom SVG code.\n    12→\n    13→## Scope\n    14→\n    15→**In Scope:**\n    16→- Mermaid.js client-side rendering for .mmd files\n    17→- Draw.io embedded viewer for .drawio files\n    18→- Type-to-renderer dispatch based on _arch.json manifest\n    19→- Diagram page/view in the web dashboard\n    20→- Loading states and error handling per diagram\n    21→\n    22→**Out of Scope:**\n    23→- AI chat panel (see chat-review spec)\n    24→- Standalone HTML preview generation (being removed)\n    25→- Template.html custom SVG rendering (being removed)\n    26→\n    27→## Requirements\n    28→\n    29→### Functional\n    30→\n    31→1. Web app reads _arch.json manifest via API, then fetches each diagram file by type\n    32→2. Mermaid diagrams: Fetch .mmd file content as text, render client-side via mermaid.js `mermaid.render()`\n    33→3. Draw.io diagrams: Embed .drawio file via Draw.io viewer iframe or embedded library\n    34→4. Each diagram rendered in its own card with title and description from manifest\n    35→5. Diagrams laid out vertically, one per card, full-width\n    36→6. Mermaid render errors show the error message inline with the raw source visible\n    37→7. Clickable diagrams (for chat context injection - handled by chat-review spec)\n    38→\n    39→### Non-Functional\n    40→\n    41→- **Performance:** Mermaid renders < 1s per diagram. Draw.io iframe loads within 3s.\n    42→- **Platform:** Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari)\n    43→\n    44→## User Workflows\n    45→\n    46→### Workflow 1: View Feature Diagrams\n    47→\n    48→**Actor:** Developer\n    49→**Trigger:** Navigate to feature architecture page\n    50→\n    51→**Steps:**\n    52→1. User opens `/project/{id}/arch/{feature_name}` in browser\n    53→2. Server returns page with manifest data\n    54→3. Client JavaScript reads manifest, fetches each diagram file via API\n    55→4. For each mermaid entry: fetch .mmd content, call `mermaid.render()`, insert SVG into card\n    56→5. For each drawio entry: create iframe pointing to Draw.io viewer URL with file data\n    57→6. All diagrams visible with titles and descriptions\n    58→\n    59→**Error Cases:**\n    60→- Mermaid parse error: Show error message + raw source in card\n    61→- Draw.io file missing: Show \"File not found\" placeholder in card\n    62→- Network error fetching diagram: Show retry button\n    63→\n    64→## Data Model\n    65→\n    66→**Entities:**\n    67→- DiagramCard: `{ name, description, type, diagramType, content (fetched), renderState (loading|rendered|error) }`\n    68→\n    69→**Relationships:**\n    70→- DiagramCard maps 1:1 to DiagramEntry in manifest\n    71→\n    72→## Integration Points\n    73→\n    74→**Dependencies:**\n    75→- Arch directory spec: Provides _arch.json manifest and file structure\n    76→- Server API: New endpoints to serve manifest and diagram file contents\n    77→\n    78→**Provides to:**\n    79→- Chat review spec: Rendered diagrams are clickable to inject into chat context\n    80→\n    81→## Technical Considerations\n    82→\n    83→### Architecture\n    84→\n    85→Server-side:\n    86→- `GET /api/projects/{id}/features/{name}/arch` - Returns _arch.json manifest\n    87→- `GET /api/projects/{id}/features/{name}/arch/{filename}` - Returns raw file content (text/plain for .mmd, application/xml for .drawio)\n    88→\n    89→Client-side:\n    90→- Renderer map: `{ mermaid: renderMermaid, drawio: renderDrawio }`\n    91→- Each renderer takes a container element and file content, produces the visual\n    92→\n    93→### Renderer Map\n    94→\n    95→| type     | Renderer          | Library                   |\n    96→|----------|-------------------|---------------------------|\n    97→| mermaid  | `renderMermaid()` | mermaid.js (CDN)          |\n    98→| drawio   | `renderDrawio()`  | Draw.io embed viewer      |\n    99→\n   100→### Libraries/APIs\n   101→\n   102→- **mermaid.js** - CDN: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid/dist/mermaid.min.js` - Client-side Mermaid rendering\n   103→- **Draw.io viewer** - Embedded via iframe with `https://viewer.diagrams.net/?...` or self-hosted viewer\n   104→\n   105→### Patterns\n   106→\n   107→- Progressive rendering: Show loading skeleton per card, replace with rendered diagram as each completes\n   108→- Error boundary per card: One diagram failing doesn't block others\n   109→\n   110→## Acceptance Criteria\n   111→\n   112→- [x] Mermaid .mmd files render as interactive SVG in browser\n   113→- [ ] Draw.io .drawio files render in embedded viewer — needs verification; no Draw.io viewer code found in architecture.html\n   114→- [x] Each diagram shows title and description from manifest\n   115→- [x] Mermaid parse errors display inline with source\n   116→- [x] Missing files show clear placeholder\n   117→- [x] No custom SVG layout code - all rendering delegated to libraries\n   118→- [ ] Page loads and renders 5 diagrams in < 3s total — not verified (performance requirement)\n   119→\n   120→## Implementation Notes\n   121→\n   122→- Mermaid.js is loaded from CDN (`https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.min.js`).\n   123→- Diagram cards support pan/zoom interaction via viewport transforms.\n   124→- Diagrams can be expanded to a full-page view at `/project/{id}/arch/{feature_name}/diagram/{filename}`.\n   125→- Live diagram updates are supported via the `DiagramWatcher` service using the `watchdog` library for filesystem events with 100ms debounce.\n   126→\n   127→## Resolved Questions\n   128→\n   129→- Mermaid.js is loaded from CDN (not bundled).\n   130→- Draw.io rendering approach is still unclear in the implementation.\n   131→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e23a7aa2-5923-4855-9cc2-f80458cf6b25","uuid":"a1f6deab-ac24-4685-af7f-e76da6579945","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/.vista/features/diagram_representations/specs/rendering-pipeline.md","content":"# Spec: Diagram Rendering Pipeline\n\n> Updated: 2026-02-15 — Draw.io status clarified, acceptance criteria updated\n\n## Overview\n\nClient-side rendering of native diagram files using type-specific libraries in the web dashboard.\n\n## Parent JTBD\n\nAs a developer, I want to see my architecture diagrams rendered visually in the web dashboard without custom SVG code.\n\n## Scope\n\n**In Scope:**\n- Mermaid.js client-side rendering for .mmd files\n- Draw.io embedded viewer for .drawio files\n- Type-to-renderer dispatch based on _arch.json manifest\n- Diagram page/view in the web dashboard\n- Loading states and error handling per diagram\n\n**Out of Scope:**\n- AI chat panel (see chat-review spec)\n- Standalone HTML preview generation (being removed)\n- Template.html custom SVG rendering (being removed)\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n\n1. Web app reads _arch.json manifest via API, then fetches each diagram file by type\n2. Mermaid diagrams: Fetch .mmd file content as text, render client-side via mermaid.js `mermaid.render()`\n3. Draw.io diagrams: Embed .drawio file via Draw.io viewer iframe or embedded library\n4. Each diagram rendered in its own card with title and description from manifest\n5. Diagrams laid out vertically, one per card, full-width\n6. Mermaid render errors show the error message inline with the raw source visible\n7. Clickable diagrams (for chat context injection - handled by chat-review spec)\n\n### Non-Functional\n\n- **Performance:** Mermaid renders < 1s per diagram. Draw.io iframe loads within 3s.\n- **Platform:** Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari)\n\n## User Workflows\n\n### Workflow 1: View Feature Diagrams\n\n**Actor:** Developer\n**Trigger:** Navigate to feature architecture page\n\n**Steps:**\n1. User opens `/project/{id}/arch/{feature_name}` in browser\n2. Server returns page with manifest data\n3. Client JavaScript reads manifest, fetches each diagram file via API\n4. For each mermaid entry: fetch .mmd content, call `mermaid.render()`, insert SVG into card\n5. For each drawio entry: create iframe pointing to Draw.io viewer URL with file data\n6. All diagrams visible with titles and descriptions\n\n**Error Cases:**\n- Mermaid parse error: Show error message + raw source in card\n- Draw.io file missing: Show \"File not found\" placeholder in card\n- Network error fetching diagram: Show retry button\n\n## Data Model\n\n**Entities:**\n- DiagramCard: `{ name, description, type, diagramType, content (fetched), renderState (loading|rendered|error) }`\n\n**Relationships:**\n- DiagramCard maps 1:1 to DiagramEntry in manifest\n\n## Integration Points\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Arch directory spec: Provides _arch.json manifest and file structure\n- Server API: New endpoints to serve manifest and diagram file contents\n\n**Provides to:**\n- Chat review spec: Rendered diagrams are clickable to inject into chat context\n\n## Technical Considerations\n\n### Architecture\n\nServer-side:\n- `GET /api/projects/{id}/features/{name}/arch` - Returns _arch.json manifest\n- `GET /api/projects/{id}/features/{name}/arch/{filename}` - Returns raw file content (text/plain for .mmd, application/xml for .drawio)\n\nClient-side:\n- Renderer map: `{ mermaid: renderMermaid, drawio: renderDrawio }`\n- Each renderer takes a container element and file content, produces the visual\n\n### Renderer Map\n\n| type     | Renderer          | Library                   |\n|----------|-------------------|---------------------------|\n| mermaid  | `renderMermaid()` | mermaid.js (CDN)          |\n| drawio   | `renderDrawio()`  | Draw.io embed viewer      |\n\n### Libraries/APIs\n\n- **mermaid.js** - CDN: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid/dist/mermaid.min.js` - Client-side Mermaid rendering\n- **Draw.io viewer** - Embedded via iframe with `https://viewer.diagrams.net/?...` or self-hosted viewer\n\n### Patterns\n\n- Progressive rendering: Show loading skeleton per card, replace with rendered diagram as each completes\n- Error boundary per card: One diagram failing doesn't block others\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Mermaid .mmd files render as interactive SVG in browser\n- [ ] Draw.io .drawio files render in embedded viewer — needs verification; no Draw.io viewer code found in architecture.html\n- [x] Each diagram shows title and description from manifest\n- [x] Mermaid parse errors display inline with source\n- [x] Missing files show clear placeholder\n- [x] No custom SVG layout code - all rendering delegated to libraries\n- [ ] Page loads and renders 5 diagrams in < 3s total — not verified (performance requirement)\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- Mermaid.js is loaded from CDN (`https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.min.js`).\n- Diagram cards support pan/zoom interaction via viewport transforms.\n- Diagrams can be expanded to a full-page view at `/project/{id}/arch/{feature_name}/diagram/{filename}`.\n- Live diagram updates are supported via the `DiagramWatcher` service using the `watchdog` library for filesystem events with 100ms debounce.\n\n## Resolved Questions\n\n- Mermaid.js is loaded from CDN (not bundled).\n- Draw.io rendering approach is still unclear in the implementation.\n","numLines":131,"startLine":1,"totalLines":131}}}
