cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.min.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@15/marked.min.js\"></script>\n```\n\n**Rendering logic:**\n\n**`renderDiagramContent()` function (lines 1288-1311):**\n```javascript\nasync function renderDiagramContent(el, filename, content, idx) {\n    if (filename.endsWith('.mmd')) {\n        try {\n            const id = `mermaid-svg-${idx}-${++mermaidCounter}`;\n            const { svg } = await mermaid.render(id, content);\n            el.innerHTML = svg;\n            // ... node click handlers ...\n        } catch (e) {\n            el.innerHTML = `<pre class=\"text-yellow-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">Mermaid parse error:\\n${e.message || e}\\n\\n${content}</pre>`;\n        }\n    } else {\n        el.innerHTML = `<pre class=\"text-gray-400 text-xs whitespace-pre-wrap\">${escapeHtml(content)}</pre>`;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Rendering dispatch:**\n- Line 1289: Checks `filename.endsWith('.mmd')` for Mermaid\n- Lines 1290-1307: Uses `mermaid.render()` from CDN library to generate SVG\n- Lines 1294-1302: Adds click handlers to `.node` elements for selection\n- Line 1303: Calls `reapplySelections()` to restore selected state after re-render\n- Lines 1308-1310: Fallback for non-Mermaid files → renders as escaped HTML in `<pre>` tag\n\n**What does NOT exist:**\n- No `RENDERERS` object/map\n- No `renderPlantUML()` function\n- No `renderD2()` function\n- No `renderGraphviz()` function\n- No `renderDrawio()` function (Draw.io files are served as raw XML, not rendered in browser)\n- No `renderMarkdown()` function\n\n**Theme toggle (lines 1016-1023):**\n- Dark/light theme switcher exists (lines 871-898, 1016-1023)\n- Controlled via `setDiagramTheme()` (not shown in excerpt but referenced)\n\n---\n\n### 5. `vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n\n**`WATCH_EXTENSIONS` (lines 26, 124):**\n```python\nWATCH_EXTENSIONS = {\".mmd\", \".drawio\"}\n```\n\nDefined twice (class-level constant in both `_DiagramEventHandler` and `DiagramWatcher`).\n\n**`_detect_diagram_type()` function (lines 102-118):**\n\n**Purpose:** Parse first line of `.mmd` file to identify Mermaid diagram subtype.\n\n**Logic:**\n1. Line 105: Read file content, take first line, lowercase\n2. Lines 107-115: Check if first line contains any of these keywords (case-insensitive, spaces/hyphens removed):\n   - `\"graph\"`, `\"flowchart\"`, `\"sequencediagram\"`, `\"sequence\"`\n   - `\"classdiagram\"`, `\"class\"`, `\"statediagram\"`, `\"state\"`\n   - `\"erdiagram\"`, `\"er\"`, `\"gantt\"`, `\"pie\"`, `\"gitgraph\"`\n   - `\"c4context\"`, `\"c4container\"`, `\"c4component\"`, `\"c4deployment\"`\n   - `\"mindmap\"`, `\"timeline\"`\n3. Line 116: Default return: `\"flowchart\"`\n4. Line 117-118: Exception handling returns `\"flowchart\"`\n\n**Auto-manifest update (lines 232-256):**\n- `_update_manifest_sync()` scans arch directory\n- Line 239: Checks for files with extensions in `WATCH_EXTENSIONS`\n- Lines 240-247: Builds manifest entries with `name`, `file`, `type`, `diagramType`\n- Lines 248-255: Writes to `_arch.json` with feature name from parent directory\n\n---\n\n### 6. Settings Service\n\n**File `vista/server/services/settings_service.py`:** **DOES NOT EXIST**\n\n**`plantuml_server_url` setting:** **DOES NOT EXIST ANYWHERE IN CODEBASE**\n\nNo references found via grep in the entire `vista/server` directory.\n\n---\n\n### 7. `vista/tests/test_architecture.py`\n\n**Test classes and functions:**\n\n#### `TestArchitectureAPI` (lines 94-227):\n- `test_get_arch_manifest_success` (97-110)\n- `test_get_arch_manifest_not_found` (112-123)\n- `test_get_arch_manifest_malformed_json` (125-137)\n- `test_get_arch_file_mmd_success` (139-152)\n- `test_get_arch_file_drawio_content_type` (154-166)\n- `test_get_arch_file_path_traversal_dotdot` (168-178)\n- `test_get_arch_file_path_traversal_absolute` (180-190)\n- `test_get_arch_file_not_found` (192-202)\n- `test_architecture_page_renders` (204-213)\n- `test_architecture_page_no_manifest` (215-226)\n\n#### `TestProgressServiceArch` (lines 229-318):\n- `test_read_arch_manifest_valid` (232-243)\n- `test_read_arch_manifest_missing_file` (245-250)\n- `test_read_arch_manifest_invalid_json` (252-261)\n- `test_read_arch_file_valid_mmd` (263-272)\n- `test_read_arch_file_valid_drawio` (274-283)\n- `test_read_arch_file_path_traversal_dotdot` (285-297)\n- `test_read_arch_file_path_traversal_absolute` (299-307)\n- `test_read_arch_file_not_found` (309-317)\n\n#### `TestSchemaValidation` (lines 320-456):\n- `test_plan_schema_valid_minimal` (328-347)\n- `test_plan_schema_valid_with_architecture` (349-371)\n- `test_plan_schema_rejects_missing_phases` (373-392)\n- `test_arch_schema_valid_manifest` (394-414)\n- `test_arch_schema_rejects_invalid_type` (416-436)\n- `test_arch_schema_rejects_missing_fields` (438-455)\n\n#### `TestProjectServiceArch` (lines 458-525):\n- `test_scan_features_detailed_has_arch_manifest` (461-494)\n- `test_scan_features_detailed_arch_diagram_count` (496-512)\n- `test_scan_features_detailed_no_arch` (514-524)\n\n#### `TestContextAssembler` (lines 527-570):\n- `test_build_prompt_includes_context` (530-540)\n- `test_build_prompt_ignores_history` (542-559)\n- `test_build_prompt_works_with_empty_context_and_history` (561-569)\n\n**Total:** 4 test classes, 29 test functions\n\n---\n\n### 8. `vista/tests/test_diagram_watcher.py`\n\n**Test classes and functions:**\n\n#### `TestDetectDiagramType` (lines 16-54):\n- `test_flowchart` (17-20)\n- `test_sequence_diagram` (22-25)\n- `test_class_diagram` (27-30)\n- `test_state_diagram` (32-35)\n- `test_gantt` (37-40)\n- `test_unknown_defaults_to_flowchart` (42-45)\n- `test_empty_file` (47-50)\n- `test_missing_file` (52-54)\n\n#### `TestReadFile` (lines 57-64):\n- `test_reads_utf8` (58-61)\n- `test_missing_file_returns_empty` (63-64)\n\n#### `TestDiagramWatcher` (lines 67-146):\n- `test_key_generation` (68-69)\n- `test_subscribe_creates_queue` (71-79)\n- `test_subscribe_starts_observer` (81-92)\n- `test_subscribe_no_dir` (94-101)\n- `test_multiple_subscribers` (103-113)\n- `test_unsubscribe_removes_queue` (115-127)\n- `test_unsubscribe_last_stops_observer` (129-139)\n- `test_unsubscribe_unknown_key` (141-145)\n\n#### `TestManifestUpdate` (lines 148-193):\n- `test_updates_arch_json` (149-166)\n- `test_no_dir_does_nothing` (168-171)\n- `test_empty_dir` (173-180)\n- `test_drawio_type` (182-192)\n\n#### `TestBroadcast` (lines 195-229):\n- `test_broadcast_delivers_to_subscribers` (197-209)\n- `test_broadcast_drops_full_queues` (211-224)\n- `test_broadcast_unknown_key` (226-229)\n\n#### `TestStopAll` (lines 232-246):\n- `test_stop_clears_state` (234-246)\n\n**Total:** 6 test classes, 24 test functions\n\n---\n\n## Summary: Current vs. Plan Gaps\n\n### Missing Format Support:\n- **Current:** Only `mermaid` and `drawio` in schema (line 29 of arch-schema.json)\n- **Plan needs:** `plantuml`, `d2`, `graphviz`, `markdown`\n\n### Missing Rendering Logic:\n- **Current:** Only `renderDiagramContent()` with Mermaid + fallback (architecture.html:1288-1311)\n- **Plan needs:** Individual renderer functions for each format\n\n### Missing Write Capabilities:\n- **Current:** No PUT/POST endpoints, no `write_arch_file()` method\n- **Plan needs:** Markdown editing endpoints and write methods\n\n### Missing Settings:\n- **Current:** No settings service, no `plantuml_server_url` configuration\n- **Plan needs:** Settings service with PlantUML server URL config\n\n### File Paths:\n- **Absolute paths:**\n  - `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/templates/arch-schema.json`\n  - `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n  - `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/server/routes/architecture.py`\n  - `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista-expanded-visualization/vista/ser